window.DOCS_INDEX=[{"s":"index","t":"Documentation","y":"Ac","h":[["three-steps-to-start","Three steps to start","Install — one curl command or build from source. See Quickstart . Log in or configure a model — AtomGit OAuth is the easiest path; any OpenAI-compatible API key also works. See Login Methods and Configuration . Ask away — run atomcode inside any project directory and describe your task in natural language. Tip For a quick taste, run a single command: atomcode -p \"give me a brief overview of this repo\" — one-shot execution with the result piped to stdout."],["documentation-map","Documentation map",""],["quickstart","Quickstart","Install paths, the 3-step first-run wizard, your first task, and the atomcode uninstall flow."],["configuration","Configuration","Every ~/.atomcode/config.toml field, per-provider examples, plus the vision preprocessor (so non-vision models can still answer about images)."],["login-methods","Login Methods","AtomGit OAuth one-click login (auto-persisted) versus API key setup, side by side."],["basic-usage","Basic Usage","How to phrase tasks, common CLI flags, file references, multiline input, and image attachments / screenshots (Ctrl+V / drag-and-drop)."],["slash-commands","Slash Commands","Reference table for the 30+ built-in slash commands: sessions, models, undo, issues, conversation modes, and the extension ecosystem."],["keybindings","Keybindings","Every TUI keybinding: input, navigation, selection, copy, and more."],["built-in-tools","Built-in Tools","A guide to filesystem, shell, code graph, web, and skill tools."],["sessions-undo","Sessions & Undo","Persistent session restore, /undo rollback, and clearing or compacting context."],["project-instructions","Project Instructions","Use .atomcode.md to give AtomCode project-level conventions to follow."],["skills","Skills","Write your own skills to extend the slash-command ecosystem."],["plugin-system","Plugin System","One-click install other people's skill / command / hook packs from any git repo — Claude Code ecosystem compatible."],["mcp-integration","MCP Integration","Plug external MCP servers in via .mcp.json — expose GitHub, databases, Playwright, and more to your model."],["changelog","Changelog","Browse new features, fixes, and related issues by release."],["faq","FAQ","Install issues, model connectivity, permission prompts, context overflows, and other common questions."],["feedback-contributing","Feedback & contributing","AtomCode is open source — issues and pull requests welcome: Repository: https://atomgit.com/atomgit_atomcode/atomcode Issues: after /login , ask AtomCode to create one with its built-in AtomGit tool, or open the repository's Issues page License: MIT"]],"x":"AtomCode · 开源终端 AI 编码助手 AtomCode Documentation An AI coding agent that lives in your terminal. Hand it a natural-language task and it will autonomously read, edit, run, and self-verify. These docs walk you from a fresh install to every feature AtomCode offers. v5.2.8 许可证 MIT 语言 Rust 1.88+ 平台 macOS · Linux · HarmonyOS PC · Windows 100% AI 生成"},{"s":"getting-started","t":"Quickstart","y":"Qs","h":[["requirements","Requirements","OS : macOS (Apple Silicon or Intel), Linux, Windows, or HarmonyOS PC Rust toolchain : 1.88+ (only required when building from source) LLM : an API key for any supported provider, or an AtomGit account (for OAuth login)"],["install","Install",""],["option-1-one-click-install-recommended","Option 1: one-click install (recommended)","On macOS, Linux, or HarmonyOS PC: curl -fsSL https://raw.atomgit.com/atomgit_atomcode/atomcode/raw/main/scripts/install.sh | sh The script downloads the prebuilt binary for your platform and places it at ~/.local/bin/atomcode . Make sure that directory is on your PATH . On Windows PowerShell: irm https://raw.atomgit.com/atomgit_atomcode/atomcode/raw/main/scripts/install.ps1 | iex It downloads the Windows x64 prebuilt binary and updates PATH ; open a fresh terminal to use the atomcode command."],["option-2-install-using-npm","Option 2: install using npm","If you already have Node.js 18+ installed, install globally with npm: npm install -g @atomgit.com/atomcode The package uses optionalDependencies to pull the prebuilt binary for your platform (macOS x64 / arm64, Linux x64 / arm64, Windows x64, HarmonyOS arm64) — one command, cross-platform."],["option-3-install-using-homebrew","Option 3: install using Homebrew","If you have Homebrew installed, install the cask (macOS x64 / arm64, Linux x64 / arm64): brew install --cask atomcode The cask downloads the prebuilt binary for your platform and links it to your PATH automatically."],["option-4-build-from-source","Option 4: build from source","git clone https://atomgit.com/atomgit_atomcode/atomcode.git cd atomcode # To use WebUI, build its frontend first (Node.js 22.6+) npm ci --prefix webui npm run build --prefix webui cargo build --release -p atomcode Run ./target/release/atomcode after building (the binary is atomcode.exe on Windows), or install it somewhere on your PATH . For terminal-only use, skip the npm commands. After updating the frontend, run cargo clean -p atomcode-daemon and rebuild if Cargo has not recompiled the daemon to embed the new assets. The free official CodingPlan quota requires an official build. With a self-built binary, use /provider to configure your own model and API key."],["verify-the-install","Verify the install","atomcode --version You should see something like atomcode 5.0.x (build-id) ."],["shell-completion-optional","Shell completion (optional)","AtomCode can generate command and option completions for common shells: atomcode completion zsh atomcode completion bash atomcode completion fish atomcode completion powershell Load the generated script using your shell's normal setup. This affects CLI completion only; inside the TUI, Tab completes input and Shift+Tab cycles execution mode."],["first-run","First run","Just run: atomcode The first launch shows a 3-step onboarding wizard (you can re-open it any time with /welcome ):"],["step-13-welcome","Step 1/3 · Welcome","███ █████ ███ █ █ ████ ███ ████ █████ █ █ █ █ █ ██ ██ █ █ █ █ █ █ █████ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ ████ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ █ ███ █ █ ████ ███ ████ █████ AtomCode Version 5.2.8 · AI coding agent in your terminal • Multi-step agent loop · built-in code-graph tools • Compatible with any OpenAI-style API • Free tokens via CodingPlan Press Enter to continue. Ctrl+C exits at any point."],["step-23-language-choose-your-language-选择语言","Step 2/3 · Language (Choose your language / 选择语言)","1. Auto-detect (LC_ALL / LANG) 2. English 3. 简体中文 (Simplified Chinese) 1-3 select · Enter confirm · ← back · Esc skip Your choice takes effect immediately and is written to the locale field of ~/.atomcode/config.toml . Run /language later to change it."],["step-33-setup-how-would-you-like-to-start","Step 3/3 · Setup (how would you like to start?)","1. One-click with AtomGit CodingPlan (recommended · free tokens + auto-configured provider) 2. Configure a provider manually (you have an API key) 3. Skip and explore the TUI first (run /login or /provider later) 1-3 select · Enter confirm · ← back · Esc skip CodingPlan — the recommended path; equivalent to running /login inside the TUI. The browser opens AtomGit OAuth; after you log in, free tokens are claimed automatically and the granted model list is written as a provider config. Configure manually — equivalent to /provider : add a provider account, then add models under it. Skip — jump straight into the TUI and run /login or /provider later. For a deeper breakdown see Login Methods . You can re-open the wizard any time with /welcome ."],["your-first-task","Your first task","cd into a project you know, launch atomcode, and just describe what you want: cd ~/projects/my-web-app atomcode > give me a brief overview of this project's directory layout and tech stack AtomCode autonomously: Runs list_directory , read_file , and similar tools to explore the code; Identifies key descriptor files ( package.json / Cargo.toml / …); Returns a structured summary. Tip Not sure what to ask? Try: \" fix every typo in the README \", \" add TypeScript types to the functions in src/utils.ts \", \" run the tests and fix any failures \"."],["uninstall","Uninstall","When you're done with AtomCode, the built-in uninstall subcommand cleans up in one shot. It asks group-by-group whether to delete: the binary plus the PATH edits the installer made, credentials such as ~/.atomcode/auth.toml , and runtime state such as ~/.atomcode/sessions/ ."],["interactive-recommended","Interactive (recommended)","atomcode uninstall Each group prompts y/N with a sensible default (binary = yes, credentials = no, state = yes) — pressing Enter is a reasonable choice."],["non-interactive","Non-interactive","# Fully automatic: take the default decisions, no prompts atomcode uninstall --yes # Wipe everything (including the entire ~/.atomcode/ directory) atomcode uninstall --purge # Only remove the binary and PATH edits; keep ~/.atomcode/ intact atomcode uninstall --keep-data # Just print the plan; do nothing atomcode uninstall --dry-run Heads up --purge also deletes all session history, memories, custom provider configs, and OAuth tokens . It is irreversible. If you might use AtomCode again, prefer the interactive default or --keep-data ."],["next-steps","Next steps","Configuration — manage multiple providers and models. Basic Usage — CLI flags and best practices for phrasing tasks. Slash Commands — get fluent with /resume , /undo , /diff , and friends."]],"x":"Quickstart Install AtomCode, run the first-time wizard, and complete your first task in a few minutes."},{"s":"login","t":"Login Methods","y":"Lg","h":[["two-methods-at-a-glance","Two methods at a glance","Method Command Who it's for AtomGit CodingPlan /login Recommended — one command runs OAuth, claims free tokens, and auto-configures provider and model API key /provider or hand-edit config Users with their own OpenAI / Claude / DeepSeek key As of v4.25.0 /codingplan has been folded into /login ; the previous \"OAuth-only without claiming tokens\" entry has been removed."],["atomgit-codingplan-recommended","AtomGit CodingPlan (recommended)","AtomGit is the open-source code-hosting platform run by CSDN / OpenAtom Open Source Foundation, and AtomCode natively integrates its OAuth and CodingPlan. /login is the lowest-friction entry point for new users: a single action logs you in → claims free token quota → auto-generates a provider config from the granted model list. After that one command you can start chatting immediately. Re-running it after you're already signed in idempotently re-syncs the model list — no double-claim."],["codingplan-tier-system","CodingPlan tier system","CodingPlan currently offers three tiers. The system automatically grants the highest tier you're eligible for. Quota is measured on a rolling 5-hour window: Tier Duration How to get Models Lite 30 days Free claim, 1,000 slots/day deepseek-v4-flash, Qwen/Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct Pro Trial 7 days Free claim, 100 slots/day at 10:00 Adds GLM-5.2 Pro 30 days Free claim, requires a merged PR in the activity repository Adds GLM-5.2 After claiming Pro or above, run /login in AtomCode to sync the updated model list. For details, visit the CodingPlan page ."],["from-the-first-run-wizard","From the first-run wizard","The first time you run atomcode , the 3-step wizard pops up automatically. Step 1 (welcome): press Enter. Step 2 (language): press 1 / 2 / 3 to pick. Step 3 (setup): pick One-click with AtomGit CodingPlan (option 1). The browser opens the AtomGit authorization page — click Allow. After authorization, the TUI claims CodingPlan and writes the provider config. No need to touch config.toml — start sending messages. If you skipped earlier and want to redo the wizard, run /welcome any time."],["from-an-existing-session","From an existing session","Once inside the TUI, run: /login The browser opens to complete authorization, claim CodingPlan, and refresh the provider list. Running it again re-syncs the model list — the local AtomGit* providers are updated to the latest entitled models."],["from-the-command-line","From the command line","atomcode login Useful in scripts, remote servers, or container images for a one-shot setup. The CLI subcommand and the TUI /login share the same flow and emit the same report. Note: atomcode codingplan is kept as a hidden alias so existing scripts and muscle memory don't break after the fold."],["check-status-log-out","Check status / log out","atomcode status # or /status in the TUI — includes CodingPlan usage and expiry atomcode logout # or /logout in the TUI — clears the OAuth token"],["api-key-method","API key method","To use your own OpenAI / Claude / DeepSeek / GLM key, there are three ways:"],["option-a-provider-in-the-tui","Option A: /provider in the TUI","Type /provider in the TUI. Choose a vendor preset or a custom account, enter its API key, then add one or more models under that account. The configuration is written back to ~/.atomcode/config.toml ."],["option-b-hand-edit-the-config-file","Option B: hand-edit the config file","Edit ~/.atomcode/config.toml directly and add a [providers.*] entry; see ProviderConfig fields ."],["option-c-one-shot-cli-override","Option C: one-shot CLI override","Don't want to touch the config file and only need a different provider for one run? Add flags at launch: atomcode --provider deepseek --model deepseek-reasoner"],["which-one-should-i-pick","Which one should I pick?","First-time user → CodingPlan ( /login ) — free tokens, just use it. Already have your own API key → skip /login and use the API key path ( /provider or hand-edit config). If you later need the built-in AtomGit repository, PR, or Issue tools, run /login to authorize them; this also claims CodingPlan and registers AtomGit-* providers. Running in CI / scripts → API key via config file or env vars. Fully offline → configure an Ollama provider — no login required."],["next-steps","Next steps","Basic Usage — first thing after logging in: learn how to phrase tasks. Slash Commands — /provider , /model , /status in detail."]],"x":"Login Methods AtomCode supports two ways to connect to an LLM: AtomGit CodingPlan (with free tokens) and traditional API keys. This page helps you pick the right path and walks through the binding."},{"s":"configuration","t":"Configuration","y":"Cf","h":[["config-file-location","Config file location","Default path: macOS / Linux / HarmonyOS PC: ~/.atomcode/config.toml Windows: %USERPROFILE%\\.atomcode\\config.toml You can also use --config /path/to/config.toml to point at any file. On the first run, if the file is missing, the 3-step wizard walks you through initial setup."],["minimal-example","Minimal example","default_model = \"deepseek/chat\" [provider_accounts.deepseek] provider = \"openai-compatible\" base_url = \"https://api.deepseek.com/v1\" api_key = \"$DEEPSEEK_API_KEY\" [models.\"deepseek/chat\"] account = \"deepseek\" model = \"deepseek-chat\" context_window = 64000 Set DEEPSEEK_API_KEY in your environment before launching AtomCode. deepseek/chat is the AtomCode selection ID and deepseek-chat is the model name sent to the API. Provider management in v5.0.7 The recommended path is /provider : add a provider account, then add one or more models under it. Protocol, base URL, and API key are shared by the account; model name and context window are stored per model. Legacy [providers.*] entries remain supported and are projected automatically."],["top-level-fields","Top-level fields","Field Type Description default_model string? Default selection ID, matching a key under [models.*] . Takes precedence over default_provider . provider_accounts table Provider accounts hold the protocol or preset, base URL, and credentials. models table Model profiles reference an account via account and store the model name and settings such as the context window. default_provider string Legacy default selection, matching a key under [providers.*] . default_workdir string? Daemon default directory. Saved only when explicitly requested. The TUI neither reads nor writes it. providers table Map of provider name to ProviderConfig vision_preprocessor_provider string? When the main provider can't see images but the user attaches one, forward it to this provider for OCR / description; the result is spliced back into the prompt as text. See Vision preprocessor init_prompt_file string? UTF-8 file whose requirements are appended to the built-in /init prompt. Relative paths resolve from $ATOMCODE_HOME ; maximum size is 64 KiB. This can also be edited in /config ."],["provider-config","ProviderConfig fields","Fields available under each [providers.xxx] table: Field Type Required Description type string yes Provider protocol — currently openai , claude , or ollama api_key string? conditional API key. Supports literal keys, env var expansion (e.g. $MY_KEY or ${MY_KEY:-default} ), direct env var names (e.g. MY_KEY ), or omitted/blank fallback to standard env vars (e.g. OPENAI_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ). Optional for ollama . OAuth providers omit this — token read from ~/.atomcode/auth.toml automatically model string yes Model name, e.g. deepseek-chat , gpt-4o , claude-sonnet-4-6 base_url string yes API base URL, pointing at the actual endpoint. e.g. https://api.deepseek.com/v1 , http://localhost:11434 capable_model integer No Capability rank. Higher is more capable; omit to leave a model unranked. Set it in [models.\"<selection ID>\"] , or in the legacy [providers.<name>] table. Explicit team auto requires at least two eligible ranked models, including the parent model. context_window integer no Model context window (tokens), default 64000. Default 8000 for ollama max_tokens integer? no Max output tokens per response. Defaults to context_window / 4 when unset retry_max_attempts integer? no Total attempts in the provider OPEN retry loop; when set, it also caps kernel-owned HTTP 429 recovery (both include the first request). Unset preserves the existing defaults (3 adapter attempts and the kernel's rate-limit safety policy). Set to 1 to disable adapter-level and 429 retries. Must be at least 1. In the account/model schema, set this on the [models.\"...\"] profile because retry behavior is model-specific. system_prompt string? no Override the default system prompt. Rarely needed user_agent string? no Override the HTTP User-Agent — useful when the upstream blocks the default UA"],["environment-variables-dynamic-api-key-resolution","Environment Variables & Dynamic API Key Resolution","To avoid storing sensitive credentials in plain text and to share environment variables with other tools, AtomCode supports flexible environment variable syntax in config.toml : Environment Variable Expansion ( $VAR / ${VAR} ) : [providers.my_openai] type = \"openai\" model = \"gpt-4o\" api_key = \"$MY_OPENAI_KEY\" # or \"${MY_OPENAI_KEY}\" base_url = \"https://api.openai.com/v1\" Supports fallback expressions with default values (e.g., api_key = \"${MY_KEY:-sk-fallback}\" ). Direct Environment Variable Name : [providers.my_claude] type = \"claude\" model = \"claude-sonnet-4-6\" api_key = \"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\" # Automatically read from environment variable ANTHROPIC_API_KEY Automatic Standard Environment Variable Fallback : When api_key is omitted or blank, AtomCode automatically checks standard environment variables matching the provider type : openai / openai-compat : reads OPENAI_API_KEY claude / anthropic : reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ollama : reads OLLAMA_API_KEY Global fallback: reads ATOMCODE_API_KEY Note: The $VAR syntax in config.toml is parsed internally by AtomCode, providing consistent behavior across Windows, macOS, and Linux. Why default to 64K instead of 128K? Even when a model advertises 128K+, its effective attention window is usually much smaller. An oversized context triggers \"lost in the middle\" failures and disables AtomCode's compaction strategy. 64K is empirically the most robust default; bump it yourself if your model is solid at higher values."],["network-proxy","Network & proxy","By default AtomCode follows your system's proxy configuration, so it works out of the box behind a corporate proxy. Tune it under [network.proxy] : [network.proxy] mode = \"follow_system\" # default — honor env vars + OS system proxy # mode = \"default_proxy\" # use the explicit http/https/all below # mode = \"no_proxy\" # force a direct connection # http = \"http://127.0.0.1:7890\" # https = \"http://127.0.0.1:7890\" # all = \"socks5://127.0.0.1:1080\" # no_proxy = \"localhost,127.0.0.1,.internal\" mode Behaviour follow_system (default) Honor HTTP_PROXY / HTTPS_PROXY / ALL_PROXY / NO_PROXY ; where those are unset, fall back to the OS system proxy (Windows registry / macOS scutil --proxy ). default_proxy Use the explicit http / https / all / no_proxy values from this section. no_proxy Force a direct connection, ignoring env vars and the system proxy. IPv6 proxy hosts are bracketed automatically ( ::1 → http://[::1]:8080 ). If a login attempt fails to connect or times out, the error message points at your proxy / network settings so you can tell a proxy problem apart from bad credentials."],["common-provider-examples","Common provider examples",""],["claude-anthropic","Claude (Anthropic)","[providers.claude] type = \"claude\" api_key = \"sk-ant-...\" model = \"claude-sonnet-4-6\" context_window = 128000"],["openai","OpenAI","[providers.openai] type = \"openai\" api_key = \"sk-...\" model = \"gpt-4o\" context_window = 128000"],["deepseek","DeepSeek","[providers.deepseek] type = \"openai\" api_key = \"sk-...\" model = \"deepseek-chat\" base_url = \"https://api.deepseek.com/v1\" context_window = 64000"],["zhipu-glm","Zhipu GLM","[providers.glm] type = \"openai\" api_key = \"...\" model = \"glm-4-plus\" base_url = \"https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4\" context_window = 128000"],["tongyi-qianwen-qwen","Tongyi Qianwen (Qwen)","[providers.qwen] type = \"openai\" api_key = \"sk-...\" model = \"qwen-plus\" base_url = \"https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1\" context_window = 128000"],["siliconflow","SiliconFlow","[providers.siliconflow] type = \"openai\" api_key = \"sk-...\" model = \"Qwen/Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct\" base_url = \"https://api.siliconflow.cn/v1\""],["ollama-local","Ollama (local)","[providers.ollama] type = \"ollama\" model = \"llama3.2\" base_url = \"http://localhost:11434\" context_window = 8000 Heads up Function-calling support varies a lot across Ollama models; weaker local models may not invoke tools reliably. Prefer the Instruct variants of Qwen2.5 / Llama3.2."],["multiple-providers-and-quick-switching","Multiple providers and quick switching","Config files can host any number of providers in parallel: default_provider = \"claude\" [providers.claude] type = \"claude\" api_key = \"sk-ant-...\" model = \"claude-sonnet-4-6\" [providers.deepseek] type = \"openai\" api_key = \"sk-...\" model = \"deepseek-chat\" base_url = \"https://api.deepseek.com/v1\" [providers.local] type = \"ollama\" model = \"qwen2.5:14b\" base_url = \"http://localhost:11434\" In the TUI, use /provider to manage provider accounts and their models. Built-in presets fill in the protocol and base URL for vendors such as AtomGit and TaoToken; choose Custom for another endpoint. Use /model to switch the current session and save the selected model as the default for sessions opened later; other already-open sessions are unchanged. The CLI also accepts one-shot overrides: atomcode --provider deepseek --model deepseek-reasoner"],["turn-round-limit","Turn round limit","[coding] max_rounds = 200 The default 0 means unlimited, with no additional fixed 300-round cap. A positive value limits work rounds. If work remains at the cap, at most one additional text-only model request summarizes progress, remaining work and next steps; it is billed and counted as a round. Interactive checkpoints, when enabled, can extend the budget first. Cancellation, timeout or provider errors can interrupt closing. Repetition guards remain independent."],["todo-eagerness","Todo eagerness","[tools.todo] enabled = true eager = \"auto\" eager accepts auto , preferred , or always . Auto adds a stronger first-round reminder for DeepSeek V4 Flash while preserving the normal behavior for other models. Preferred applies that reminder to every model. Always requests todowrite as the first tool of a new task when no active list exists; OpenAI-compatible and Anthropic providers enforce the named choice, while adapters without named-tool selection still receive the imperative reminder. Set enabled = false to remove the tool, prompt guidance, and todo hooks together; restart the current runtime after changing this master switch. ATOMCODE_TODO remains an environment override."],["vision-preprocessor","Vision preprocessor","When the active provider's model can't read images (text-only models like DeepSeek-V3 / Kimi) and the user attaches an image , AtomCode doesn't refuse — it forwards the image to a separate \"vision preprocessor\" provider for OCR + description, then splices the resulting text into the user message before sending to the main model. To enable: name an image-capable provider key as vision_preprocessor_provider in the config: default_provider = \"deepseek\" vision_preprocessor_provider = \"qwen-vl\" [providers.deepseek] type = \"openai\" api_key = \"sk-...\" model = \"deepseek-chat\" base_url = \"https://api.deepseek.com/v1\" [providers.qwen-vl] type = \"openai\" api_key = \"sk-...\" model = \"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-32B-Instruct\" base_url = \"https://api.siliconflow.cn/v1\" qwen-vl must be an existing key under [providers.*] , and its model must support vision input (common ones: Qwen3-VL-* / GLM-4V-* / claude-3+ / gpt-4o / gemini-* ). When the active provider can already see images, the preprocessor is skipped — the raw image bytes are sent directly. The /login flow auto-picks a VL/OCR model from the granted model list and writes this field for you (you can override afterwards). VL calls use an idle timeout : no total cap as long as the stream keeps producing chunks; the request times out after 30 seconds with no activity. On failure the main model still receives a \"vision recognition failed\" notice rather than a silent drop. For usage-level details see Basic Usage · Image attachments / screenshots ."],["three-ways-to-edit-the-config","Three ways to edit the config","Hand-edit — open ~/.atomcode/config.toml in your favourite editor. /config in the TUI — search and edit safe settings in place. The dynamic Retry attempts (current model) row writes retry_max_attempts to the active model; press Delete twice to restore the default. /provider in the TUI — interactively manage provider accounts and their models; changes are written back to disk."],["ui-keybindings","TUI shortcuts","Set newline = [\"alt+j\", \"ctrl+j\"] under [ui.keybindings] to customize newline chords. You can also search for “newline” in /config and record a chord or type its name. Changes apply immediately. See Custom newline shortcuts ."],["next-steps","Next steps","Login Methods — skip manual key management with AtomGit OAuth. Basic Usage — see how CLI flags can override config for one run."]],"x":"Configuration AtomCode's config is TOML, supports any number of providers side by side, and lets you switch on the fly. This page explains every field and shows examples for common providers."},{"s":"basic-usage","t":"Basic Usage","y":"Bu","h":[["launching","Launching","# Launch the TUI in the current directory atomcode # Specify a working directory atomcode -C /path/to/project # Override provider / model for this run only atomcode --provider claude --model claude-sonnet-4-6 # Continue the previous session atomcode -c atomcode --continue # Use a specific config file atomcode --config ./custom.toml # Skip all permission prompts, auto-approve every tool call atomcode -y atomcode --dangerously-skip-permissions"],["cli-flag-reference","CLI flag reference","Flag Short Purpose --dir PATH -C Working directory; defaults to the current directory --continue -c Continue the previous session instead of starting a new one --provider NAME — Override the default provider --model NAME — Override the current provider's model --config PATH — Use the given config file --prompt TEXT -p Non-interactive mode: one-shot execution, reply to stdout --prompt-file PATH — Read prompt from file (useful for long input; mutually exclusive with -p ) --verbose -v In non-interactive mode, print tool calls and token usage to stderr --no-tools — Headless only. Exposes no built-in, MCP, skill, or child-agent tools to the model. --dangerously-skip-permissions -y Skip all permission prompts — auto-approve every tool call (bash, file edits, MCP, etc.). A ⚠ BYPASS badge is shown in the TUI status bar while active Tip In the interactive TUI, use /toolbox to inspect available tools and /toolbox off <name-or-pattern> to turn matching tools off. See Built-in Tools . Warning -y / --dangerously-skip-permissions bypasses all permission prompts, including bash execution, file writes, and MCP tool calls. The agent can execute arbitrary actions without confirmation. Only use this flag when: Running in CI/CD pipelines or other automated environments Executing benchmarks inside a sandbox or container Working on non-critical projects where you trust the agent's built-in safety constraints"],["how-to-phrase-tasks","How to phrase tasks","AtomCode's agent loop is only as good as the task description you provide. A few rules of thumb: State goals, not steps — \"Fix the 404 after login\", not \"Open src/auth/callback.ts, delete line 27, then…\". The model has plenty of exploration ability. Name your constraints — say them out loud: \"preserve API compatibility\", \"don't touch test files\", \"use TypeScript not JS\". Provide a verification method — \"after the fix, run npm test to confirm\" lets the model close the self-verification loop. Discuss before editing — when direction is unclear, first ask it to \"analyse this module and propose a refactor plan\"; once aligned, let it implement."],["example-tasks","Example tasks","# Bug fix > Fix the bug where users are redirected to 404 after OAuth callback; restore the original path after callback. # New feature > Add a dark mode toggle to the settings page using Tailwind's dark: prefix, persisted in localStorage. # Refactor > Refactor src/db/*.ts to use a connection pool while keeping the public API unchanged; run npm test after. # Tests > Write unit tests for src/payment/processor.ts, covering all exception branches. # Code understanding > Briefly explain this repo's directory layout, build entry point, and the responsibilities of the core modules."],["multiline-input","Multiline input","In the TUI: Enter sends the message. \\ then Enter inserts a newline — works in every terminal (a trailing backslash makes the line a continuation). Shift+Enter / Ctrl+Enter insert a newline (requires Kitty keyboard protocol: kitty / WezTerm / Alacritty / iTerm2 ≥3.5 / Windows Terminal ≥1.21; not available on Windows). Generic web terminals use legacy key reporting by default. Set ATOMCODE_KITTY=1 to force Kitty keyboard enhancement on, or ATOMCODE_KITTY=0 to force it off. Alt+Enter inserts a newline (works in most terminals, but Windows Terminal binds it to \"toggle fullscreen\" by default — unbind in settings). The input area grows with content."],["at-mention","@ file references","Type @ in the input (preceded by whitespace or line start) to pop up a menu of files and directories in the project. This is the fastest way to point the model at a specific path — you handle locating, the model decides via read_file what to expand and how much to read."],["interaction","Interaction","Trigger — @ only triggers when preceded by whitespace or line start. A mid-string @ like email@host.com won't pop the menu — avoiding accidental triggers. Filtering — type to substring-match (case-insensitive). @cra hits crates/ ; @toml hits every *.toml . Drill in — type / to enter a directory; the menu scopes to that directory. @crates/ → @crates/atomcode-cli/ → … Navigation — ↑ / ↓ move; Enter or Tab select; Esc closes without inserting. Insertion form — on select, the @xxx in the input is replaced with the @full/relative/path (directories get a trailing / ) plus a trailing space; the cursor sits after the space, ready for more typing. Backspace to keep picking — delete the trailing space and the menu re-opens in place, handy for drilling further from the current directory."],["where-candidates-come-from","Where candidates come from","All files and directories under the project root — both files and dirs can be selected; dirs are marked with a trailing / . Honours .gitignore (and global ignore, .git/info/exclude ); ignored paths never appear. .git/ internals are excluded — almost nobody wants to @ -reference git metadata. Dotfiles stay — .env , .atomcode.md , and other dot-prefixed files are matchable (provided gitignore doesn't suppress them). Cross-level fuzzy matching — once you start typing a filter, matches reach across directory levels (not just the current scope's direct children). With an empty filter only the current scope's direct children are shown. Ordering : direct children of the current scope first → directories before files → alphabetical."],["what-it-means-for-the-model","What it means for the model","On submit, @crates/atomcode-cli/src/main.rs is sent to the model as literal text — AtomCode does not read and inline the file content in the frontend. The model sees the path and decides to call the built-in read_file tool as needed. Benefits: Large files don't get blindly stuffed into context — the token budget stays predictable. When you reference a directory, the model can list first and then read selectively. Re-referencing the same path doesn't inline the content twice. Tip If you want to force a file's contents into the conversation directly (e.g. a tight code review where you don't want another read_file round trip), use paste — drop the content into the input. Bracketed paste collapses it to an [paste #N] placeholder and ships the full payload on submit."],["limits","Limits","The candidate menu shows at most 30 entries ; typing more filter characters narrows the results. Paths with spaces don't appear in candidates — the @ reference uses whitespace as a terminator. The file index is built once per session ; files created during the session don't appear until you switch sessions or restart. Symlinks are not followed. No size or type filtering — every non-ignored file shows up."],["pasting-long-text","Pasting long text","AtomCode supports bracketed paste. When you paste a chunky block (e.g. a wall of logs), the TUI collapses it to a compact [paste #N · 132 lines] indicator so the input doesn't blow up. The full payload is sent on submit."],["image-attach","Image attachments / screenshots","Beyond text, you can also drop images into the conversation — error screenshots, UI mocks, whiteboard photos. AtomCode offers three entry points: Ctrl+V — when the system clipboard holds an image (you just Cmd+Shift+4 -captured something, copied an image from a browser, etc.), Ctrl+V attaches it directly. This is the fallback for macOS + iTerm2 where Cmd+V doesn't forward the image to the PTY, and works in any terminal. Cmd+V (macOS / iTerm2, with one-time setup) — iTerm2 → Settings → Profiles → Keys → Key Mappings, map ⌘V to Send Hex Codes: 0x16 ; from then on Cmd+V == Ctrl+V. Finder drag / iTerm2 path drop — drag an image onto the terminal window; iTerm2 / WezTerm and friends paste the file path as plaintext. AtomCode recognises an absolute path + .png / .jpg / .jpeg / .gif / .webp extension + existing file + size ≤ 20MB, and attaches it automatically. The raw path string is removed from the input. On a successful attach, an [Image #N] marker is inserted in the input; the bytes ride along with the message on submit. The status bar also shows Image in clipboard · ctrl+v to paste when an unpasted image is sitting in the clipboard."],["how-non-vision-models-handle-images","How non-vision models handle images","When the active provider can't take image input (text-only models like DeepSeek-V3 / Kimi), AtomCode doesn't refuse — it routes the image to a separate VL preprocessor (a vision model like Qwen3-VL / GLM-4V) for OCR + description, then splices the result into the user message as text before sending to the main model. So you can \"drop a screenshot and ask\" regardless of the main model. Which model does the preprocessor use? Controlled by vision_preprocessor_provider in the config — see Configuration · Vision preprocessor . The /login flow auto-picks a VL/OCR model from the granted list and sets the field for you. VL calls use an idle timeout : as long as the stream keeps producing chunks there's no total cap; it only times out after 30 seconds of silence. On failure you get a VL preprocess failed warning — image recognition fails but the message still goes through. Tip If the current model supports vision (Claude 3+ / GPT-4o / Gemini / Qwen-VL, etc.), the raw image bytes are sent directly — the preprocessor is skipped."],["switching-sessions-and-directories","Switching sessions and directories","/resume — switch between or restore previous sessions /session — start a clean session /cd or just type cd /path — switch working directory and start a new session (status bar updates live) /clear — clear messages in the current session /compact — compact history to free up context budget Full behaviour at Sessions & Undo ."],["inspecting-token-usage-and-diff","Inspecting token usage and diff","/cost — prompt, completion, and cached tokens accumulated per model in this session /diff — git diff of uncommitted changes in the working directory /undo — roll back every file edit from the last turn"],["next-steps","Next steps","Slash Commands — full reference for the 30+ commands Keybindings — fluency at the keyboard pays off quickly"]],"x":"Basic Usage Get fluent with CLI flags, how to phrase tasks, how to give the model context, and how to move between several tasks."},{"s":"slash-commands","t":"Slash Commands","y":"Sc","h":[["core","Core","Command Purpose /login Recommended — one command runs AtomGit OAuth + claims CodingPlan free tokens + auto-configures a provider from the granted model list. The lowest-friction entry point for first-time users; re-running after you're already signed in idempotently re-syncs the model list. As of v4.25.0 /codingplan has been folded into /login ; the standalone entry has been removed /resume Open the session picker to restore any previously persisted session (messages, directory, and model state) /session Start a fresh, clean session /background · /bg One command, two names — every form works under either. Bare: send the current session to the background and open a new foreground. With a task ( /background <task> ): start a one-shot task in a background slot directly. Subcommands: list , <N> , drop <N|id> , help . See Background sessions /rename <new-name> Rename the current session (changes the display name in the /resume picker) /provider Manage provider accounts and their models, using a vendor preset or a custom endpoint /model Set the default model / provider and switch the current session; other open sessions are unchanged /cd Switch to the requested directory and start a new session. You can also type cd /path directly."],["tools-utilities","Tools & utilities","Command Purpose /view · /view <filepath> Open a read-only file viewer. With no argument , a fuzzy files-only picker opens (type to filter; a path-like query such as ~/… or ./… can open a file outside the project). With a path, it opens that file directly. Scroll with arrows / PageUp-Down / Home-End (or g / G to jump to top/bottom); Esc backs out, Ctrl+C exits /undo · /undo N Roll conversation memory back to before the last turn (or turn N) and restore that prompt into the input box; rewinds memory only — does not revert files on disk /diff Show the git diff of uncommitted changes in the working directory (the file list shows up to 5 rows at a time with a \"more files\" scroll indicator) /review Code review the current changes: /review reviews uncommitted changes, /review staged the staged diff, /review <base> against a base ref /paste Attach an image from the clipboard (Windows fallback for when Ctrl+V is captured by the terminal) /cost Prompt, completion, and cached tokens accumulated per model in the current session. Distinct from /usage , which queries the CodingPlan gateway for your plan quota /context Show this turn's context budget breakdown: system prompt, tool defs, cold-zone compaction, total messages, and context-window usage /context prompt · /context persona TUI: inspect the currently assembled system prompt, or just the persona and append settings; see context and prompt inspection /compact Compact history: summarise earlier messages to free up context budget /rewind Choose an earlier prompt and roll back the conversation, code, or both; see Sessions & Undo /clear Clear the current session's messages (working directory and model are kept) /init Scan the working directory and create or improve the active project instruction file ( .atomcode.md , AGENTS.md , or CLAUDE.md , in precedence order). Output follows the current language; an optional custom prompt file can be configured under /config . /background <task> Dispatch a task to an isolated background agent (read-only-leaning tool subset) without polluting the main conversation. Useful for \"go check X on the side\" sort of light exploration. See Background sessions /worktree <subcommand> Git worktree isolation: create a new branch with its own worktree, list existing worktrees, done only return to the main checkout (no commit, squash or merge), cleanup remove a worktree (does not verify it is merged; commit and merge work you want to keep first; --force discards uncommitted content) /todo · /todo add <task> · /todo clear Reprint the current todo list — derived from the session transcript (locates the most recent todowrite tool call and re-renders it), with \"in-progress / done\" status markers. /todo add <task> appends a task deterministically (no model round-trip); /todo clear empties the list. The list is stateless (nothing extra is written to disk); the model maintains it during long tasks and you can run this anytime to check progress /copy Copy the last reply to the clipboard: /copy copies the whole reply as raw markdown (the whole turn, without tool output); /copy code copies the last code block, /copy code N the N-th, /copy code all every code block (the old /copy N , /copy all and /copy msg still work). /save Export the current conversation to a markdown file: /save uses an auto-generated filename, /save <filename> a name you choose AtomGit Issues are tools, not slash commands /issue has been removed. After /login , ask in natural language—for example, “Create an AtomGit issue for this bug.” AtomCode will select the built-in atomgit_issue tool; write actions still require approval. See Built-in Tools . Read-only reports run mid-turn You don't have to wait for a turn to finish to check on things: /status , /diff , /cost , /usage , and /rename run even while the agent is streaming. They render as a transient panel below the input box (press Esc to dismiss) without interrupting the running turn. /usage mid-turn is also tab-switchable across its Current / Overview / Models views."],["quality","Quality checks","/quality on enables checks, /quality off disables them, /quality status reports the current state, and /quality evidence shows the latest evidence. Quality is independent of Build / Auto approval modes; commands still obey existing permissions. Change the policy only while idle. Explicitly configure checks in your user configuration first. Replace these examples with the project's actual commands: [quality] # Disabled by default; /quality on enables it for the current session enabled = false [[quality.gates]] name = \"tests\" command = \"npm test -- --run\" timeout_secs = 120 [[quality.gates]] name = \"types\" command = \"npx tsc --noEmit\" timeout_secs = 60 After loading the configuration, ordinary tasks that change files run all checks sequentially before handoff. Quality Passed requires successful checks with no further file changes during verification. Failure, denial, timeout, cancellation, or evidence persistence failure cannot pass. Files are retained; no automatic rollback or commit occurs. After later edits, /quality status marks old results Stale. Unchanged tasks are NotRequired, which does not claim tests ran. To explicitly accept an unverified result after the task stops, run /quality waive <reason> . This adds an audited human waiver, retains the original failure evidence, and displays Waived rather than Passed. Future tasks remain gated. Passing only establishes that configured commands succeeded for the recorded file version, not that the code is bug-free. The first version supports ordinary foreground tasks in local Git worktrees with an initial commit; goal / loop, team delegation, and background commands are unavailable while it is enabled. Snapshots cover tracked files and nonignored new files, not ignored build artifacts or external services; submodules are unsupported. Each check allows 1–300 seconds. Snapshots allow up to 256 MiB of file contents, 64 MiB per file, and 32 MiB of diff; exceeding a limit refuses verification. Evidence under quality-evidence/ in the user data directory includes file fingerprints, diffs, commands, actual exit codes, durations, and output. It may contain private code or sensitive logs; review before sharing. After restart, the configuration determines the enabled state, and saved evidence remains readable."],["context-inspection","Context and prompt inspection","/context reports context-budget and usage statistics. In the TUI, /context prompt displays the system prompt assembled by the currently loaded components, while /context persona shows only the persona and its append settings. The system prompt is not the complete model request: tool definitions and conversation history are separate. These prompt-text inspection commands apply to the TUI; the WebUI's /context provides budget statistics only. For compaction protection and why prompts can change after resuming, see session prompt retention ."],["conversation-modes-thinking","Conversation modes & thinking","Command Purpose /plan Switch to Plan mode : read-only exploration. The model can call read_file / grep / list_directory and other non-writing tools, but edit_file / bash are blocked. Useful for getting alignment before action /build Switch back to Build mode (the default): all tools available — read, write, execute. /plan and /build are freely interchangeable /goal <text> Set a completion goal and let the agent run an autonomous loop — turn after turn — until the goal is met. /goal (no args) shows the current goal and round count; /goal clear stops it /loop <interval> <prompt or /command> Repeat a prompt or slash command on a fixed interval . e.g. /loop 5m /diff runs /diff every 5 minutes; /loop 30s check the build re-sends that prompt every 30 seconds. Interval units are s / m / h , range 10s–24h /loop <prompt> With no interval, enters self-paced mode: the task is handed to the model, which decides when to run the next round itself — good for \"keep at this until it converges\" work that doesn't map onto a fixed period /loop · /loop stop /loop (no args) shows the current loop status; /loop stop (or off / clear / cancel ) stops it. /loop and /goal are mutually exclusive — setting one automatically cancels the other /think on / off Toggle extended thinking (for supported models — Claude / DeepSeek-R1 / GLM-4.5 / …). When on, the model surfaces its reasoning at the cost of latency and tokens /think budget <N> Cap the thinking token budget (Claude family); controls reasoning length /effort <high|max|off> DeepSeek reasoning-effort control — trade latency/tokens for deeper reasoning on DeepSeek models"],["team-panel","Team panel","Command Purpose /team · /team toggle Expand / collapse the team panel (toggle). Collapsed, it keeps only its header row — member rows are not drawn and the keyboard no longer lands on them /team show · /team open Expand the team panel. With no members and no background tasks it answers \"No team members or background tasks; there is no team panel to show.\" /team hide · /team fold · /team close Collapse the team panel (members keep running in the background; none is cancelled), answering \"Team panel collapsed.\" Anything else Refused with the usage line — those three states are all /team takes ( status , clear and the like are not among them) All three subcommands only change what is drawn: the acknowledgement appears as a notice for about five seconds, does not enter the conversation, and does not call the model; none of them starts, cancels or waits for a member. The panel's header gives the member and background-task counts, and each member row says what it was asked to do, how long it has run and how much context it holds; members come from the agent delegating through the team tool (several in parallel, each with a role and scope). See also Subagents (short-lived subtasks via the task tool)."],["persistent-memory","Persistent memory","Command Purpose /remember <content> Write to project-scoped memory (default scope, bound to the current working directory) /remember --global <content> Write to global memory (shared across all projects) /forget <keyword> Delete every entry in global + project memory matching the keyword (case-insensitive) /memory Show all active memories, grouped by [Global] / [Project] Full usage and best practices at Persistent Memory ."],["extension-ecosystem","Extension ecosystem","Command Purpose /setup On first run, install the bundled atomcode-automation-recommender skill into ~/.atomcode/skills/ , append .atomcode/local/ to project .gitignore , and write .atomcode/setup-state.json (signals hash + atomcode version + installed list) under a project-level lock. Then invoke the recommender skill — it scans the project (languages, frameworks, hooks already in use), searches the web, and proposes additional atomcode skills to install for this codebase. Subsequent runs skip the seed install and re-invoke the skill directly. Extra text after the command is forwarded to the skill as a steering hint, e.g. /setup focus on testing . The CLI form atomcode setup --force forces a clean reinstall of seed files even when their content hash matches /skills Browse loaded skills (project- and user-level). Each skill also appears as a standalone slash command in the menu — trigger with /<skill-name> /plugin Open the interactive plugin manager — browse marketplaces, install/uninstall plugins, add/remove marketplaces from one screen /plugin marketplace add|remove|update|list Manage marketplace registrations (add clones a git repo, remove deletes, update pulls latest, list shows all) /plugin install <plugin>@<marketplace> Install a plugin from the named marketplace /plugin uninstall <plugin>@<marketplace> Uninstall an installed plugin (the marketplace registration is kept) /plugin list List locally installed plugins /plugin reload Reload all plugins (re-scan disk, refresh skill/hook registration) See Skills and Plugin System for details. Plugins can register their own slash commands. For example, the official channel plugin adds /wechat (shows the AtomCode WeChat community group QR code): /plugin marketplace add https://atomgit.com/atomgit_atomcode/AtomCode-Channel /plugin install weixin@atomcode-channel"],["mcp-integration","MCP integration","Command Purpose /mcp List successfully connected MCP servers and their status (failed servers don't show here — only as red error lines in the session area) /mcp tools <server> Async-list the remote tools actually exposed by a specific MCP server (you'll be told if it times out or fails) /mcp reload Re-read .mcp.json / ~/.atomcode/mcp.json and reconnect every server in the background Full configuration and usage at MCP Integration ."],["web-ui-sync","Web UI & sync","Command What it does /webui Open the local browser and show a phone relay QR; no VPN needed. Use --local for local access only. The current TUI session is attached to live sync automatically /webui --host <addr> Bind the server to a given address; /webui lan equals --host 0.0.0.0 (exposes it to the LAN). A usable LAN address is shown as both a text link and a QR code for your phone. Use the default /webui relay QR for remote access — see Remote Access /webui stop Stop the webui server /sync Attach the current TUI to a running webui session (run /webui first). Both ends sync live in both directions; multiple browsers / terminals can watch the same session /sync off Leave sync and return to a standalone session /app Expose the current session to the mobile App via the official relay: a QR code is printed right in the terminal, scan it with the App to pair, then view and drive this conversation live from your phone (same source as /webui — one shared session, two-way live sync; the difference is no browser, and it goes over the relay rather than the LAN). Requires /login first /app stop Stop App remote access, disconnect the relay, and return to a local session More in Web UI and the Remote Access guide."],["config-help","Config & help","Command Purpose /status Show login status, current provider, model, context budget, CodingPlan usage and reset time /whoami Show the username / email of the current AtomGit-logged-in user /config Show the path of ~/.atomcode/config.toml /reload Hot-reload ~/.atomcode/config.toml from disk — external edits (or changes from another terminal's /login ) take effect without restarting atomcode /proxy Switch outbound proxy mode: follow the system proxy (default) / force a specific proxy / connect directly with no proxy. For corporate proxy networks or when you need to force a proxy or force a direct connection; the choice is written back to config /language Switch UI language: auto-detect ( LC_ALL / LANG ), English, or Simplified Chinese. Takes effect immediately and is written back to ~/.atomcode/config.toml /welcome Re-open the 3-step first-run wizard (welcome → language → setup). Non-empty sessions are confirmed with a y/N before clearing the screen. Both language and default onboarding path can be revisited here /logout Clear the AtomGit OAuth token /upgrade Auto-upgrade to the latest version; /upgrade rollback reverts to the previous version /guide Built-in onboarding guide: /guide lists topics you can ask about (quickstart, switch model, MCP, Skills, memory, background tasks, context, keybindings, config); /guide <topic> explains it right in the chat (first run auto-installs the atomcode-skills plugin) /help List every available slash command /keys Show the keyboard-shortcut reference (grouped by input / history / session / modal navigation, with per-terminal compatibility notes for Shift+Enter and Alt+Enter ). See Keybindings /quit · /exit Exit atomcode (or hit Ctrl+C twice)"],["tips","Tips","Autocomplete — typing / pops up the menu immediately; use ↑↓ to navigate, Tab / Enter to confirm. Fuzzy match — completion supports substring matching, e.g. /prov hits /provider . Interrupt the model — while the model is streaming, press Esc to interrupt; you can then enter a new command or prompt. Skills appear in the menu — once you add your own commands under Skills , they show up in the menu in the same format."],["typical-workflows","Typical workflows",""],["first-launch-one-click-onboarding","First launch — one-click onboarding","> /login ✔ Logged in as alice (alice, alice@example.com) ✔ CodingPlan claimed — CodingPlan Lite · expires 2026-05-22 (29d / 30d) ✔ 3 models registered as AtomGit-* providers ✔ Default provider set to AtomGit-GLM > hello"],["check-token-usage-before-wrapping-up","Check token usage before wrapping up","> refactor src/db to use a connection pool ... (AI works) > /cost AtomGit · deepseek-v4-flash Prompt tokens: 7210 Completion tokens: 1132 Cached tokens: 5080 (70% hit rate) Total tokens: 8342"],["rewind-and-re-ask-when-the-answer-goes-sideways","Rewind and re-ask when the answer goes sideways","> add JSDoc to every function ... (the reply went off the rails) > /undo Rolled back to turn 3 of 3. ⚠ Only conversation memory was rewound; files on disk were not restored. Revert code manually or check /diff. (your last prompt is back in the input box — edit and resend)"],["swap-the-model-when-it-underperforms","Swap the model when it underperforms","> /model > (pick claude-opus-4-6 from the popup) > try again — this time preserve existing comments"],["next-steps","Next steps","Keybindings — pair commands with keybindings to double your speed Sessions & Undo — full behaviour of /resume , /undo , /compact"]],"x":"Slash Commands Start an input with / in the TUI to trigger a command and get an autocomplete menu. The 50+ built-in commands are organised below; commands loaded from Skills and Plugins also appear in the menu automatically."},{"s":"keybindings","t":"Keybindings","y":"Kb","h":[["input-editing","Input editing","Key Action Enter Send the message \\ then Enter Insert newline (universal — a trailing backslash makes the line a continuation, works in every terminal) Alt+Enter Insert newline (most terminals; macOS Apple Terminal needs \"Use Option as Meta key\" enabled under Settings → Profiles → Keyboard; Windows Terminal reserves it by default — release in settings) Shift+Enter Insert newline (only terminals that disambiguate the modifier: Kitty / WezTerm / iTerm2 with Report Modifiers / Windows Terminal / Ghostty / Warp. Apple Terminal, xterm, GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal all collapse it to Enter — use \\ + Enter instead) Ctrl+Enter Insert newline (requires a Kitty-keyboard-protocol terminal such as Kitty or WezTerm) Ctrl+J Insert newline when the terminal distinguishes the chord Esc Clear current input / interrupt streaming output Esc Esc Undo the previous turn when the prompt is idle and empty ↑ / ↓ Browse input history → Fill a faint next-prompt suggestion into an empty input (press Enter separately to send) Ctrl+R Reverse-search input history (type to filter live; Ctrl+R again jumps to the next older match; Enter accepts into the input, Esc cancels) Tab Accept slash-command, skill, or file completion Shift+Tab Cycle to the next execution mode when no completion menu is open (also works while streaming) Ctrl+D Delete forward; when idle and empty, press twice within two seconds to quit Ctrl+B / Ctrl+F Move one character left / right Ctrl+U Delete to the start of the current line Ctrl+W Delete a word Ctrl+K Delete from cursor to end of line Ctrl+A Move cursor to line start Ctrl+E Move cursor to line end while typing; edit the highlighted question option"],["custom-newline","Custom newline shortcuts","Open /config , search for “newline”, and select “Keyboard shortcuts / Newline”. Press Enter or A to add a chord, press that chord, then press Enter to confirm. Press M to type comma-separated names such as alt+j, ctrl+j ; Tab also switches capture to manual entry. Delete removes the selected binding, Ctrl+D restores defaults, and Esc goes back. [ui.keybindings] newline = [\"alt+j\", \"ctrl+j\"] The list replaces the default newline chords. Changes apply immediately and /keys shows the effective bindings. \\ + Enter remains available. Use newline = [] to disable the chords, or remove the newline entry to restore defaults. Conflicts with existing actions or reserved keys, duplicate chords, and invalid names are rejected without changing the active bindings. Plain printable characters cannot be shortcuts. Names accept ctrl , alt , shift , and cmd modifiers, letters, digits, enter , space , arrows, and f1 – f24 . AtomCode cannot detect or release shortcuts intercepted by the terminal or IDE; verify that manually entered chords reach the app."],["browse-scroll","Browse & scroll","Key Action PageUp / PageDown Page by the visible conversation height, keeping one overlap row Mouse wheel Scroll the conversation /read Open a read-only conversation snapshot with expanded tool output; no GUI or clipboard required ↑ / ↓ / j / k Reader: scroll one line PgUp / PgDn / Ctrl+B / Ctrl+F Reader: page up / down Ctrl+U / Ctrl+D Reader: half-page up / down Home / End Reader: jump to beginning / end Esc Leave the reader, preserving the draft and main scroll position; reopen /read to refresh the snapshot"],["selection-copy","Selection & copy","Key / action Effect Mouse drag Select text in the chat area (atomcode-managed; auto-scrolls at selection edges) Shift+ mouse drag Use the host terminal's native selection (bypasses atomcode; better for cross-viewport copy) Ctrl+Shift+C Copy selection to system clipboard Right-click menu Some terminals offer direct copy/paste (depends on the terminal, not atomcode)"],["control-flow","Control flow","Key Action F2 / Shift+F2 Switch to the next / previous configured model; Mac keyboards usually require Fn+F2 / Fn+Shift+F2 Ctrl+T Show / hide the tool-output fold F3 / Shift+F3 Step to the next / previous declared reasoning-effort level; Mac keyboards usually need Fn+F3 / Fn+Shift+F3 . The levels are the closed set /effort offers Ctrl+O Show / hide tool output and reasoning (verbose mode) Esc Cancel the in-progress tool call or streaming output Ctrl+C First press cancels the current action; second consecutive press exits"],["new-screen","New screen (atomcode --tui)","Most keys are the same as above; these differ. Type /keys in a session for the full list. Key Action Ctrl+O Reasoning: one line / in full / folded, cycles (also /reasoning ; Alt+R works too when the terminal sends Option as Meta) Ctrl+T Tool output: all / one summary each / summarised in groups, cycles; the opening step opens answered approvals too (the way to them while the mouse is handed back and a click cannot reach them) Ctrl+G Hand the mouse to the terminal (use its own selection), again to take it back (also /mouse ). While it is handed back the wheel, the trackpad and ↑ ↓ scroll the conversation; with [ui] mouse = false it starts that way Ctrl+P / Ctrl+N Step through the input history (always; with the mouse handed back ↑ ↓ scroll, so these are the way to the history) Ctrl+X Interrupt the current turn and immediately send the queued messages, one per turn (each with its image); with nothing queued it is a plain interrupt Double-tap Esc Open the rewind panel (same as /rewind ) to pick an earlier prompt to roll back"],["tool-permission-dialog","Tool permission dialog","When the model is about to execute a dangerous action (destructive bash, writing sensitive files, deleting source code, etc.), AtomCode pops a confirmation dialog: Key Action y / Enter Allow once a Always allow this pattern for the current session n / Esc Deny Don't get greedy \"Always allow\" is granted per tool name + argument pattern and only for the current session — it resets next launch. For permanent cross-session exceptions, manage them in config (e.g. allowlists for specific paths)."],["next-steps","Next steps","Slash Commands — pair keybindings with command completion Sessions & Undo — what /undo actually undoes"]],"x":"Keybindings AtomCode's TUI is built on ratatui + crossterm; common keybindings stick close to the conventions of mainstream terminal tools. Run /keys in a session to dump this table into the current scrollback, or /help for the slash-command list."},{"s":"sessions","t":"Sessions & Undo","y":"Ud","h":[["session-lifecycle","Session lifecycle","Each atomcode launch creates a session. A session contains: Full message history (user prompts, AI replies, tool calls) The associated working directory The associated provider / model Token usage stats File-history snapshots of every file edit made in that session Session data is persisted under ~/.atomcode/sessions/ , grouped by project (working-directory hash)."],["prompt-retention","Are the system prompt and original task retained?","Distinguish the system prompt , assembled by AtomCode from its persona, project instructions and capability guidance, from your first task message , which is your own input. Content During normal conversation and compaction The currently active system prompt Continues to be used in subsequent model requests. Ordinary history summarization does not discard it. The text of the first real user message Is protected from compaction. Normal compaction does not delete the original task or replace it with a summary. Later messages and tool results May be summarized or shortened. Saving session records to disk does not mean every request sends their entire original text. This describes normal context compaction. Explicitly running /clear , starting a new session with /session , or rolling back the conversation with /undo / /rewind changes the effective history. Images and other attachments may also be converted or folded separately; protecting message text does not mean attachments are always sent unchanged."],["prompt-resume","Is the system prompt identical after resuming?","/resume and --continue restore effective history from persisted session records, including the original task when it is still part of that history. Saved session context also participates in restoration. The system prompt is assembled from the currently loaded components; version, configuration or project-instruction changes can make it differ from the prompt at session creation. Resuming is not a byte-for-byte replay of the original model request."],["inspect-system-prompt","Where can I inspect the current system prompt?","In the TUI , use: /context prompt # Inspect the currently assembled system prompt /context persona # Inspect the persona and its append settings /context # Inspect context-budget and usage statistics /context prompt shows the application-assembled system prompt, not a complete model request containing tool definitions and all conversation history. These prompt-text inspection commands refer to the TUI; the WebUI's /context budget statistics are not a full prompt viewer. See the command reference ."],["resuming-sessions","Resuming sessions",""],["continue-the-last-one-from-the-cli","Continue the last one from the CLI","atomcode -c # or atomcode --continue The most common case: pick up exactly where you left off yesterday."],["switch-sessions-inside-the-tui","Switch sessions inside the TUI","/resume Opens the session picker. It lists this project's historical sessions newest-first; jump to any of them quickly. Each entry uses the most recent user prompt as its label for easy recognition. While a turn runs, select another session in /resume or run /resume <id> . The current session keeps running in the background; the view switches only after the target is ready. A failed open leaves the current session intact. Returning to a background session in this process reuses its runtime instead of restarting the task. Use /bg list to inspect up to 16 background slots. Switching remains restricted while awaiting approval or interactive input, reconfiguring, or sharing live sync with the WebUI. If all slots are full, stop an unneeded session with /bg drop <N> . This applies to the TUI; it does not add running-session switching to the WebUI."],["start-a-clean-new-session","Start a clean new session","/session Spin up a fresh context without changing the working directory. Good for \"the previous task is wrapped — onto something totally unrelated\"."],["bg","Background sessions ( /background · /bg )","Need to juggle multiple tasks without losing the current conversation? /background (alias /bg ; the two are equivalent) parks the current session in the background and opens a fresh foreground — switch back any time. Up to 16 concurrent background slots . Command What it does /bg Send the current session to the background and open a new foreground /background <task> (same as /bg <task> ) Start a one-shot task in a background slot without swapping foreground (see below) /bg list (alias /bg ls ) List all background sessions: slot, ID, state, created, summary /bg <N> Resume slot N as foreground (the current foreground is swapped to background) /bg drop <N> Drop background slot N /bg help (aliases -h , --help ) Show built-in help"],["session-states","Session states","The state column in /bg list reflects what each background session is doing: running — the model loop is still executing; tool calls and output keep advancing in the background idle — the model turn finished; waiting for your next prompt done — the session was explicitly ended cancelled / error — interrupted, or the background run hit an error So /bg isn't just \"suspend\" — the model actually keeps working in the background; when you switch back, the result is already there."],["background-task-one-shot-dispatch","/background <task> — one-shot dispatch","If you don't want to swap foreground/background manually and just want to \"have it look something up real quick\", just pass a task (both names work) — /background <task> or /bg <task> : /background list every unused dependency under src It starts a one-shot task in a /bg slot (configured with a read-only tool subset by default so the main conversation context isn't polluted). When done, check /bg list , use /bg <N> to read the result, /bg drop <N> to discard. Typical pattern The foreground is debugging module A; the model is editing and running cargo check (slow). You realise you also want to refactor module B — /bg straight to a new foreground for B. The build on A finishes in the background, state flips to done ; /bg 1 to switch back and read the result."],["background-lifetime-and-multiple-processes","Background lifetime and multiple processes","Background sessions depend on this AtomCode process. Exiting stops their runtimes; this is not process-independent execution. Saved conversations can be resumed, but their original tool processes are not guaranteed to keep running. One installation is enough: run the same executable in multiple terminals with different sessions. Different sessions in the same project and home can run concurrently. An exclusive lease prevents two runtimes from writing the same session in the same storage bucket. Interactive resume may fork a session held by another process; check the notice. Config writes use a cross-process lock and atomic replacement, but settings remain shared. Separate ATOMCODE_HOME values isolate configuration and session storage. Neither session leases nor separate homes protect project files. Use separate Git worktrees when agents edit concurrently to avoid conflicting file or Git operations."],["clear-vs-compact-vs-new-session","Clear vs compact vs new session","Command Keeps history Keeps session ID When to use /clear No Yes \"Reset the dialogue\" within the same session; keep the session entry so you can /resume later /compact Partial (summarised) Yes Context is filling up but you don't want to lose the earlier thread /session Starts new thread No (new ID) Beginning a completely unrelated task"],["rewinding-conversation-memory-with-undo","Rewinding conversation memory with /undo","/undo rewinds conversation memory to before a given turn — removing that turn and everything after it — and drops the prompt you typed for that turn back into the input box so you can edit and resend it. /undo # rewind the last turn /undo N # rewind to turn N (1-based; counts only the prompts you actually typed) The scrollback dividers for the removed turns are cleared too, and the session is saved immediately — so your next /resume reflects the rewound state. Where the boundary is /undo rewinds conversation memory only — it does not restore files on disk. If the AI edited code during those turns, those changes stay in your working tree; use /diff to review and revert them manually, or rely on git. You can't /undo while a turn is in flight — press Esc to cancel it first."],["safe-rollback-with-rewind","Safe rollback with /rewind","/rewind lists recent user prompts and lets you choose the scope: conversation only, code only, or both conversation and code. Code rollback requires a Git worktree and is confirmed before it runs. For a simple one-turn conversation rollback, /undo remains the lighter option."],["recovery-after-an-interrupted-exit","Recovery after an interrupted exit","AtomCode saves temporary progress while a turn is running. After a terminal crash or network interruption, /resume attempts to restore the last user prompt, generated response, and tool-call progress instead of falling back to the previous completed turn. Pending permissions and questions are never auto-approved."],["inspecting-and-managing-token-usage","Inspecting and managing token usage","/cost Shows cumulative input / output tokens for the current session. When the number approaches the provider's context_window : Use /compact to compact history (early messages become a summary) Or just /session and start fresh To avoid keeping large tool-call results, tell the model in the prompt to \"stop re-reading those big files\""],["context-summary-count","Context summary count","TUI and WebUI show the recorded summary count beside existing token usage, hidden before the first summary. Progress appears in the running status or conversation, never in the footer; completion leaves a numbered record. Failures, cancellations, no-ops and tool-output cleanup do not increase the count. The count comes from the session event log, so resume and reconnect do not double count it, and a new session starts fresh. Unknown history before import cannot be reconstructed; undo does not erase the historical fact that a summary happened."],["multi-project-workflows","Multi-project workflows","AtomCode groups sessions by working directory. Recommended ways to switch: From the CLI, specify with -C Use /cd in the TUI to switch directories and start a fresh session. On the next launch, use -C to choose a directory or /resume to restore the relevant session."],["next-steps","Next steps","Project Instructions — lock in per-project context with .atomcode.md"]],"x":"Sessions & Undo AtomCode persists every conversation by default, so you can restore, resume, clear, or compact at any time. A single /undo rewinds conversation memory back to any earlier turn."},{"s":"interactive-questions","t":"Interactive Questions","y":"Iq","h":[["the-three-question-types","The three question types","Type Behaviour single Radio list — pick exactly one option. Submits immediately on Enter . multiple Checkboxes — pick any number, then confirm on the Submit row. text Free-form text answer, no options. For single and multiple , an “Other — type your own answer” row is offered as well, so you are never trapped inside the listed options. The model cannot disable this free-text answer channel."],["answering-in-the-terminal","Answering in the terminal","Key Action ↑ / ↓ Move between options (and the Other / Submit rows) 1 – 9 Jump to (single) or toggle (multiple) the N-th option Space Toggle the current checkbox (multiple); type a space when editing the Other row Enter single: submit the highlighted option · multiple: submit from the Submit row · text: submit the buffer type / Backspace Edit the Other row or the free-text answer Ctrl+E Edit the highlighted option; inside an input, move to the end Esc Cancel the current option edit; otherwise decline the whole request Ctrl+C Decline the whole request, including while editing A single question needs just one keystroke to answer (highlight, then Enter ). A multiple question toggles rows with Enter / Space and only confirms when you activate the dedicated Submit row."],["editing-options","Edit a suggested answer","Highlight an option and press Ctrl+E to edit its label inline, with the caret at the end. In single choice, Enter confirms the answer. In multiple choice, it saves and checks that option; use the Submit row to send the full answer. Several options can be edited independently, without also submitting their original labels or overwriting the Other draft. Esc discards the current edit. Search for “Edit question option” in /config to change the shortcut, or configure: [ui.keybindings] question_edit = \"alt+e\" Editing applies only to ordinary questions; permission choices remain fixed. Batch pages preserve drafts, and unfinished edits must be saved or cancelled before submission."],["several-questions-at-once","Several questions at once","When the agent has more than one thing to ask at the same decision point, it batches them — up to four — into a single panel instead of interrupting you repeatedly. Use Tab to move between questions, answer each, and submit them together in one round-trip. A lone question renders exactly as before."],["in-the-web-ui","In the Web UI","The same questions surface as a UserInputCard in the Web UI : radio buttons, checkboxes, or a text box, plus the same optional free-text row. A batch becomes a small stepper — step forward / back with the → / ← buttons, then one Submit that posts every answer at once. Skip declines. Answers stream back over the live SSE channel, so a turn driven from the browser pauses and resumes just like the terminal. Use “Edit option” beside a suggestion to modify its text. “Confirm answer” confirms a single choice; “Save and select” keeps an edited multiple-choice item for the final submission. Enter confirms and Esc cancels an edit. Going back to a batch page preserves its changes."],["turning-it-off","Turning it off","The feature is enabled by default. To opt out, set the environment variable before launching: ATOMCODE_REQUEST_USER_INPUT=0 atomcode Any of 0 , false , off , or an empty value disables it; unset (or any other value) leaves it on. When disabled, the agent never asks — it always proceeds with its best judgment. Bypass mode auto-skips questions In Bypass / 免审批 mode the panel is skipped automatically and the agent proceeds without waiting. Build , Plan , and Accept Edits modes all show the question as normal."],["related","Related","Permissions & Approvals — the separate permission-gate system Web UI — approval modes and the browser experience Configuration — environment variables and settings"]],"x":"Interactive Questions At a genuine fork in the road — ambiguous requirements, a choice between two workable designs — the agent can pause and ask you a structured question instead of guessing. You answer inline; it resumes with your choice. This is backed by the request_user_input tool and is on by default . Not the same as an approval A permission approval asks whether the agent may run a tool (a command, a file edit). An interactive question asks for your decision — a preference or a choice between approaches. Different panel, different keys, different meaning. Declining a question is never an error; declining an approval blocks the tool."},{"s":"tools","t":"Built-in Tools","y":"Tl","h":[["filesystem-shell-9","Files & Shell","Tool Purpose Confirmation? read_file Read file content; supports line offset and range No write_file Write a full file (overwrite) Sensitive paths: yes edit_file String-match local edits; returns the edited context Sensitive paths: yes search_replace Batch string replacements; good for multi-line / multi-site patterns Sensitive paths: yes bash Run shell commands; destructive commands trigger the permission dialog Destructive: yes grep Regex search with ripgrep semantics No glob Filename glob matching (e.g. src/**/*.ts ) No list_directory List directory contents No Sensitive paths Writes to paths like /etc , ~/.ssh , and shell rc files always trigger the permission dialog — \"always allow\" cannot skip them. Likewise, rm on source files always needs explicit confirmation. Background long-running tasks Start long-running commands with bash_start , then use the returned job ID with bash_poll to read output or bash_kill to stop the job. Use pwsh_start to start a PowerShell job, and the same bash_poll and bash_kill tools to manage it. Use /cd to change the session working directory. Destructive-command guard High-risk commands like rm -rf , dd , mkfs , and sudo , plus schema-destroying database migrations (e.g. migrate:fresh , db:reset ), always force a permission prompt. This confirmation always fires — even a prior \"always allow\" on bash cannot skip it."],["code-graph-8","Code graph (8)","This is what sets AtomCode apart from generic agents. With the code-graph index, the model can pinpoint symbols, references, and call relationships without scanning the entire tree — especially valuable on large repos. Tool Purpose list_symbols List all symbols defined in a file or directory (functions, classes, constants, …) read_symbol Read a symbol's full definition surgically, without dragging the entire file into context find_references Find every location that references a symbol trace_callers Walk the caller chain of a function backwards trace_callees Expand a function's downstream calls trace_chain Search for a possible call chain between two symbols file_deps Analyse a file's imports / dependency graph blast_radius Estimate the files / symbols a change to a given symbol could affect"],["typical-scenarios","Typical scenarios","Pre-refactor risk assessment — \"How big is the blast if I change formatDate 's signature?\" The model calls blast_radius + find_references . Bug root-causing — \"Why doesn't this button respond?\" Start at the entry function and trace_callees downward. Understanding unfamiliar code — \"Walk me through AuthService.login \" → read_symbol + trace_callees ."],["web-2","Web (2)","Tool Purpose web_search Search the web for keywords; returns a list of title / snippet / URL web_fetch Fetch a URL and convert it to markdown for the model Common uses include reading documentation, comparing library APIs, and reading public issues."],["automation-2","Skills","Tool Purpose list_skills List available skills. use_skill Invoke a user-defined skill — package a multi-step flow as a reusable command See Skills for details."],["atomgit","AtomGit integration (3)","After /login , the model can operate AtomGit directly through these built-in tools. Describe the outcome in natural language; there is no /issue slash command. Tool Purpose Confirmation? atomgit_repo List current-account repositories (not public search); inspect code repositories by owner/repo or repository URL; create, delete, fork, clone, create tags and manage labels. An empty personal list does not mean a public repository is missing. Model/dataset sites are outside this URL lookup scope. Writes: yes atomgit_pr List, inspect, create, close, and comment on pull requests; link or unlink related Issues Writes: yes atomgit_issue List or inspect Issues; create an Issue and view, add, edit, or delete comments Writes: yes Ask: Create an AtomGit issue for this bug, including the reproduction steps and environment."],["large-tool-outputs","Large tool outputs","When a tool result is too large, AtomCode shows a stable preview and stores the full content with the current session. The model can page through the remainder with fetch_output , so “output truncated” does not mean the result was lost. Stored output is removed when its session is deleted."],["disabling-specific-tools","Disabling specific tools","In the TUI, use /toolbox to inspect the current session’s tools. Turn matching tools off with /toolbox off <name-or-pattern> and back on with /toolbox on <name-or-pattern> . In headless mode, use --no-tools to remove the entire model tool catalog."],["next-steps","Next steps","Sessions & Undo — every file-edit tool routes through file-history, so /undo can roll back changes Skills — wrap your own workflows with use_skill"]],"x":"Built-in Tools AtomCode ships built-in tools for filesystem & shell, code graph, web, automation, and native AtomGit operations. The model picks tools per task — you almost never need to specify them by hand."},{"s":"subagents","t":"Subagents","y":"Sa","h":[["two-kinds-of-subagent","Two kinds of subagent","Type What it can do explore Read-only investigation — reads and searches the codebase to answer a “where / how” question, then returns findings. Cannot edit files. worker Executes a tightly-specified change. Reads freely, but its writes are confined to a declared scope ."],["how-they-run","How they run","Subagents run in parallel, up to max_concurrent at a time, each in an isolated context. The native task accepts a model selection ID on each call. When omitted, it uses the current session's model. Only models available for delegation in this session can be named. The main agent reviews each result before continuing — a subagent proposes, the main agent decides."],["worker-scope-safety","Worker scope & safety","A worker subtask must declare a scope : a list of working-directory-relative globs it is allowed to write, e.g. [\"src/auth/**\", \"Cargo.toml\"] . This is enforced, not advisory: Writes outside the scope ( edit_file , write_file , search_replace ) are hard-denied — not prompted — by the WorkerScopeGate. Available tools depend on the runtime configuration. Team members have no general-purpose shell. A dispatch that contains any worker is treated as a Risky action, so it goes through approval first, with the scopes shown. When several workers run at once, give them non-overlapping scopes so they cannot clobber each other."],["configuration","Configuration","Tune the subagent pool in ~/.atomcode/config.toml : [subagent] max_concurrent = 3 # parallel subagents at once (min 1) max_rounds = 0 # per-subtask model-round cap (0 = unbounded) Child rounds are unlimited by default; existing explicit positive budgets are preserved. Set [subagent] max_rounds = 0 or ATOMCODE_SUBAGENT_MAX_ROUNDS=0 to remove an old 200-round limit. Positive budgets allow at most one extra text-only closing request. Concurrency, cancellation and repetition guards remain independent. External Codex/Claude agents retain their own execution policies. Key Default Meaning max_concurrent 3 How many subagents run in parallel max_rounds 0 Model-round high-water mark per subtask; 0 = unbounded Environment overrides: ATOMCODE_SUBAGENT_MAX_ROUNDS take precedence over the config values."],["custom-team-roles","Custom team roles","The team ( team ) picks members by role . Besides the built-in roles you can define your own as Markdown files in either of: <project>/.atomcode/agents/<role>.md — this project only; ~/.atomcode/agents/<role>.md — every project. The file name (without .md ) is the role's name. A file named like a built-in role replaces it; when both directories have a file of the same name, the one in your home directory wins. A role file is a header of fields between --- lines, then the role's instructions: --- permission: explore # required: explore (looks, changes nothing) | worker (may edit files within its assigned scope) difficulty: hard # required: simple (the fast model) | hard (the strong one) effort: high # optional: low | medium | high | xhigh | max model: glm-4.6 # optional: a model selection id, overriding difficulty when: designing systems # optional: one line on when to hand it work tools: read_file, grep # optional: limit its tools, chosen from what permission allows --- You design. Read the existing code first, then propose a design and its trade-offs. Field Required Values permission yes explore (read-only investigation) or worker (scoped writes) difficulty yes simple (fast model) or hard (strong model) effort no low / medium / high / xhigh / max model no inherit uses the parent model, auto chooses by difficulty from eligible ranked models, or supply a model selection ID. Omission keeps legacy difficulty routing. when no One line on when to hand this role work tools no Comma-separated tool names, selected from permitted built-ins and read-only MCP queries granted to this role allowed_tools no Inline array alias for tools . Omit for role defaults, or use [] to clear this list. denied_tools no Inline array of tool names to remove, even if also allowed. allowed_mcp_servers no Inline array of servers. Only previously granted read-only queries are eligible. Omit to keep the existing per-tool behavior, or use [] to disable MCP for the role. Use a build that supports these fields when sharing role files. Older builds ignore the new tool-list fields. For a role shared with older builds, keep using the tools: allowlist they understand. Two things to note: This permission is not the CLI's --permission-mode ( plan / accept_edits / auto ); they only share a name. This one decides whether the member may change anything; that one is how the whole session asks for approval. This is not Claude Code's agent file format. name , description and user_invocable are not read: the role's name is the file name, and its tools are limited with tools . A role file that does not parse is skipped and the session starts anyway. You are told once per session which file was skipped and everything that is missing or wrong in it; a file named like a built-in role leaves the built-in in use."],["query-skill-documentation-from-a-team-member","Query skill documentation from a Team member","In the user-level mcp.json , add a per-role grant to the documentation server. For example, on the docs server, grant the research role one tool: \"teamReadOnlyTools\": {\"research\": [\"search_docs\"]} Set tools: read_file, mcp__docs__search_docs in research.md . The server must be connected and advertise readOnlyHint for that tool. User-level grants apply across projects by role name. Grant only trusted read-only implementations. Project MCP configurations cannot issue these grants. Members receive tell_parent automatically. Each query leaves a reference in the lead session without waking the lead. The lead can use team(action=\"evidence\", name=\"member\", reference=\"reference\") to inspect the original arguments, returned text and error status, including after resuming in the same project. For a Python-only skill, the repository example examples/mcp/skill_docs.py exposes a fixed lookup script over stdio MCP. Install the adapter and trusted skill in a user-controlled location. Configure the server command as uv with arguments run , --script , the absolute adapter path and the absolute path to the installed scripts/search_docs.py . Append --query-option=--query if the script requires a named query argument. The example passes one search string and expects UTF-8 text."],["turning-it-off","Turning it off","The task tool is enabled by default. To remove it entirely, set: ATOMCODE_SUBAGENT=0 atomcode Any of 0 , false , or off disables it; unset (or any other value) leaves it on."],["related","Related","Built-in Tools — the tools a subagent has access to Permissions & Approvals — why a worker dispatch asks for approval Configuration — the full config.toml reference"]],"x":"Subagents When a task splits cleanly — parallel edits, mechanical repetition, or read-only investigation — the main agent can hand subtasks to short-lived subagents through the task tool. Each subagent runs in its own isolated context; the main agent keeps the cross-file reasoning and owns the final result. The task tool is on by default ."},{"s":"approvals","t":"Permissions & Approvals","y":"Ap","h":[["model","The core: four approval levels","This is the spine of the whole page. Before any tool runs, it lands in one of these four levels: Level What it means Can “Always allow” remember it? Auto-approve Runs straight away, no interruption. Safe in-project actions live here. — (never asks) Ask Prompts; choosing “Always allow this session” stops asking for that tool for the rest of the session. ✅ yes Always ask Prompts every time, even after you pressed “Always” — reserved for destructive / high-risk actions. ❌ no Scoped ask Prompts; “Always allow” remembers only this one resource (e.g. a single file). A different one still asks. same resource only Keep these four in mind — everything below is just \"which level does this action land in, and why.\""],["triggers","Which actions hit which level","Rule of thumb: working inside the current project directory flows freely ( Auto-approve ); reaching outside it, touching secrets, or running something destructive escalates to a level that needs your confirmation. Action Triggered when… Level Shell ( bash ) destructive command rm -rf , dd , git push --force , chmod , mkfs … Always ask Shell reads/writes outside the project The command touches a path outside the project dir read = Ask / write = Always ask Edit / create / replace file The target is a sensitive file or outside the project Always ask (sensitive / outside) Read file / list symbols / diagnostics Reading a sensitive file outside the project (e.g. ~/.ssh/id_rsa ) sensitive = Scoped ask / plain outside = Ask web_fetch URL points at a private / loopback address (public sites auto-approve) Ask MCP tool call Every call — unless the tool or its server is trusted Ask Always auto-approved: reading, searching, globbing and editing inside the project, plus cd , list_dir , grep , web_search , and the todo list."],["test-command-rules","Authorize repeated project tests","User/project JSON settings support command rules. For example, in the project's .atomcode/settings.local.json : { \"permissions\": { \"allow\": [\"Bash(cargo test --bin ponent defense_tests*)\"], \"deny\": [\"Bash(git push --force*)\"] } } A granted command can be combined with read-only helpers and fixed numeric loops: cd /project && for i in 1 2 3; do cargo test --bin ponent defense_tests 2>&1 | tail -5; done . Each command is checked separately; deny rules win. Dynamic expansions, loops that change directories and file-writing redirects use the normal approval flow. This authorizes running project code; it does not classify tests as read-only or confine their filesystem/network effects. Credential and sensitive-path checks still apply."],["choices","Your choices on a prompt","When a tool lands in Ask / Always-ask / Scoped-ask, you get these options: Deny — reject this call; the agent continues without it. Approve — allow just this one call. Always allow this session — remember for the rest of the session (in memory only; gone when you quit). Has no effect on the Always ask level; on Scoped ask it remembers only the current resource. Always allow this tool — MCP tools only. Permanently auto-approve this one tool by writing it to mcp.json (see two-tier consent ). In the terminal: y / Enter approve, a always-this-session, n / Esc deny, Ctrl+C cancel the whole turn. In the web UI these are buttons on the approval card."],["mcp","Two-tier consent for MCP tools","MCP tools call external code , so they default to the Ask level. If you trust a tool or a server you can lift it to Auto-approve — across three levels, from least to most durable, and only the first two are reachable from a button: Always allow this session (the [A] key / button) — in memory, this session, this tool only . Always allow this tool (button, MCP only) — persistent, this tool only . Appends the bare tool name to that server's autoApprove list in mcp.json : { \"mcpServers\": { \"my-docs\": { \"command\": \"my-docs-server\", \"autoApprove\": [\"query\", \"search\"] } } } Trust the whole server — hand-edit only. No runtime button ever sets this: { \"mcpServers\": { \"my-docs\": { \"command\": \"my-docs-server\", \"trust\": true } } } Why a single click can't trust a whole server MCP tools run with their own permissions and bypass AtomCode's own path/command guards — a server can write files, hit the network, or spend money. The approval prompt is your gate. trust: true auto-approves every tool on that server, including write/destructive ones you've never seen, so it's deliberately something only you can set by editing the file — a stray click (or a prompt-injection trick) can never escalate one approval into permanent, whole-server trust. Reserve trust: true for servers you fully control (ideally local and read-only)."],["sensitive","Sensitive paths","“Sensitive” is what pushes an outside-the-project path into Always ask (writes) or Scoped ask (reads). These count as sensitive: System directories — /etc , /usr , /System , /Windows , /Program Files … Secret directories — ~/.ssh , ~/.aws , ~/.gnupg Secret files — .env , credentials , id_rsa , *.pem , *.key , *.p12 … Ordinary application config ( ~/.config/<app>/… ) is not treated as a secret. Two details that echo the levels above: reading a sensitive file is Scoped ask — “Always allow” remembers only that one file (so re-reading it in chunks stops re-prompting), while a different file still asks; writing outside the project and destructive commands are Always ask — they prompt every time and can't be silenced with “Always.”"],["web","Web fetching","web_fetch auto-approves public sites; it only drops to the Ask level for loopback / private-network / link-local literals ( 127.0.0.1 , 192.168.x , localhost , *.local ). Either way, fetching always enforces SSRF protection at execution time : it re-resolves the host and refuses loopback, private and cloud-metadata addresses and any non- http(s) scheme — so relaxing the prompt never weakens the actual safety check."],["modes","Two special modes","Plan mode: the agent is restricted to read-only tools — it can't edit, write, or run shell — so no change-approval prompts appear at all. This is a tool restriction, not a blanket permission grant. --dangerously-skip-permissions (dangerous) Launching with this flag short-circuits all four levels to auto-approve — including rm -rf , git push --force , and writes outside the project — with no prompts at all. Only use it in throwaway or sandboxed environments you don't mind losing."],["project-rules","Approval reasons and project rules","Approval requests show the specific reason, matching permission rules and their source files, and command segments not covered by allow rules. Eligible Bash requests also offer “Approve and save exact project rule”, previewing the complete rule and destination .atomcode/settings.local.json path before confirmation. This approves the pending call and saves an exact command rule, effective after reload or in a new session. Other configuration fields are preserved. Existing deny rules, invalid settings, a project change or a failed save reject the operation rather than silently approving it. Independent security approvals such as sensitive paths do not offer this save action."],["config","Config reference","MCP trust lives in mcp.json — project-level .mcp.json or user-level ~/.atomcode/mcp.json — per server: Field Effect trust: true Lift all of the server's tools to Auto-approve . Hand-set only. autoApprove: [\"toolA\", …] Lift specific tools to Auto-approve . The “Always allow this tool” button appends here."],["next","Next","Built-in Tools — what each tool does and what it can touch MCP Integration — adding servers, and where trust / autoApprove live Configuration — config files and precedence"]],"x":"Permissions & Approvals AtomCode runs tools on your behalf — editing files, running shell commands, fetching the web, calling MCP servers. Its safety model fits in one sentence: every tool call is sorted into one of four “approval levels,” and the level decides whether it runs straight away, pauses to ask you, and whether choosing “Always allow” can remember it. This page starts with that model , then unfolds it: which actions hit which level, the choices you get on a prompt, and how to make it ask less — without giving away the safety net."},{"s":"skills","t":"Skills","y":"Sk","h":[["what-skills-are-good-for","What skills are good for","Codifying frequent workflows: cutting a release, writing a changelog, running regression tests, generating weekly reports… Wrapping complex tasks that need step-by-step guidance: refactor playbooks, bug root-cause analysis, performance tuning Making the model follow your defined steps and validation rules on a specific topic"],["skill-file-layout","Skill file layout","A skill is usually a directory containing at least a SKILL.md : my-skills/ ├── release/ │ └── SKILL.md ├── write-changelog/ │ └── SKILL.md └── debug-flaky-test/ ├── SKILL.md └── references/ └── pattern-library.md A typical SKILL.md : --- name: release description: Cut a new release tag, update the changelog, and publish --- ## When to use When the user says \"ship a new version\", \"cut a release\", or \"tag it\". ## Steps 1. Inspect `git log` for changes since the last release. 2. Ask the user to confirm the semver bump (patch / minor / major). 3. Add the new entry to `CHANGELOG.md`. 4. Run `pnpm build` and ensure it passes. 5. Create the git tag `v<version>` with release notes. 6. Run `pnpm publish` (or the corresponding publish command). ## Rules - Version numbers must follow semver. - Never skip tests — fix any failure first. - If publish fails, roll back the local tag and changelog edits."],["skill-names","Skill names and display titles","name is the stable invocation identifier. It supports Chinese and is limited to 1–64 characters. When omitted, directory skills use the directory name and standalone Markdown skills use the filename. The optional display-name supplies a human-readable title; without it, menus keep showing the identifier. --- name: linyaps-packager display-name: 玲珑打包技能 description: Generate application packaging configuration --- Menus show the title alongside /linyaps-packager and support searching by either. Selecting a skill inserts its identifier. You can also invoke it with $linyaps-packager or /skills linyaps-packager . Renaming the title does not change invocation; titles are not aliases. A display-name may contain up to 128 characters. Control, zero-width and bidirectional control characters are rejected with a warning and a fallback."],["bundled-resources","Bundled resources","A loaded directory skill can use read_file to read files beside its SKILL.md and in its subdirectories, including installed plugin skills outside the workspace. Resolve relative resource paths against the skill directory. A standalone Markdown skill grants access only to that file. This adds read access only: workspace write restrictions and sensitive-file approvals still apply. Links cannot extend a skill's access to unrelated locations. Reload skills after disabling or removing them to update the execution world's resource access."],["allowed-tools","Tool preauthorization: allowed-tools","allowed-tools preauthorizes matching tools for the turn that invokes a skill. It is not an exclusive tool whitelist: other tools remain available and follow normal permission and approval rules. Prefer allowed-tools . The underscore alias allowed_tools accepts the same syntax and validation. Repeated declarations, including mixed spellings, refuse loading. --- name: setup description: Install hidapi for vibekeys-plugin allowed-tools: - Bash(pip3 *) - Bash(pip *) - Bash(python3 -c *) --- Use a YAML block list, an inline list ( allowed-tools: [Bash, read_file] ), or a space/comma-separated scalar ( allowed-tools: Bash(pip3 *) read_file ). Spaces inside patterns are preserved. Names and patterns use the static permissions matcher, including aliases such as Bash / bash and Read / read_file . Malformed declarations refuse loading rather than widening the grant. Slash commands, the $ menu, /skills and successful use_skill calls share this behavior. Grants belong only to the calling agent and expire on its next user input (including steering), turn completion or cancellation. Session switching, runtime rebuilding and history replay do not restore grants. Global/project deny rules remain authoritative, and sensitive-path, credential and plan-mode boundaries still apply. AtomCode additionally keeps normal approval for destructive shell commands: a skill cannot preauthorize them. This is a product safety restriction on top of Claude Code compatible preauthorization; explicit static allow rules retain their existing behavior. Bash preauthorization is not a sandbox. Shell commands may read/write files and access the network. Plugin hooks and shell snippets executed while expanding a skill are separate execution paths, outside this model-tool preauthorization."],["skill-directories","Skill directories","AtomCode loads skills from a few well-known locations: Global : ~/.atomcode/skills/ Project-level : .atomcode/skills/ at the current working directory or any ancestor (if present) Project-level skills override same-named globals, so you can define the same name with different flows per project."],["invocation","Invocation",""],["via-slash-command","Via slash command","Every successfully loaded skill appears in the slash-command completion menu: > /release > /write-changelog > /debug-flaky-test"],["via-the-menu","Via the $ menu","Type a $ at the start of the input box to pop up a skills menu (the same set of invocable skills that /skills lists); keep typing to filter, press Tab to complete the highlighted name, and submit $<name> [args] to invoke that skill. It's a parallel entry point to slash commands: / drives slash-command completion, while $ is dedicated to picking a skill and can carry arguments inline, e.g. $brainstorming help me design login . In v5.0.3, /skills can match several skill names or fragments in one request and echoes the skills that were actually loaded. Newly installed skills are refreshed automatically, so a restart is normally unnecessary."],["model-driven-invocation","Model-driven invocation","The model can call the use_skill tool itself to run a relevant skill as a sub-flow. If you say \"publish a new version\", the model may pick this skill on its own without you typing /release ."],["tips-for-writing-a-good-skill","Tips for writing a good skill","Be specific in the description — it's the menu's blurb, and the main signal the model uses to decide whether this skill applies. Order matters — the model reads top-to-bottom; put strong dependencies up front. Make branches explicit — \"if build fails …; otherwise …\" is far more reliable than letting the model guess. List red lines — put hard rules in a dedicated \"Rules\" section to maximise compliance. Use sub-docs when needed — park long references in references/*.md and leave a one-liner like \"see … if needed\" in SKILL.md ."],["与项目指令的分工","Versus project instructions","Scenario Where it belongs Always-on project conventions (tech stack, code style, commands) .atomcode.md A specific workflow that needs to be triggered explicitly Skill A one-off ad-hoc requirement Just write it in the prompt"],["next-steps","Next steps","Basic Usage — back to everyday workflows FAQ — why isn't my skill showing up in the menu?"]],"x":"Skills A skill is a user-defined, reusable command — basically a chunk of markdown with frontmatter telling the AI \"here's how to handle this kind of task\". Once you've written one, it shows up alongside the built-in slash commands in the menu, or can be invoked on-demand by the use_skill tool."},{"s":"mcp","t":"MCP Integration","y":"Mc","h":[["session-pause","Pause all MCP servers for this session","Choose “Pause all” at the top of /mcp , or press Ctrl+S in its list view. The WebUI MCP menu offers the same control. Pausing removes MCP tools from the model and releases connections. Resume reconnects according to each server’s existing configuration, leaving individually disabled servers off and configuration files unchanged. Finish the current task and goal/loop, collect background jobs, and stop delegated agents first. The pause survives model changes and configuration reloads in the same session. Starting or reopening a session, or changing directory, resets it; it is not a persistent setting."],["what-it-enables","What it enables","Operate GitHub, GitLab, Jira, and other external services via official MCP servers Connect to Postgres / MySQL / DuckDB and other databases Use community servers for the filesystem, Playwright browser, Slack messages, and more Expose your team's domain-specific tools to the model without modifying atomcode source"],["two-config-locations","Two config locations","Path Scope <project-root>/.mcp.json Current project only — good for living next to the code ~/.atomcode/mcp.json User global, shared across every project Both can coexist; same-named servers prefer the project-level entry (it overrides the user-level one). The repo's .mcp.json.example ships heavily-commented stdio + HTTP templates — start from there."],["config-schema","Config schema","The top-level key is fixed at mcpServers (the legacy servers key still works). Each server should pick one transport: stdio : command (required) + optional args , env , timeout_ms , disabled HTTP : url (required) + optional headers , auth , timeout_ms , disabled If a server has both command and url , the current implementation treats it as stdio ( command ). To avoid ambiguity, don't write both. Strings support ${VAR} and ${VAR:-default} environment expansion; never hard-code sensitive tokens — keep them in env vars. disabled: true temporarily turns off a server without removing the entry. .mcp.json also accepts JSONC comments — // line comments and /* */ block comments — so you can annotate a server or comment one out without deleting it. Comment tokens inside string values (e.g. the // in a URL) are preserved."],["required-experimental-capabilities","Required experimental capabilities (optional)","Inside a server entry, requiredExperimentalCapabilities maps documented backend capability names to exact positive integer versions. For example: \"requiredExperimentalCapabilities\": { \"vendor/feature\": 1 } Use only a capability and version the backend actually documents. AtomCode checks every MCP initialization, including stdio recovery, before making the connection available. Missing, malformed or different versions fail closed. For constrained HTTP sessions, an unexpected session ID change requires reconnecting. Omit this field for existing behavior. Version checks do not activate a feature or negotiate its client protocol. They grant no tool permissions and do not prove that an external backend correctly implements its advertised policy."],["stdio-example-local-subprocess","stdio example (local subprocess)","{ \"mcpServers\": { \"filesystem\": { \"command\": \"npx\", \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem\", \"/tmp\"], \"timeout_ms\": 10000 } } }"],["http-example-remote-endpoint","HTTP example (remote endpoint)","{ \"mcpServers\": { \"github\": { \"url\": \"https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/\", \"headers\": { \"Authorization\": \"Bearer ${GITHUB_TOKEN}\" }, \"timeout_ms\": 30000 } } }"],["github-remote-mcp-oauth","GitHub remote MCP + OAuth","{ \"mcpServers\": { \"github\": { \"url\": \"https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/\", \"auth\": { \"type\": \"oauth\", \"provider\": \"github\" } } } } Before first use, you need AtomCode's own GitHub OAuth App client id, then run: atomcode mcp add-github-oauth --global ATOMCODE_GITHUB_MCP_CLIENT_ID=<client_id> atomcode mcp login github atomcode Inside the TUI you can also set the env var and run /mcp login github ; after a successful login, /mcp reload reconnects."],["one-line-server-add","One-line server add","atomcode mcp add writes the stdio config to JSON for you — no hand-editing required: # Write to project-root .mcp.json (current directory by default) atomcode mcp add playwright npx @playwright/mcp@latest # Write to user-global ~/.atomcode/mcp.json atomcode mcp add playwright npx @playwright/mcp@latest --global # Pin a specific project directory atomcode mcp add playwright npx @playwright/mcp@latest -C /path/to/repo The first positional is the server key name (which will appear in tool names); the rest is the executable + args. For GitHub remote MCP OAuth there's a dedicated entry: atomcode mcp add-github-oauth --global ATOMCODE_GITHUB_MCP_CLIENT_ID=<client_id> atomcode mcp login github Note A same-named server is fully overwritten . The GitHub OAuth token is stored at ~/.atomcode/mcp_auth.toml — it is not written to .mcp.json ."],["what-happens-at-startup","What happens at startup","Mode Connection behaviour When tools appear TUI Connects in parallel in the background — doesn't block the UI Each server registers as it connects, possibly slightly after the first frame One-shot ( -p ) Connects synchronously at launch; waits for enabled servers' connection attempts to finish MCP only mounts once at least one batch of tools is available In the TUI you'll see ✓ MCP server 'github' connected or ✗ MCP server '…' failed: … in the session area. A single server failure does not break other servers or the main program."],["image-results","Image results","Inline MCP image blocks enter the existing tool-image pipeline alongside text, for models that support vision. PNG, JPEG, GIF and WebP are supported. Original bytes and dimensions are preserved; screenshots are not silently resized. A result with isError: true retains both its error flag and valid screenshots. Base64, declared MIME type, actual encoding and pixel data are validated. Limits are 4 MiB of Base64 per image, four images and 8 MiB of Base64 per result, 8192 pixels per edge and 16 million pixels per image. The request-level image budget can further omit historical images. Invalid or oversized output retains text and returns an explicit tool error, with no partial screenshot set or automatic re-execution. Ask the server to capture a smaller region when needed. This does not install a desktop executor, grant operating-system permissions or change the selected model. Text-only models do not gain vision. Image resource links are not fetched automatically, and embedded resource blobs are not treated as screenshots."],["browser-use","Isolated browser workflow","The optional browser integration uses an external Playwright MCP backend. AtomCode bundles neither Node nor a browser and does not download them on startup. Install Node 20+ and Chrome explicitly. Only macOS has local acceptance evidence so far; Windows and Linux require their own acceptance before being called verified. # Explicit external installation; choose a directory outside the repository npm install --prefix /absolute/path/browser-backend @playwright/mcp@0.0.85 atomcode browser doctor --server /absolute/path/browser-backend/node_modules/@playwright/mcp/cli.js atomcode browser enable --server /absolute/path/browser-backend/node_modules/@playwright/mcp/cli.js atomcode On Windows, use an absolute Windows path for --server ; --node can select an installed Node executable. Stock setup checks versions only: it does not launch Chrome or prove that browser binaries are installed. An unavailable browser is an explicit runtime error; AtomCode does not install it automatically. /browser status /browser doctor /browser reload Open the local test page, fill the authorized form and verify the result. /browser disable /browser reload The first setup requires a terminal server path. Once configured, /browser enable reuses it. Configuration changes need an explicit reload or restart. status reads saved configuration; use /mcp for live connections, project overrides and pause/resume. Custom same-name configuration and edited skills are preserved rather than overwritten. The managed backend uses an isolated profile and disables page-provided WebMCP. It does not attach your personal Chrome profile or import cookies. Native MCP approvals remain in place ( trust: false , empty autoApprove ); read-only annotations and tool-wide Always grants still apply. These approvals are not site-scoped access control . The stock backend has no enforced origin allowlist; the optional origin-scope backend below supplies an explicit execution boundary. The browser runs on the MCP host, which may differ from your client computer. The managed allowedTools list exposes reviewed navigation, observation, form, interaction and close tools. Code evaluation, unsafe scripts, file upload and browser-install tools are excluded. Generic MCP configurations may also use allowedTools with exact raw tool names: omitted permits all, an empty array permits none. This filter is checked for discovery, cached tools and execution; it grants no approval and is not an operating-system or network sandbox. Generated snapshots and screenshots are stored under <user tree>/integrations/browser-use/artifacts , outside the project. Setup restricts that directory to the owner on Unix; Windows inherits directory ACLs. The backend receives a 16 MiB output eviction target, not a hard disk quota. Disabling preserves these files; remove them yourself when no longer needed. After one-time setup and reload, describe a webpage task to automatically load browser guidance and let the model use connected tools; no per-task slash command is required. Explicit $browser-use remains available. [no-auto-skills] , auto-load: off and disabled host auto-loading remain respected; paused MCP connections are not resumed implicitly. Screenshots require a vision-capable model, while structured page snapshots can support text-only models. Cancellation and disabling configuration cannot undo dispatched external actions. Re-observe unknown outcomes before retrying; close only browser resources owned by your workflow."],["browser-origin-scope","Exact-origin scope (optional backend)","First setup requires an explicitly installed origin-scope backend.cjs and the pinned package directory; nothing is downloaded or copied automatically. This backend checks actual HTTP(S)/WS(S) destinations, including redirects, frames and subresources, rather than relying on Playwright's convenience allowed-origins flag. atomcode browser enable --origin-backend /absolute/path/to/backend.cjs \\ --backend-root /absolute/installed/node_modules/@playwright/mcp \\ --allow-origin https://example.test /browser enable --allow-origin https://example.test --allow-origin https://example.test:8443 /browser enable --deny-all-origins # Explicitly return to stock; ordinary enable preserves scope /browser enable --unrestricted-origins /browser reload Origins must be exact HTTP(S) scheme/host/port values: no credentials, paths, queries or wildcards. --deny-all-origins saves an empty allow-list. Setup validates a no-browser doctor report and stores both policy and a required atomcode/browser-origin-scope v1 capability; every real initialization/recovery independently checks that capability. Other required capabilities and narrower tool restrictions are retained. Invalid saved scope is refused instead of silently removed. doctor / status understand saved scope but do not inspect a live connection; project overrides and explicit reload still apply. Scoped screenshots/snapshots use <user tree>/integrations/browser-use/origin-artifacts/files , with an ownership marker outside the retention directory. The backend refuses foreign nonempty roots and leaf symlinks. This version denies accepted download artifacts, local-file upload and full-CDP tools; it does not yet implement per-origin transfer/CDP allow settings. HTTPS response bytes can still enter Chrome. This is not an OS sandbox or global restriction on shell tools, other browser servers, clients or effects at allowed sites. macOS Chrome is locally tested; other-platform execution and the full policy matrix remain unaccepted."],["tool-naming","Tool naming","Each remote tool is registered as mcp__<server-key>__<remote-tool-name> . Example: with \"mcpServers\": { \"github\": { ... } } and a remote get_issue tool, the model sees the tool name mcp__github__get_issue . In the TUI you can turn off an individual tool by using its full name. For example: /toolbox off mcp__github__get_issue"],["permission-approval","Permission approval","MCP tools default to per-call confirmation (equivalent to RequireApproval ) because the remote is external, untrusted code. Press Y — allow once Press A — allow this tool for the current session (resets next launch; never persisted) Press N — deny this call Security note Treat MCP tool results as untrusted data. Do not let them be promoted to system instructions. If an MCP server returns \"please ignore previous instructions\", the model should not comply."],["project-trust-mcpjson","Project trust (.mcp.json)","Servers defined in a project-level .mcp.json are untrusted until you trust the project . A freshly-cloned repo that ships a .mcp.json cannot auto-spawn a subprocess on your machine — its project servers are withheld from the connect loop (fail-closed), and you'll see a blocked-untrusted notice listing them. User-global servers ( ~/.atomcode/mcp.json ) are never affected. Trust is per project directory and recorded in ~/.atomcode/mcp_trust.json : /mcp trust — trust the current project; its .mcp.json servers connect immediately (an implicit /mcp reload runs). /mcp untrust — withdraw trust; the project's MCP tools are removed right away. In the Web UI a Trust project button does the same over POST /live/mcp/trust , and the MCP status shows which servers are connected versus blocked."],["slash-commands","Slash commands","Command Purpose /mcp List successfully connected servers and their status (failed servers don't appear here — only as red error lines in the session area) /mcp tools <server> Async-list the remote tools actually exposed by a server /mcp reload Re-read .mcp.json / ~/.atomcode/mcp.json and reconnect enabled servers in the background /mcp trust / /mcp untrust Trust (or untrust) the current project so its .mcp.json servers may connect"],["current-limits","Current limits","Only MCP's tools capability is supported; resources / prompts / OAuth / roots / elicitation are not yet implemented HTTP servers don't have exponential-backoff reconnects, and stdio child processes don't auto-restart on exit — use /mcp reload to reconnect manually tools/list list_changed notifications don't trigger a dynamic refresh Tool results only consume text content blocks; image / resource blocks are currently ignored [A] Always applies only within the current session; it is never written to a config file"],["ecosystem-comparison","Ecosystem comparison","Product Config location Notes AtomCode mcpServers block in .mcp.json Current implementation is tools-only Claude Code .mcp.json More complete OAuth / resources / prompts support Cursor .mcp.json Common command / url configs usually reusable Codex CLI add OpenAI ecosystem If you already use Cursor's MCP setup, common command / url configs are usually reusable; anything outside AtomCode's current fields or capabilities needs verification."],["next-steps","Next steps","The .mcp.json.example at the repo root — heavily-commented stdio + HTTP templates Configuration — overall config overview Slash Commands — full command list including the /mcp family"]],"x":"MCP Integration MCP (Model Context Protocol) is an open protocol that plugs the \"tools\" exposed by external programs or HTTP services into AtomCode, so the model can call them like built-in tools. Since v4.20.4, AtomCode ships a built-in MCP client and re-uses the same mcpServers configuration block as Cursor and others."},{"s":"plugins","t":"Plugin System","y":"Pl","h":[["core-concepts","Core concepts","Marketplace — a git repository whose root contains .atomcode-plugin/marketplace.json or .claude-plugin/marketplace.json , declaring the plugins it provides. Plugin — an entry in a marketplace. It can be a subdirectory of the same repo, or it can point to an external git repository ( url / github / git ) or a local path ( local ). Skill / Command / Hook — the three asset types a plugin contributes. Skills and commands are namespaced with plugin-name: (to avoid collisions); hooks fire on events."],["command-reference","Command reference","Command Purpose /plugin Open the interactive plugin manager (↑/↓ to select, Enter to confirm, Esc to go back). Browse marketplaces, install/uninstall plugins, add/remove marketplaces — all from one screen /plugin marketplace add <url> Clone a git repo and register it as a marketplace /plugin marketplace remove <name> Remove a registered marketplace (refuses if any of its plugins are still installed) /plugin marketplace update <name> Pull the latest commit for a marketplace repo, refreshing its plugin list /plugin marketplace list List all registered marketplaces /plugin install <plugin>@<marketplace> Install a plugin from the named marketplace /plugin uninstall <plugin>@<marketplace> Uninstall an installed plugin (the marketplace registration is kept) /plugin list List all locally installed plugins /plugin reload Reload all plugins (re-scan disk, refresh skill/hook registration)"],["install-a-plugin","Install a plugin",""],["method-1-interactive-manager-recommended","Method 1: interactive manager (recommended)","Type /plugin in the TUI (no subcommand) to open a full-screen interactive manager. Navigate with arrow keys, confirm with Enter: /plugin # → Opens the manager home screen: # Browse & install — Browse a marketplace's plugins, Enter to install/uninstall # Add marketplace… — Type/paste a git URL to add a new marketplace # Remove marketplace… — Pick a marketplace to remove # Installed (N) — View installed plugins, Enter to uninstall Installed plugins show a ✓ mark; pressing Enter toggles install/uninstall. Cloning and installing are async — a status line appears at the bottom during the operation and the list refreshes automatically when done."],["method-2-slash-command-subcommands","Method 2: slash-command subcommands","# 1. Register the marketplace (clones its git repo locally) /plugin marketplace add https://gitcode.com/gmq123/ascend-model-agent-plugin # 2. Install one of its plugins /plugin install ascend-model-agent-plugin@ascend-model-agent-plugin # 3. List installed plugins /plugin list"],["method-3-cli","Method 3: CLI","atomcode plugin marketplace add <git-url> atomcode plugin install <plugin>@<marketplace> atomcode plugin list atomcode plugin uninstall <plugin>@<marketplace> atomcode plugin marketplace remove|update|list The CLI and TUI share the ~/.atomcode/plugins/ directory; anything installed on one side is visible on the other immediately."],["after-install","After install","Skills contributed by the plugin appear in the / menu with a <plugin-name>: prefix, e.g. /ascend-model-agent-plugin:ascend-model-verification . The model can also invoke these skills through the UseSkill tool. Hooks require explicit trust before they activate — run atomcode plugin trust <name> after reviewing the printed notice; hooks load on the next session. See Hook trust flow below."],["directory-layout","Directory layout","~/.atomcode/plugins/ ├── marketplaces.json # Registered marketplace metadata ├── installed_plugins.json # Status records for installed plugins ├── marketplaces/ │ └── <marketplace-name>/ # The marketplace repository clone │ ├── .claude-plugin/marketplace.json │ └── <plugin-subdir>/ # Inline plugin └── installed/ └── <marketplace>/<plugin>/ # Clones of plugins from external sources"],["pluginjson-shape","plugin.json shape","The plugin.json in each plugin's root (or its .claude-plugin/ / .atomcode-plugin/ subdirectory): { \"name\": \"my-plugin\", \"version\": \"1.0.0\", \"description\": \"What it does\", \"skills\": [\"./skills\"], // Also accepts the string \"skills\" \"commands\": [\"./commands\"], \"hooks\": { // Also accepts a path string \"hooks.json\" \"UserPromptSubmit\": [{ \"hooks\": [{ \"type\": \"command\", \"command\": \"python \\\"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hook.py\\\"\", \"timeout\": 5 }] }] } }"],["hook-events","Hook events","Plugins can hook the following events (matching CC). Event names are case/style-insensitive — the loader accepts both PascalCase ( PreToolUse , SessionStart ) and snake_case ( pre_tool_use , session_start ); the two spellings are equivalent. Event When it fires Typical use UserPromptSubmit After the user submits a message, before the LLM call Inject additional context / route / block PreToolUse Before a tool call Validation, blocking, argument rewriting PostToolUse After a tool call Audit, side effects SessionStart Session startup Warm-up, logging SessionEnd Session end Cleanup, archiving Stop Turn ended — normal stop, safety fuse, user cancel, or rate-limit pause Notify the plugin the turn has ended; trigger follow-up actions StopFailure Turn ended because of an API/provider error (stream failure / timeout) Notify the plugin the turn failed; alert / log Notification System notification Forward to external alert channels Every turn end fires exactly one of Stop / StopFailure — never both, never none. StopFailure is reserved for turns that ended because of an API/provider failure; a tool error mid-turn does not fire it (the turn continues and ends with its real terminal instead). The stdin payload carries hook_event_name , session_id , cwd , the session's transcript_path (the append-only JSONL transcript, null for non-persistent runs), a CC-style stop_hook_active flag (true when another terminal hook is configured and fires alongside — use it to avoid a Stop hook recursively re-triggering itself), and a kernel stop_reason (e.g. Stopped , ProviderError , Timeout , Cancelled ) so a hook can refine the outcome without parsing anything else."],["default-directory-auto-discovery","Default-directory auto-discovery","A plugin's assets are discovered from default directories automatically — no need to declare them in plugin.json : Hooks — loaded from hooks/hooks.json first (CC layout), falling back to a root-level hooks.json . Skills — auto-scanned from the skills/ directory. Commands — auto-scanned from the commands/ directory. Only when your layout deviates from these defaults (e.g. a custom subdirectory name) do you need explicit \"skills\" / \"commands\" / \"hooks\" fields in plugin.json ."],["hook-trust-flow","Hook trust flow","To prevent a malicious plugin from silently running arbitrary commands, plugin hooks are protected by a trust gate: On install ( /plugin install / atomcode plugin install ) — AtomCode prints a notice of the hook commands found. Hooks are not run yet . Grant trust — after reviewing the notice, run: atomcode plugin trust <plugin-name> AtomCode records a hash of the current hook command set. Takes effect next session — trusted hooks are loaded and activated on the next startup. Re-trust after updates — if a plugin update changes its hook commands, the stored hash is invalidated automatically; run trust again to approve the new version. To revoke trust: atomcode plugin untrust <plugin-name>"],["userpromptsubmit-io-protocol","UserPromptSubmit IO protocol","The hook receives JSON on stdin and decides what to do via stdout: { \"session_id\": \"...\", \"hook_event_name\": \"UserPromptSubmit\", \"prompt\": \"the user's input text\", \"cwd\": \"/working/directory\" } The hook can respond in the following ways (highest priority first): Exit 2 with a deliberate block reason — blocks the prompt; other nonzero exits and launch failures are not business block decisions. JSON on stdout {\"decision\": \"block\", \"reason\": \"...\"} — block with an explicit reason. JSON on stdout {\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"additionalContext\": \"...\"}} — append additionalContext to the user message as extra LLM context. Plain text on stdout — the whole block is injected as additionalContext . Empty stdout / unparseable JSON — passthrough; the prompt reaches the LLM unchanged. When parsing stdout, AtomCode first tries the last non-empty line as JSON; on failure it falls back to whole-text injection — so a hook script can print debug output earlier without affecting the final decision."],["path-variables","Path variables","Hook command strings can reference these environment variables (injected by the executor): ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} — absolute path of the plugin install directory (CC compatible). ${ATOMCODE_PLUGIN_ROOT} — same thing, atomcode alias. Plugin hooks accept checked plugin-relative scripts and literal arguments, optionally using python, python3, node, sh or bash. Plugin-root placeholders resolve as paths without a shell. Move pipelines, redirections and inline code into scripts. Known Node path wrappers normalize to scripts; recognized batch/bash polyglot .cmd wrappers run through bash. Ordinary .cmd/.bat files remain unsupported. Only user-authored hooks retain shell expansion. Trust includes plugin contents (excluding Git metadata). Script/helper changes require explicit atomcode plugin trust name . Incompatible configurations are withheld at load with a diagnostic; repair the entry point or disable the plugin. This is not a sandbox, does not cover external dependencies/environment, and does not guarantee atomic execution against concurrent file mutation."],["marketplace-management","Marketplace management","# List registered marketplaces /plugin marketplace list # Pull the latest commit (refreshes the plugin list this marketplace exposes) /plugin marketplace update <name> # Remove (refuses if any plugin from this marketplace is still installed) /plugin marketplace remove <name>"],["walkthrough-installing-the-ascend-plugin","Walkthrough: installing the Ascend plugin","/plugin marketplace add https://gitcode.com/gmq123/ascend-model-agent-plugin # > cloning marketplace from https://gitcode.com/... # > marketplace `ascend-model-agent-plugin` added at 7a59537 (1 plugins) /plugin install ascend-model-agent-plugin@ascend-model-agent-plugin # > installing `...`... # > installed `ascend-model-agent-plugin@ascend-model-agent-plugin` — 23 skills loaded, 5 skipped # This plugin installs a UserPromptSubmit hook (workflow_planner_hook.py). # When you say \"help me verify Qwen3 adaptation on Ascend\", it injects a # workflow JSON and routes the model through the ascend-model-verification # skill pipeline. help me verify Qwen3 adaptation on Ascend"],["known-limits","Known limits","Unsupported CC events : PreCompact / SubagentStop are silently skipped. Multi-line indented JSON output : when a hook prints with print(json.dumps(..., indent=2)) , the last line is } , which our last-line JSON parser fails on — falling back to plain-text injection. Functionally it still works (the LLM still reads the content) but it's not on the structured path. Hook authors should use single-line json.dumps(...) output. Strict skill-name validation : [a-z0-9_-] , matching CC. Skill names with / or mixed case are skipped."],["next-steps","Next steps","Skills — write your own skills; they work inside plugins too. Slash Commands — full /plugin command list. MCP Integration — another path for connecting external tools; complementary to plugins."]],"x":"Plugin System A plugin is a bundle of skills / commands / hooks distributed over a git repository. One /plugin install drops someone else's workflow into AtomCode and you can use it immediately. AtomCode's plugin protocol is compatible with Claude Code — CC-ecosystem plugin repos install and run out of the box. To install from your shell, use atomcode plugin install <plugin>@<marketplace> with the name published in the marketplace manifest. A bare plugin name must match exactly one entry across registered marketplaces."},{"s":"memory","t":"Persistent Memory","y":"Me","h":[["command-overview","Command overview","Command Effect /remember <content> Record an entry in project memory (default scope, bound to the current working directory) /remember --global <content> Record an entry in global memory (shared across all projects) /forget <keyword> Delete every entry in global + project memory matching the keyword (case-insensitive); the output lists what got removed /memory Show all active memory entries, grouped under [Global] / [Project] , with disk paths"],["storage-locations","Storage locations","Scope Path Global ~/.atomcode/memory.md (or $ATOMCODE_HOME/memory.md ) Project <project_root>/.atomcode/memory.md The format is plain Markdown — one entry per - -prefixed list item. Use /remember or hand-edit; AtomCode rereads on the next turn. Lines not starting with - are ignored , so feel free to add comments, blank lines, or grouping headings without affecting entries."],["how-the-model-uses-memory","How the model \"uses\" memory","At session start, AtomCode merges global + project memory through the coding runtime memory hook ( crates/atomcode-coding/src/parts.rs ), formatted as: === MEMORY === The user has asked you to remember these facts and preferences: [Global] - Prefers concise answers, no long-winded explanations - Reply in Chinese, but write commit messages in English [Project: atomcode] - Test command is cargo test --workspace --no-fail-fast - When CI fails, first check .github/workflows/ci.yml lines 78-92 The model sees this block on every turn. There is no \"semantic retrieval\" or \"on-demand recall\" — it's unconditional full injection. The more entries, the more tokens per turn. Prune stale entries to keep this tight."],["capacity-limits","Capacity limits","Limit Value What happens at the limit Single memory file size 64 KB Only the trailing 64 KB is read (aligned to line boundaries — UTF-8 characters are never split) Total characters in the injected prompt 4000 chars Truncated with a trailing [...truncated, run /memory to review] note Once you hit the limit, use /forget to clean up — drop entries that are no longer relevant."],["suggested-uses","Suggested uses",""],["1-project-specific-commands-conventions-footguns-project-sco","1. Project-specific commands, conventions, footguns (project scope)","> /remember use npm run check for type-checking (not npm run typecheck) > /remember when CI fails, check .github/workflows/ci.yml lines 78-92 first > /remember never use sed -i in this repo (macOS/Linux behaviour differs) > /remember DB migration SQL must run on staging before main"],["2-global-coding-preferences-workflows-global","2. Global coding preferences, workflows (global)","> /remember --global run tests before committing > /remember --global don't git push on your own — let me confirm manually > /remember --global reply in Chinese but write commit messages in English > /remember --global prefer editing existing files — don't create docs (*.md) on your own"],["3-personal-or-team-info-global","3. Personal or team info (global)","> /remember --global my GitHub username is alice > /remember --global default timezone Asia/Shanghai > /remember --global team standup is Mon/Wed/Fri at 9:30"],["4-cleaning-up-stale-memories","4. Cleaning up stale memories","> /forget npm run check [project] - use npm run check for type-checking (not npm run typecheck) (removed 1 matching entry) > /memory [Global] (/Users/alice/.atomcode/memory.md) - run tests before committing - don't git push on your own — let me confirm manually [Project] (/Users/alice/code/myrepo/.atomcode/memory.md) - when CI fails, check .github/workflows/ci.yml lines 78-92 first"],["memory-vs-project-instructions-vs-session-history","Memory vs project instructions vs session history","AtomCode offers three ways to persist \"context\", each with a different role: .atomcode.md Memory (memory.md) Sessions ( /resume ) Best for Full specs, tech stack, detailed conventions Stray facts, personal preferences, command cheats Past conversation + tool calls Scope Project Project + global One specific session How to add Hand-edit /remember or hand-edit Auto-saved per conversation Injection Loaded into system prompt at startup Injected into system prompt every turn Restored wholesale via /resume Token cost High (full doc) Capped at 4000 chars Bounded by the context window Typical combinations: Team conventions in .atomcode.md (commit it; shared by everyone) Personal preferences via /remember --global (only on your machine) Project-specific footguns via /remember (lives in the project's local .atomcode/memory.md ; commit or gitignore your call) Whether to commit .atomcode/memory.md : if the team also uses AtomCode and the memory is project knowledge (footguns, conventions), commit it; if it's personal notes, add it to .gitignore ."],["next-steps","Next steps","Project Instructions — the best home for full specs Slash Commands — full command reference Sessions & Undo — the details of /resume"]],"x":"Persistent Memory Use /remember to capture stray preferences, conventions, and commands. AtomCode injects them into the system prompt on every turn. It complements .atomcode.md project instructions : instructions are for full specs; memory is for the \"oh, I should tell it about that\" facts."},{"s":"project-instructions","t":"Project Instructions","y":"Pi","h":[["why-bother","Why bother","A typical scenario: your team uses the Composition API exclusively — Options API is banned. Every time you ask AtomCode to write a new component, you have to remind it. With .atomcode.md , that preference rides along on every conversation automatically."],["file-location","File location","Default path: .atomcode.md at the project root AtomCode walks upwards from the current working directory until it finds the file, or hits $HOME If the file doesn't exist, no related content appears in the system prompt"],["example","Example","# Project Instructions This is a Vue 3 + TypeScript project using Pinia for state, Tailwind for styles, and Vitest for unit tests. ## Conventions - Components must use `<script setup lang=\"ts\">` Composition API - Only Tailwind for styling — no inline style attributes, no standalone .css files - All API calls go through `src/services/*`; never fetch directly in components - State lives in Pinia stores — components keep no derived global state ## Commands - Dev: `pnpm dev` - Typecheck: `pnpm typecheck` - Tests: `pnpm test` - Build: `pnpm build` ## Notes - Do not modify `src/generated/*` — it's auto-generated from OpenAPI - Test coverage must stay above 80%; new modules must ship with unit tests"],["tips-for-writing-atomcodemd","Tips for writing .atomcode.md","Only write what's different from the norm — the model already knows generic best practices; don't repeat them here. Prefer commands over descriptions — \"run tests with pnpm test \", not \"please run the unit tests\". Use imperatives — \"Use X\", \"Don't Y\" — avoid hedge words like \"suggest\", \"if possible\". List forbidden zones — call out files / directories that must not be touched. The model is highly compliant. Keep it short — every line costs tokens; 30-80 lines is usually plenty. Tip If you have repetitive workflows (e.g. the same set of commands every bug fix), don't bloat .atomcode.md — write a Skill instead. It's clearer and more reusable."],["relationship-to-agentsmd-claudemd-geminimd","Relationship to AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md / GEMINI.md","AtomCode natively supports AGENTS.md , the open standard for AI coding agent context. If you have a project that already uses AGENTS.md , AtomCode will pick it up automatically — no extra setup needed. The lookup order is: .atomcode.md ATOMCODE.md AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md / claude.md First match wins. If you also use Claude Code or Gemini CLI in the same project, they each have their own instruction files: AtomCode → .atomcode.md or AGENTS.md Claude Code → CLAUDE.md Gemini CLI → GEMINI.md These don't conflict. By using AGENTS.md , you can share the same instruction file across multiple AI coding tools that follow the open standard."],["next-steps","Next steps","Skills — abstract reusable workflows into commands"]],"x":"Project Instructions Drop a .atomcode.md in your project root to pin tech-stack details, conventions, and preferences. AtomCode injects it into the system prompt at startup, so you don't have to repeat the rules every conversation."},{"s":"webui","t":"Web UI","y":"Wb","h":[["start-stop","Start & stop","Run these in the AtomCode TUI input box: # Launch the webui and open the browser (local server binds 127.0.0.1:13457; phones connect through the relay) /webui # Stop the webui server /webui stop On launch, AtomCode starts a local HTTP server and opens your browser to a URL like http://127.0.0.1:13457/?token=<one-time token> . The token in the URL is the credential — it's equivalent to a password , so don't share it. The current TUI session is also attached to live sync automatically (see Live sync across devices below). Phone access through the relay The local webui binds 127.0.0.1 and connects to the HTTPS relay at https://relay-atomcode.atomgit.com . Scan the QR in the terminal or Remote access dialog with your phone; no VPN is needed. Add --local for local-only access. See Remote Access ."],["two-ways-to-run","Two ways to run it, and when each stops","The webui server lives in the process that started it; when that process exits, the server stops: Started by Stops when Good for /webui inside AtomCode you run /webui stop , or that AtomCode exits using the terminal and the browser together, synced to one session atomcode webui in a terminal you press Ctrl+C there, or close that terminal window using only the browser, or the webui installed as a desktop app # Run the webui on its own, without any AtomCode terminal UI atomcode webui # Do not open a browser (scripts, desktop app); only print the link atomcode webui --no-open # Choose the port or the address to bind atomcode webui --port 13457 --host 127.0.0.1 Every start mints a new token and the old link stops working; open the link this start printed. That link works in any browser for as long as this run lasts. If the default port 13457 is taken (say a /webui is already running), the next free port is used — go by the printed link. With the webui installed as a desktop app (Chrome / Edge “Install app”), opening the app while nothing is running shows a page that says how to start it, instead of the browser's “can't reach this page”. Once started, open the newly printed link once."],["what-the-interface-offers","What the interface offers","The browser UI brings the terminal's capabilities into a graphical interface: Area What you can do Sidebar Session history grouped by project, search sessions, start a new chat, rename / delete sessions; collapses to an icon rail (a drawer on mobile). Model selector Switch provider / model right under the input box; same-named models are disambiguated with a provider tag. Model config Manage provider accounts and multiple models under each account, including protocol, base URL, API key, context window, and the default model. Settings Theme (light / dark), language (中 / EN), model config, and the remote-access entry. Image attachments Paste or pick images to send with a message (2 MB each); non-vision models fall back to VL; thumbnails show in history. Tool execution Tool calls show their arguments and output inline, expandable line by line, both live and in history. Attach menu (+) Upload an image, pick a file for context, or insert a Skill. Working directory Switch the working dir, browse folders, create a new folder, set a default working dir."],["workspace-actions","Manage the workspace list","The menu before the + button on each workspace offers Pin / Unpin workspace, Clear sessions and Remove workspace. Pinning and visibility are saved by the local server and survive refreshes and restarts. Remove workspace only hides its group. Project directories, code and session records are kept. History remains accessible through the Sessions view or search. Add the directory again to restore its group. Clear sessions requires confirmation and permanently deletes the workspace's listed session records, keeping the empty workspace and project files. Running sessions and sessions owned by another process are not forcibly deleted. If a deletion fails, the operation stops and shows the number already deleted; retry to clear the remaining sessions."],["live-sync","Live sync across devices","Behind the webui is a LiveSession : one session can be open in the terminal and multiple browser tabs at once, and every input, streamed AI reply, and tool result is broadcast live to all connected views — a viewer that joins late first receives a snapshot replay. When you run /webui , the current TUI session is attached automatically — messages you send in the terminal appear in the browser, and vice versa. In another TUI, run /sync to attach to the running webui session (a /webui must already be running). /sync off — leave sync and return to a standalone session. Sync mode supports /compact . Model changes follow runtime confirmation and are not applied halfway through an active turn. Uploaded images, the current working directory, and active sessions survive refreshes and view switches. This makes \"start in the terminal, watch progress on a phone / tablet\" — or several people watching the same agent session — possible."],["approval-modes","Approval modes","A pill in the bottom bar sets how the agent's actions are gated — the browser mirror of the terminal's approval modes. The default is Build . Mode Behaviour Build (default) Interactive — every file edit and command asks for approval before it runs. Accept Edits File edits are auto-approved; commands still ask. Plan Read-only exploration — write and execute tools are blocked so the agent proposes a plan first. Bypass (免审批) ⚠ Auto-approves everything, including edits and commands. Use with care. The mode is process-wide and broadcast over the live channel, so switching it in one tab updates every connected view. It is not written to your config — it resets to Build on restart. When the agent needs a decision from you mid-task, an interactive question card appears (single choice, multiple choice, or free text) and the turn pauses until you answer. See Interactive Questions for the full behaviour."],["remote-access","Remote access","Run /webui (or atomcode webui standalone), then scan the relay QR with your phone browser to open the same conversation. The devices may use different networks. See Remote Access ."],["next","Next","Remote Access — open the webui from your phone through the HTTPS relay Headless & Daemon — the daemon and HTTP/SSE API behind the webui Slash Commands — quick reference for /webui , /sync and more"]],"x":"Web UI Besides the terminal TUI, AtomCode ships a built-in browser interface : type /webui in the TUI to launch it, then chat, browse session history, add/edit/delete model providers, and upload images in the browser — and use /sync to mirror one session live between the terminal and the browser. It reuses this machine's login, models, and session history, so there's nothing extra to configure. First, install AtomCode on your computer. If building from source, follow the installation guide to build the WebUI frontend first. Keep the process that starts WebUI running while you use it. After context compaction, retained historical user messages are labeled as historical rather than new requests. Use “View full history” above the conversation to read original turns, reasoning and tool records without changing the current task or draft. Refreshing reloads the session view; /reload reloads configuration and does not compact context."},{"s":"webui-remote-access","t":"Remote Access","y":"Ra","h":[["connect","Connect","Keep AtomCode running and run /webui . It opens the local browser and prints a phone link and QR code. Scan with your phone browser, or copy the relay link from the WebUI Remote access dialog. The devices may use different networks. The phone and TUI share the same conversation. /webui stop , signing out in the terminal, or exiting AtomCode stops relay sharing. Standalone: atomcode webui . Local only: /webui --local or atomcode webui --local . Explicit /webui lan or --host <address> uses the local network instead of automatically connecting a relay."],["troubleshooting","Connection failures","Local access remains available if relay setup fails. The terminal and Remote access dialog explain the failure. If WebUI is unsupported, upgrade the relay server and install the matching WebUI assets, then retry /webui . Use ATOMCODE_APP_RELAY to select an existing compatible relay and ATOMCODE_ENABLE_RELAY=0 to disable relay access."],["relay-address","Relay address","The default HTTPS relay is https://relay-atomcode.atomgit.com ; no extra configuration is needed. On your phone, open the pairing link generated by AtomCode or scan its QR code."],["self-hosted-relay-requirements","Self-hosted relay requirements","The address override does not install a server. relay-client is not a relay server. The server is maintained in the separate atomcode-relay project; this guide provides neither server source nor a public download. Contact maintainers through a project Issue to confirm compatible server artifacts, supported platforms, and matching built WebUI assets. A public Docker image is not implied. After obtaining a compatible server, place it behind HTTPS with WebSocket upgrades and unbuffered SSE forwarding. For containers, listen on the container network and expose the port only to the reverse proxy; another container cannot reach its loopback address. Set ATOM_RELAY_ADMIN_SECRET , limit ATOM_RELAY_MAX_TUNNELS (for example, 10 for personal use) and ATOM_RELAY_MAX_CONCURRENT , and enforce registration rate and connection limits at the reverse proxy. Serve compatible built assets using ATOM_RELAY_WEBUI_DIR , or use ATOM_RELAY_WEBUI_BUNDLES_DIR with the supplied versioned bundle installation instructions. Before starting AtomCode, set ATOMCODE_APP_RELAY=https://relay.example.com and ATOMCODE_APP_RELAY_SECRET to match the server registration secret. Existing /app and /webui use the official relay-client; the server must implement its handshake and forwarding protocol. Check /health , registration, pairing, streaming, and reconnection separately. Registration secrets, route tokens, and WebUI access tokens are distinct credentials. Until server artifacts are available to you, keep using an existing SSH reverse tunnel or VPN. Operators manage their own TLS, access, bandwidth, and upgrades. Self-hosting does not provide model inference credits."],["security","Security and lifetime","The link grants access: keep it private. HTTPS protects transport; the local WebUI still checks its access token. The relay can process traffic; this is not end-to-end encryption. Pairing credentials survive reload in tab-scoped sessionStorage and are cleared when the tab closes. Network disconnects reconnect automatically. Access stops while the computer is asleep, offline, or AtomCode has exited."],["lan","Local network alternative","/webui lan remains available on the same Wi-Fi. /webui --host <virtual IP> also works with an existing VPN. These local HTTP connections require a trusted network."]],"x":"Remote access Run /webui and scan the relay QR code with your phone browser. No VPN or public listening port is needed. First, install AtomCode on your computer. Keep the process that starts WebUI running while you use it."},{"s":"faq","t":"FAQ","y":"Fq","h":[["install-launch","Install & launch",""],["the-install-script-fails-or-times-out","The install script fails or times out","The one-click installer pulls the binary from GitCode releases by default. If the network blocks it: Download the archive for your platform manually from the releases page and drop atomcode onto your PATH ; or build from source: cargo install --path crates/atomcode-cli --locked (requires Rust 1.88+)."],["running-atomcode-says-command-not-found","Running atomcode says \"command not found\"","The install directory isn't on your PATH . The default location is ~/.atomcode/bin — add it to your shell rc file: export PATH=\"$HOME/.atomcode/bin:$PATH\""],["macos-says-cannot-be-opened-because-the-developer-cannot-be-","macOS says \"cannot be opened because the developer cannot be verified\"","Either click \"Open Anyway\" under System Settings → Privacy & Security, or run: xattr -d com.apple.quarantine $(which atomcode)"],["login-models","Login & models",""],["the-browser-doesnt-open-during-oauth-login","The browser doesn't open during OAuth login","Check whether you're on a remote server without a desktop session. For remote environments, prefer API-key login (see Login Methods ), or finish OAuth locally and copy ~/.atomcode/auth.toml to the same path on the server."],["cant-reach-the-model-hangs-forever-timeouts","Can't reach the model / hangs forever / timeouts","First check that base_url in ~/.atomcode/config.toml is reachable — curl the matching /v1/models endpoint; On corporate networks it's usually a proxy issue — set HTTPS_PROXY and retry; On Windows, v5.0.7 uses the system SChannel certificate store by default, including enterprise roots. If it still fails, check the system certificate, proxy, and overrides such as SSL_CERT_FILE separately; If you're in mainland China hitting an overseas model, verify your egress network. You can run /model to switch to AtomGit's official channel first to prove the whole pipeline works."],["how-do-i-switch-models","How do I switch models?","Type /model and pick from the menu. The command switches the current session and saves the choice as the default for sessions opened later; other already-open sessions keep their current model. See Configuration ."],["context-overflow-context-length-exceeded","Context overflow / \"context length exceeded\"","Run /compact to have the model summarise the conversation so far and keep going; or /clear to wipe the current context and start over (history is kept as a session — you can /resume at any time); Avoid pasting a whole giant file into a prompt; let AtomCode use its file tools to read what it needs."],["permissions-safety","Permissions & safety",""],["confirming-every-command-gets-annoying","Confirming every command gets annoying","That's the default safety policy. You can: Allow ad-hoc: pick \"Always allow this kind of action\" in the confirmation prompt; Allow via config: add commands to the [permissions] allowlist in config.toml ."],["where-does-atomcode-send-my-code","Where does AtomCode send my code?","Only to the model endpoint you've configured in config.toml . Project files are read locally by tools and shipped as part of the prompt; AtomCode itself does not upload or telemeter code content."],["can-i-disable-specific-tools","Can I disable specific tools?","Yes — under [tools] in config.toml , set disabled = [\"shell\", \"web_fetch\"] to block tools you don't want the model to use."],["usage-interaction","Usage & interaction",""],["how-do-i-point-it-at-a-specific-file","How do I point it at a specific file?","Type @ in the input to trigger file completion, e.g. walk me through @src/main.rs entry logic . You can also just describe the path and the tool will call read_file on its own."],["how-do-i-enter-a-multiline-prompt","How do I enter a multiline prompt?","Shift + Enter , Alt + Enter , or Ctrl + Enter insert a newline; Enter sends. Full reference at Keybindings ."],["how-do-i-roll-back-a-bad-edit","How do I roll back a bad edit?","Run /undo to revert the file changes produced by the last tool turn. See Sessions & Undo ."],["can-i-resume-the-previous-session","Can I resume the previous session?","Yes. Launch with --continue (or -c ) to pick up the last session, or run /resume from inside a new session and pick one from the history list."],["prompt-retention","Is the prompt sent at the start of a session retained?","During normal conversation and compaction, the currently active system prompt continues to be used, and the first real user message's text is protected from compaction. Later history and tool results may be summarized or shortened; persisted history is not necessarily sent in full with every request. Explicitly clearing, starting a new session or rolling back changes the effective history. Resuming restores saved effective history, but the system prompt is assembled using the current version, configuration and project instructions. It is not guaranteed to match the original prompt word for word. See system-prompt and original-task retention ."],["inspect-system-prompt","Where can I inspect the current system prompt?","In the TUI, use /context prompt for the currently assembled system prompt, or /context persona for the persona and append settings. Plain /context reports the context budget, not the prompt text. See the command reference ."],["skills-project-instructions","Skills & project instructions",""],["my-skill-doesnt-show-up-in-the-menu","My skill doesn't show up in the menu","Check the path: globally ~/.atomcode/skills/<name>/SKILL.md , per-project .atomcode/skills/<name>/SKILL.md ; Check the frontmatter: both name and description are required; Restart atomcode or run /reload to rescan."],["whats-the-difference-between-atomcodemd-and-a-skill","What's the difference between .atomcode.md and a skill?","The former is an \"always on\" project-level convention; the latter is an explicitly invoked workflow. See Skills · Versus project instructions ."],["troubleshooting","Troubleshooting","Logs first For any problem, step one is to look at ~/.atomcode/logs/ . Launching with --log-level debug prints far more detailed request/response logs."],["when-filing-an-issue-please-include","When filing an issue, please include","The output of atomcode --version ; Your OS and architecture; Minimal repro steps for the error; Relevant logs (redact your API key)."],["next-steps","Next steps","Back to overview Quickstart — install from scratch Configuration — every adjustable option"]],"x":"FAQ A roundup of questions that keep coming up in user channels and issues. If yours isn't here, ask AtomCode to create an Issue with its built-in AtomGit tool (after /login ), or open it on the AtomGit repository ."},{"s":"changelog","t":"Changelog","y":"Cl","h":[["v5.2.9","v5.2.9 2026-11-26","Overview This release is about teamwork, long-session stability and everyday controls. Team members can hand work over to each other under an explicit authorization instead of routing everything through the lead; members can opt into request budgets and task cost accounting. Sessions gain cross-project browsing and resume, previews and cleanup of old sessions, and a write guard — an existing file the session never touched is no longer overwritten. The review text from before a compaction can be expanded again. The terminal and the web page were reworked together: /provider is now a list → detail pair, and the WebUI Git panel follows the VSCode source-control layout with read-only access to team members' conversations. On the security side, failed local API authentication is rate-limited and token comparison is constant-time. On the performance side, streamed replies are appended in place and rendered incrementally, session history and event logs are read incrementally, and file-index filtering no longer lowercases every entry. Changes Authorized handovers between team members : Members can hand tasks and conclusions directly to each other under an authorization instead of routing everything through the lead. tell_parent requires the delivered content to actually reach the report, a read-only member is told at once how to deliver, a member that stops after a progress report wakes the lead, and a member reporting completion reminds the lead to check it before stopping it. Members can opt into request budgets and task cost accounting, roles can look up read-only MCP tools by duty and verify the results, and delivery checks distinguish members with and without a shell. Write guard for files : write_file no longer overwrites an existing file this session never touched. Loop detection counts per session, compaction and overflow guards compute the window from the current agent's model, repeated retries of malformed tool calls are bounded, long-thinking models lose fewer useless rounds and share one streaming timeout. Browse and resume sessions across projects : The TUI can browse and resume sessions across working directories and preview and clean up old sessions. /agents lists one-shot task sub-agents, with the header carrying a sub-agent label. Background tasks read the session event log incrementally, history loading is faster and merges session preview requests, and the session start notice is de-duplicated while the SSE stream is consumed. Review text from before a compaction : Recall can expand the review text from before a compaction; team member sessions can be compacted too, and a delegation kept after a member's compaction is marked as a historical message; compaction discloses the user requirements dropped in favor of an alternative. /provider is now a list → detail pair : Enter / Ctrl+E / Ctrl+D behave the same throughout, forms use fixed key meanings and drop ^o / ^f and the Key field; the detail page offers \"add and use\" when no model is available, and the qualification is single and can be explicitly withdrawn. WebUI source control follows VSCode : The Git panel follows the VSCode source-control layout, with the discard and commit scope, read-only rendering and empty-repository loading fixed; a session goal status bar with live timing was added, team members' conversations can be viewed read-only, the attachment menu is no longer cut off on small screens, and larger images can be pasted in live chat. Local API authentication hardened and rate-limited : Failed local API requests are rate-limited by count, valid tokens stay usable during a block, token comparison is constant-time, Windows sets and verifies a user-only ACL for credential files, and panic telemetry is scrubbed while WebUI SSE events are size-limited. Streamed replies append in place : The TUI no longer copies the whole reply for every delta — it appends in place and renders incrementally, and buffered deltas survive a view switch. Unchanged render rows are reused, but only after the amended text is checked; generation speed excludes burst frames so the number is no longer inflated. file-index filtering is faster : Filtering no longer lowercases every entry and keeps only the top 30 — the selection is bounded and totally ordered, non-ASCII needles reuse one lowercase buffer, ASCII needles skip folding, and candidate clones and comparisons are bounded. Terminal interaction fixes : The @ mention menu no longer pops up again after Esc, rejected tokens are identified by offset and text, the browse state keeps the rejection record, editing and cursor tracking are correct, a late receipt no longer closes the strength selector, Esc during a turn no longer discards the background-task completion notice, short screens no longer trade the command line for the panel's footer, narrow screens drop the timer before the badge state, the approval panel keeps a separating line between legend and status bar, and approvals on routes with no answer are hidden. The /goal badge shows its running time : It counts up while running and freezes when paused, using only its own samples. The status bar shows the current member's worktree branch, and the footer reminder is rechecked immediately after a quota recovery. Captured process output is bounded : Captured process output has a cap, truncated foreground output keeps its encoding, and the TUI live cache is capped as well. AI inline completion (ghost text) : The editor extension and the daemon side support AI inline completion, expired completion requests are cancelled and the originally inserted text is preserved. VS Code chat focus recovery : Alt+Tab back restores the chat input focus and intercepts a lone Alt, with the focus-recovery condition tightened. Session and runtime consistency : The running state is synchronized and history loading blocks less; repeated tool checks are fewer and tasks end in time; background reviews keep their single-execution limit, and the peak whole-document copy in long-session requests and subscription catch-up is reduced. Site and docs rework : The bilingual changelog is shown with unified branding, the footer wordmark becomes a permanently lit \"fluorescent horizon\"; the site and the docs pages were visually reworked, and the mobile installation experience improved with the docs calibrated. Related issues 本节收录 v5.2.9 里程碑 下的全部 issue，不区分状态与标签。此列表用于关联跟踪，不表示所有条目均已实现或完成发布验收。 #1819 Feature Request: Engineering Opportunity Reports for Recoverable Technical Limitations #1820 Code Review: host.rs (Host↔Runtime adapter) #1823 Team 模式下调用次数消耗过快：成员默认无轮次限制 + Hard 角色高消耗组合 #1824 历史记录 JSONL 无限增长导致用户磁盘爆炸：缺乏自动清理与容量控制机制 #1825 Team 模式缺少 Member 间直接通信机制：星型拓扑导致协调效率低 #1828 子代理取技能数据/执行命令必须经主模型中转 —— 建议支持工具调用直通子代理 #1833 [Bug] WebUI「＋」附件菜单：小屏幕 100% 缩放下弹层顶部被裁出视口，顶部菜单项不可点击且滚动无法找回 #1835 上下文压缩导致评审条目丢失，用户需手动恢复上下文 #1836 file-index: 过滤时只保留前 30 名，并去掉逐项 lowercase #1837 auth: rate-limit failed local API authentication #1840 [Bug] 默认权限下审批弹窗样式需优化：缺少默认选中项，底部 footer 与状态栏粘连 #1841 [Bug] TUI /goal 徽标缺运行时长：运行中动态递增、暂停后冻结（仅 /goal，/loop 不在范围） #1842 webui重复展示加载claude.md #1843 [性能] TUI 流式回复逐 delta 复制全文，建议原地追加并增量渲染"],["v5.2.8","v5.2.8 2026-11-20","Overview This release makes \"moving over from another AI coding tool\" a real workflow: the new atomcode import command and /import scan the instructions, skills, MCP servers and provider settings left behind by Claude Code, Codex and OpenCode, explain item by item what already takes effect, what can be brought over and what cannot, and write provider accounts only after confirmation. Structured Git status, configurable vision preprocessing models, hosted web search with automatic failover give both the model and the user a more reliable view of the current situation. Stability work focuses on long thinking and streaming. Continuous reasoning has no cumulative time limit, and reasoning content refreshes the stream idle timer. SSE line buffers have a size limit and scan only new bytes. Sessions, compaction, background tasks, teams and sub-agents have fewer races and polling loops. The terminal now guides first-time model setup and sign-in recovery, and @ session references can be filtered to the current working directory. Changes Import another AI coding tool's assets : Add atomcode import ( --json for a machine-readable report, --apply to write accounts after per-item confirmation, --yes to skip confirmation for accounts without a literal credential) and a TUI /import panel, scanning Claude Code, Codex and OpenCode instructions, skills, MCP servers and provider accounts. The report shares one skill-root resolution rule with the runtime, so it cannot claim a skill is in effect that the runtime does not read. Provider accounts already present in the configuration are reported as imported rather than offered again, and credentials are compared by kind only, never by value. Anything deliberately left out shows up in the exit code, so a script is never told everything went in when it did not. Structured Git status : Add a git_status tool that returns the branch, HEAD, upstream, ahead/behind commit counts and the staged, unstaged, untracked and conflicted paths in one call. Paths are repository-relative and exclude uncommitted changes inside submodules. It is read-only, does not fetch, and reports unavailable comparisons as nulls rather than guesses. Add a configurable diff wrapping policy so long diff lines are no longer cut off on narrow terminals. Vision preprocessing and search : Configure the vision preprocessing model (VL) from the TUI and WebUI, with multimodal requests following a separate provider and separate streaming path. Web search gains hosted backends and automatic failover, switching across services in routing order; a legacy Exa selection migrates to auto. Providers and models : Add vendor protocol choices. Model discovery preserves errors from providers and shows models.dev suggestions only when the protocol or endpoint does not support listing models. Expand the Alibaba, Xiaomi, Kimi and Tencent presets and keep subscription credentials separate from plan URLs. Support a per-model output token budget, and let CodingPlan name a provider account per model with automatic gateway whitelisting. Switching models can warn that the next message may exceed the context window or that automatic compaction is about to start. An unknown window stays silent. Code intelligence and prompts : The built-in LSP tool's diagnostics are no longer empty — on Windows the URI a server returns (lower-case drive letter and a percent-encoded colon) differs from the one sent in didOpen, so the whole push was dropped; the lookup now uses the filesystem's path identity. The system prompt asks for important conclusions to rest on inspected evidence, to distinguish observation from inference, and to report failed or unperformed checks honestly. Long thinking and streaming : Continuous reasoning is no longer cut off by a cumulative time limit — while the model keeps producing reasoning content the request keeps waiting, the first-response and stream-idle deadlines still apply and reasoning content refreshes the idle timer, and the manual and automatic recovery paths after a reasoning timeout are removed. Auxiliary calls of a model with a configured reasoning effort (session title, compaction summary and similar) inherit the model's default effort, an explicit value wins, and the effective effort and its source are logged. Bound SSE lines in the Anthropic, Ollama and Responses decoders: a line or unterminated tail above 16 MiB ends the stream with a terminal error. The decoders scan only new bytes instead of re-draining the buffer per line. Bare scalar enums in tool schemas now carry a type, fixing HTTP 400 responses from strict validators such as Volcano's kimi-k3-1-pro. Sessions, compaction and recovery : Report a rejected summary separately from \"nothing to compact\" and keep the diagnostics. Summarize long histories in recoverable windows. Name the reason for a refused session switch, report a turn that ended abnormally when resuming, and keep Unavailable / Stale typed across the embedded boundary. A rewind still takes effect when checkpoint retention fails, and rewind storage gains a retention bound so snapshots do not accumulate without limit. Background tasks, teams and sub-agents : Align background waits with host wakeups, bound the cancellation wait, preserve pending requests and limit the cost of Git statistics. Team members stop polling for status and resolve qualified model routes. Sub-agents support read-only Grok and OpenCode delegation, with a preflight check that reports blockers explicitly. WebUI and TUI experience : Session browsing keeps sessions held by other runtimes read-only and shows their activity. It offers independent forks, serializes history refreshes, and retries the final refresh. Workspace file previews link to the Git panel and bound the cost of read-only statistics. Model selection and reasoning effort share one control, with model labels and chronological turn navigation preserved. The turn highlight moves past completed reply tails. Mobile composer controls remain accessible by touch, and offline pages gain contrast in dark mode. Interrupted WebUI response streams finish cleanly. The workbench Git panel shows an empty state outside Git repositories. The TUI uses a blinking bar cursor and leaves room for it next to the empty-composer placeholder. It measures generation speed over streamed output, excludes display prompts from copied user messages, and wraps long diff lines by display policy. TUI model setup and sign-in recovery : On first launch, sign in to CodingPlan or choose a provider from the welcome screen. Click the authorization link to open it or press c to copy it. After signing out or when sign-in expires, the TUI points to /login or /provider and preserves the draft during sign-in recovery. CodingPlan models can show localized aliases and descriptions. Search slash commands by description in the TUI and WebUI. In the TUI, /theme opens the theme setting, and changes apply after restart. Find session references by working directory : In the TUI, use @ to find local sessions from other working directories, or narrow the list to the current directory with “Sessions · this workspace.” Search by session ID or preview text. Unnamed sessions can show their first saved user message even if the turn never finished. Invalid references report the specific format error. Tool approvals : TUI tool approvals require explicit confirmation. Regular typing and input methods remain available for drafting. Managed headless runs can use --require-approval-hook to require a user-level approval hook covering every tool. A call is blocked if the hook fails, times out, or does not explicitly approve it. Compaction and project knowledge : Compaction reuses the already-sent request prefix where possible and treats a tool call during summarization as an incomplete summary. Previews of compacted tool output keep the beginning and end so final errors and exit details remain visible. The project knowledge index can list when a topic applies, why it matters, and its file path. The model opens relevant notes and source evidence as needed. Windows WebUI and version rollback : On Windows, the WebUI uses a system-assigned port if no port was specified and the default port range is unavailable. After a version rollback, startup honors the rollback and suppresses the previously staged automatic upgrade. Import and batch operations : Import reports flag failed session scans and identify where MCP settings came from. Large reviews run in batches and report how much finished if they time out. If a batch search-and-replace write fails, the tool attempts to restore verified writes and reports the result. IDE plugin improvements : The VS Code chat panel zooms its font with Ctrl (Cmd on macOS) plus the mouse wheel, and a change to atomcode.fontSize takes effect immediately without reloading the window. Body and code block sizes scale together. Code review and tools : Reviews trace timing and share Git evidence, candidate verification is scoped to the changed file, and merged dimension tags are compared as a slice. The todowrite full-plan receipt becomes a status count, and background review presets a task title to avoid reporting tools as unavailable. AtomGit tool arguments parse leniently and write paths give a consistent UN_KNOW self-correction hint. The grep sensitive-path check no longer round-trips JSON per file and keeps single-quote boundaries. Network and credentials : Use Termux DNS configuration when the system resolver is unavailable, fixing the static Linux build falling back to a loopback address when it cannot read /etc/resolv.conf , which blocked login. Keep relay diagnostics for remote task recovery. Manage saved SSH credentials from the TUI, diagnose unattended credential problems and suppress unattended prompts. Permission rules save literal Bash rules without wildcard expansion. Telemetry scrubs the longer path first and redacts provider errors before sending them. Related issues 本节收录 v5.2.8 里程碑 下的全部 issue，不区分状态与标签。此列表用于关联跟踪，不表示所有条目均已实现或完成发布验收。 #1412 [Bug] 手机 App（/app）发指令后立刻切换会话，指令被截胡到另一会话执行（时序竞态，稳定复现） #1600 [共创大赛][Bug] atomcode二进制文件硬编码127.0.0.1，导致在termux中无法正常登录 #1791 [Bug][CLI][Team] --model 不切 provider 账号导致请求打到默认后端；团队 lead 反复轮询 status 空转 #1792 [Bug][LSP] 内置 lsp 工具 diagnostics 恒为空：publishDiagnostics 的 URI（小写盘符 + %3A 编码）与 didOpen URI 不匹配，整条推送被丢弃 #1793 [Feature] WebUI 缺少 vision_preprocessor_provider（VL 视觉预处理模型）的展示与修改入口 #1795 webui页面滚轮操作老是往上跳，挑到前几轮会话的地方去了 #1796 Review — atomcode schedule subcommand #1797 Code Review: Background session manager #1799 更新版本以后，安卓手机app连接到CLI以后点击始终任务，在cli上不生效 #1800 [共创大赛][Bug] atomcode提示一直无法连接到服务器 #1801 增加Epistemic Discipline约束 #1804 [Feature] 为 diff 显示增加自动换行（wrap）选项 #1806 /compact 上下文一直压缩不了呢 #1807 [Feature] 一键迁移其他 AI Coding Agent 的资产（指令/技能/配置/会话） #1808 [Bug]: reasoning_without_output 预算不随 reasoning 增量重置，且重试成倍叠加（单轮挂起约 15 分钟、usage 全部丢失） #1809 [Bug]: 同一模型已配置 reasoning_effort = \"high\"，实际请求交替下发 omitted #1811 feat(vscode): 聊天面板支持 Ctrl+鼠标滚轮缩放字号（atomcode.fontSize 实时生效） #1812 [Bug] debug 工具 schema 的 action 字段 enum 缺少 type，导致火山 kimi-k3-1-pro 全部请求返回 400 InvalidParameter #1813 Feature: Add structured git_status tool with unpushed commit detection for AI model"],["v5.2.7","v5.2.7 2026-11-12","Overview This release improves long-running tasks and everyday controls: pause and resume all MCP servers for a session, load long conversation histories on demand, and recover more reliably from interruptions. It also expands skill invocation, debugging and project setup, with improvements to the WebUI workspace, terminal input and tool diagnostics. Changes Pause and resume all MCP servers : Use Ctrl+S at the top of the /mcp list to pause all MCP servers and press it again to resume. Controls are available in both TUI and WebUI, apply only to the current session, and preserve individual server configuration. Fix non-ASCII paths during environment variable expansion and improve MCP tool search relevance. Long histories and context compaction : TUI and WebUI load display history in pages on demand. Bound summary inputs and old tool records, reduce copying and repeated computation, and distinguish a failed summary from a compaction that needs no changes. Recovery and task progress : Improve recovery of accepted prompts after interruptions and keep todo records aligned across undo, rewind, forks and cancellation. Verify quota availability before resuming paused loops, with bounded retries and jitter for automatic recovery. Automatic browser workflows : Configure a separately installed browser backend once through /browser , then describe webpage navigation, forms, clicks or screenshots to automatically load browser guidance and use connected tools. Existing approvals and explicit session reload remain; no per-task skill or slash command is required. Skill names and invocation : Support Chinese skill names, separate display titles and multiple $skill references in one input. Add usage history and conservative spelling suggestions. Debugging and project setup : Add DAP debugging and local adapter discovery. Project setup checks existing capabilities and offers optional tool installation with confirmation. An optional read-only architecture evidence capability can be enabled in shared settings. Task checks and automatic review : Add configurable, audited checks for task handoffs and automatic review guidance. Improve background review permission inheritance, execution limits and failure reporting, including blocked writes by team members. WebUI workspace and navigation : Pin, clear and remove workspaces, resize the sidebar, and view the current Git branch and session identity. Improve cross-client image retention, file refresh, narrow layouts and scroll positioning for newly submitted turns. Terminal input and upgrade feedback : Show download progress, speed and remaining time during upgrades. Ctrl+C clears nonempty input first. Improve Windows and HarmonyOS scrolling, Unicode input and script encoding warnings, and clarify when the lead agent is waiting for members. Tool results and diagnostics : Reject undefined replacement capture groups that could erase text. Report invalid todo IDs, invalid structural search patterns and ambiguous symbols explicitly. Patch import errors identify the failing stage and path; artifact storage can fall back to a temporary directory. Model transport and efficiency : Improve streamed tool arguments, missing call IDs and SSE buffering. Reduce repeated context estimation and tool execution work, compress embedded WebUI assets, and expose native session identity in headless JSONL startup events. Related issues 本节收录 v5.2.7 里程碑 下的全部 issue，不区分状态与标签。此列表用于关联跟踪，不表示所有条目均已实现或完成发布验收。 #873 [共创大赛] write_file覆盖时read_to_string全量读取导致大文件OOM #1000 [共创大赛]webui界面左侧鼠标移入标题显示的是工作目录而不是标题完整内容 #1486 Context window not adapted for auto model when using openrouter or openai-compatible provider #1662 [Feature] 希望在Agent内核里添加DAP技术 #1735 [共创大赛][Bug] Agent 文本输出声称任务全已完成，但底层 Todo 列表仍显示 18 个待办项（状态不同步） #1737 [Feature] 按项目语言推荐 MCP / 工具：检测到 Rust 项目时主动提示装 rust-mcp、ast-grep 等 #1738 [Performance] 消除热路径冗余分配：Vec 中转 join / Arc 上多余 to_vec / 每帧 HashMap 查找分配 String / sgr 的 format! 链 #1739 [Bug][LSP] 真实仓颉服务端下 document_symbols 取不到大纲：.cj 的 languageId 兜底成 \"cj\"（须为 \"Cangjie\"），且工具层仍判 IDE-only #1741 [Feature] 让会话内 code_review（任务完成前的自动评审）可单独关闭 #1742 [Bug]输入/app不能生成二维码 #1743 [Bug] team/子 agent 工作时 main agent 等待期间误显示 ✻ Done，让用户以为任务已完成 #1744 [Feature] 输入框被 history 填充后缺少安全清空机制，用户不敢按 Ctrl+C #1745 鸿蒙 PC 登录自动打开浏览器仍报 Exec format error：5.2.6 发布二进制早于 #1161 的 sh 兜底修复 #1746 [Bug] team 成员 agent 之间不互通，\"not my file → skip\" 无任何处理机制，导致协作遗漏 #1747 [Feature] coding plan 刷新后，因碰上限停止的任务应自动恢复 #1748 [Feature] 需要机制告诉模型：任务前已是脏工作区时，不要简单 git checkout/reset，容易炸仓库 #1749 [Feature] 状态栏与工作台显示当前 git 分支，避免在错误分支上跑一整轮 #1750 [Feature] skill 多加载可发现性：/skills 用法提示、$a $b 一致化、已加载状态可见 #1751 [Docs] 大+小模型混合使用：能力已存在但配置文档缺失（capable_model 示例、跨账号陷阱、路由前提） #1752 [Feature] /upgrade 下载进度展示太粗糙，应换成进度条，可加网络吞吐曲线 #1753 优化重试策略：基于历史成功率动态调整重试间隔 #1757 Refactor webui api.ts: deduplicate SSE parsing and unify error handling #1759 [Feature] UltraCode 模式：面向质量保障的专业运行模式 #1761 文档改进：系统 prompt 保留策略应在文档中明确说明，而非需要阅读代码 #1763 文档改进：用户会话初始提示词的保留策略应在文档中明确说明 #1765 [Windows] 中文路径 codepage 串码：归档时把 UTF-8 中文工作区路径按 GBK 写坏，落盘成乱码幽灵目录树 #1766 官网docs中似乎有错误信息 #1768 Feature Request: Architectural Topology Intelligence (ATI) Motivation #1770 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 希望能增加工作目录删除按钮 #1771 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 希望能增加对 skill name 的中文支持 #1773 建议为 MCP 加个开关功能 #1774 provider: SSE 解码器行缓冲无上限，逐行 drain 为 O(n²) #1776 Windows 控制台代码页 936 时，TUI 输入框粘贴 emoji（✅❌❓⚠️⏭）被静默丢弃"],["v5.2.6","v5.2.6 2026-11-05","Overview This release focuses on continuity for long-running tasks and a more consistent experience across clients. Sessions can recover saved partial output and execution records after an abnormal exit, selected original task requirements survive context compaction, and reasoning loops have bounded detection and recovery. WebUI adds a project workbench for files, terminals, and Git. TUI and WebUI also gain model information, comparisons, and persona inspection, alongside improvements to skills, mobile session switching, and Windows reliability. Changes Interrupted-session recovery and team persistence : Streaming replies periodically save recovery records. Reopening a session preserves saved partial output and identifies the interrupted turn. Tools without recorded results are marked as having an unknown outcome and are not rerun automatically. Improve team-member lease ownership, stopping, and log persistence to reduce missing records at turn completion. Sessions containing the new recovery records require this or a newer version. Preserve original requirements and task progress : Retain selected original user requirements across context compaction so important constraints remain available. Task plans can reference their original user guidance. TUI and WebUI show recorded context-summary counts beside token usage to make context changes easier to follow. WebUI project workbench : Add a project start page and session-scoped access to files, terminals, and Git. Support a fullscreen workspace, more room for file content, and clearer narrow-screen layouts, errors, and operation feedback. Reasoning-loop detection and recovery : Detect clear repetition loops in reasoning streams, stop the current generation, and attempt one automatic recovery when replay is safe. Stop explicitly when retrying is unsafe or the recovery budget is exhausted. Discarded reasoning cannot reappear in partial replies. Explicit one-shot follow-up tasks : Register the next task to run after the current turn succeeds, either in the same session or in an independent session, with controls to inspect and clear registrations. Independent tasks use unattended approval rules and do not inherit temporary grants from the original session. Shared settings also expose automation approval policies. Model information and local model setup : Add offline model cards and comparisons to TUI and WebUI. Setup can detect Ollama and offer guidance when its local service is unavailable. Simplify model-card presentation while keeping list scrolling stable. Custom personas and provenance inspection : Configure and override the assistant persona and system prompt. Use /context persona or WebUI to inspect the effective persona fragment and its source after model switches, session resumes, or configuration reloads. More complete skill invocation : Improve when matching workflows are loaded for debugging and similar tasks. Preserve images attached to direct skill invocations, allow read-only access to resources belonging to loaded skills, improve catalog budgeting, and avoid dependency-tree scans and directory cycles. Import and apply patch files : TUI and WebUI can import raw text patches for inspection and application through immutable patch artifacts, making existing diff files easier to use without repeatedly pasting large patches. Terminal scrolling and input : Preserve the reading position when users scroll upward. Reduce selection and context-menu overhead during long streaming sessions, including dense mouse-move traffic, and hide the conversation scrollbar by default. Guard shortcuts during IME composition, allow suggested question answers to be edited, and fix caret visibility, SSH wheel/history interactions, window titles, and missing recent directories in /cd . Mobile pairing and session navigation : Make pairing content scrollable while keeping action hints visible when terminal zoom clips the QR code. Mobile and WebUI share project and session navigation, with clearer ownership errors and switching feedback. Browsing history no longer rebinds the active session. Improve link opening on HarmonyOS PC. File search and language services : Fix repository-external ignore rules leaking into file indexes and inconsistent ignore boundaries for relative or symlinked roots. Cancel obsolete scans and reuse WebUI search indexes to reduce repeated traversal. LSP initialization and settings file paths support template variables, with local outlines, bounded retries for empty results, and clearer search-scope feedback. Windows proxy handling and background execution : Provide clearer diagnostics and bounded retries when reading system proxy settings fails. Improve loopback probing: only explicit connection refusal permits a direct route, while timeouts preserve the proxy. Background command polling collects output and exit status promptly, completion notifications are enabled by default, and several Windows path and test-compatibility issues are fixed. Permissions and tool-output protection : Improve approval matching for compound Bash commands and saving exact project rules. Tool-output directories create their own Git ignore sentinel to reduce accidental tracking of full outputs. Tighten MCP server identity and prompt-label validation, and guide AtomGit API calls to consult documentation first. Companion IDE plugin improvements : VS Code improves local command-history refresh and model-specific reasoning choices. JetBrains improves project-scoped session history, model and slash-command selection, default execution modes, and error feedback; reduces redundant redraws; and fixes macOS sidecar files affecting packaging and runtime behavior. Related issues 本节收录 v5.2.6 里程碑 下的全部 issue，不区分状态与标签。此列表用于关联跟踪，不表示所有条目均已实现或完成发布验收。 #1228 Feature: plan/build 模式支持绑定不同模型和思考强度 #1367 [共创大赛][Bug] 让agent不要忽略被.git遗忘的内容 #1654 [Bug][VSCode] .ui 状态重复挂载历史 /login 与 /reload，权威 .events 中无对应 user_message #1698 鸿蒙 PC：/login 的登录链接只能看不能打开（希望回车/点击直接用本机浏览器打开） #1700 [Feature][讨论] 是否借鉴 open-claude-ui 逆向出的 Claude Code 交互物理学与工程算法以大幅提升用户体验 #1701 [Feature] atomcode webui希望增加类似dsh-better-sidebar的功能 #1702 [bug] aarch64(树莓派/Debian 12) TUI 模式下发起工具调用即冻屏，-p 非交互模式正常 #1703 [Feature][LSP] local 后端补 document_symbols 能力 + 空结果自动重试（retry/interval） #1704 [Feature][Config] 多项目下 LSP multiModuleOption.name 必须手改全局配置；建议（白名单式）支持项目级 config 合并覆盖全局 #1705 [Feature][Schedule] 定时任务创建/修改/删除的强制审批不受 permissions.default_mode=auto 控制，建议提供配置化开关 #1706 [Bug] atomcode连接手机时二维码显示不全，不能正常扫码连接 #1707 [Bug] 手机上查看不同项目，切换失败 #1708 [共创大赛]-[Feature] .atomcode/artifacts/ 工具输出目录缺少目录级 git 哨兵保护 #1709 [Bug] session-store: member session log persist fails intermittently — \"already in use by another runtime\" (lease race at team member stop / turn end) #1710 [Bug][Windows/TUI] 长会话流式输出中拖选后右键,整屏持续卡顿(右键菜单触发 1003 每格上报 + 选区切换全量布局预算) #1711 [Bug]直接调用skill时，不能传输图片 #1712 [Bug]atomcode在复杂问题调试时，不能主动调用相关skill进行处理 #1713 [Feature] 缺少推理复读检测：thinking 内容自循环时无中断与重新生成机制 #1714 [Feature] Task Specification Pinning：上下文压缩不得把用户给定的权威任务规范降级为摘要 #1715 [Feature] Lossless Large Patch Application：让工具直接应用用户提供的大 patch，而不是让模型分段复述 #1716 [共创大赛][Bug] #1717 [Feature] Bash 命令审批检测应更智能：本地测试/只读循环应自动放行而非每次询问 #1718 [Feature] question 选项应支持就地编辑：快捷键把选项文字调入输入框再改，而非只能从零在 type your own 行手敲 #1719 【建议】技能数量超过阈值后的提示预算治理：目录截断、低优先级技能不可见、无命名空间隔离 #1720 【问题】插件目录内技能自带资源无法被 read_file 读取（outside the world's root） #1722 建议增加「上下文压缩次数」提示功能 #1723 todo list 应在用户给出长篇代码指导时一并保存原始 patch/diff #1724 [webui] 回合运行中在侧栏切换会话被拒绝，且提示是「请先停止当前回合，再执行该命令」的命令口径 #1725 [webui] @ 引用默认「全部」把会话混进文件候选，自动名 session-&lt;id&gt; 与目录同形难分辨 #1726 [codingplan] 主模型被写成 supports_vision=false 时缺少视觉兜底：应自动借 qwen3.8-27b 转述图片 #1727 [webui] 展开「工作区」后主列布局错位：会话内容不再位于输入框上方 #1728 feat: 增加「模型卡」展示模型 benchmark 分数，辅助用户选择合适模型 #1729 feat: Ollama 接入缺少「快速配置通道」——添加 provider 时自动检测本机 daemon 并引导启动 #1730 [Feature] 主 coding agent 支持多种 system prompt 切换/覆盖（--persona / --system-prompt / 消费 config 字段） #1731 [Bug] Windows 下 WebUI 工作区「文件」页报 TypeError: Failed to fetch，无法浏览目录 #1732 [Feature] 支持「任务完成后自动执行预设 prompt」：任务链 / follow-up prompt / post-task hook"],["v5.2.5","v5.2.5 2026-10-28","Overview This release improves context management and reliability for long-running tasks, including automatic compaction, protection against failed summaries, background completion notifications, and session recovery. It also adds shared automation management, configurable default execution modes, and improvements to model setup, history navigation, remote access, and terminal interaction. Changes More reliable automatic compaction : Long active turns can summarize their older content, and compaction can run again in the same turn after usage falls and rises. Reduce redundant tool output and schema overhead, with on-demand discovery for AtomGit tools. Preserve dialogue when summaries fail : With a summary model configured, failed, empty, truncated, interrupted, oversized, or timed-out summaries no longer authorize dropping old dialogue. Emergency recovery also preserves user input and assistant conclusions. If safe compaction cannot make the input fit, the turn stops with an explicit error and can resume after recovery. Explicit model-free behavior is unchanged. Shared automation management : TUI and WebUI share task management, schedules, execution history, and access to task results. Configurable default execution mode : Set [permissions].default_mode to build , plan , accept-edits , or auto , including through /config . New sessions use the configured mode, in-session switching remains available, and explicit permission-bypass startup flags take precedence. Background completion and waiting : Improve completion notifications and waiting for builds and downloads, reduce repetitive polling, and correct background checks, exit-status handling, and native tail previews. Model setup and connections : Simplify Provider connections with model capability discovery, batch additions, and per-model editing. Clarify batch review versus active model selection. WebUI follows the runtime model identity; expired-login errors retain sign-in guidance, and connections can recover after a local VPN proxy stops. History and session navigation : Read full history from native event logs, load archived WebUI turns inline in their original assistant/tool order, and provide history navigation. Keep interactive resume within the current project, hide unavailable workspaces, and show the latest content after background session switches. Mobile and remote access : Enable phone relay access from the browser and improve pairing links, explicit sharing, mobile resume, compatible links, and QR-code presentation. Terminal interaction : Accept visible history completion with Tab; improve SSH, PuTTY, and browser-terminal clipboard, mouse, and glyph handling. Hide unnecessary todo disclosure hints, reduce routine progress notices, reposition restart and history-loading notices, and avoid temporary allocations during panel changes. Custom command arguments : Declare command arguments and validate them consistently across user skill invocation paths. Language services and diagnostics : Configure LSP initialization options and expose read-only diagnostics. Add schema-size, background-job timing, and stream-idle phase diagnostics. Streaming and execution boundaries : Improve incomplete stream handling, tool-call fragments, output limits, and preservation of usage/error facts. Honor tool opt-out, and refine requirement review, team role precedence, and todo completion behavior. Related issues 本节收录 v5.2.5 里程碑 下的全部 issue，不区分状态。 #669 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 请求体超出 20MB 限制时，应提供更主动的防护机制而非静默失败 #781 [共创大赛] 指令文件读取无大小检查导致OOM #782 [共创大赛] memory文件超限时读取整个文件导致OOM #1682 [共创大赛][Bug] V5.2.3 SSH 终端复制粘贴无法兼容 PuTTY，体验较 V5.2.2 退化 #1684 内置工具每请求全量加载：41 个工具 ≈15K token 死重，导致上下文迅速膨胀、频繁压缩 #1685 默认执行模式无法配置：每个新会话都从 Build 起步，缺 Claude Code permissions.defaultMode 等价物 #1687 perf(tui): borrow layout known module ids as &str instead of allocating Vec<String> #1688 [Feature][WebUI] WebUI 增加右侧\"对话节点导航轨\"(Turn navigation rail),支持按回合快速定位 #1689 weui的二维码也太大了吧，严重影响进一步操作，希望优化下 #1690 建议开源或发布 atomcode relay 服务端，支持自建中继 #1693 [Feature][LSP] 可配置/内置 LSP 初始化消息（initializationOptions）+ 逐项功能开关 + 自调试通道 #1695 [Bug] 共享会话期间 TUI 侧 /resume 被拒，webui/App 侧却能切换并同步回 TUI（两端规则不一致） #1696 [共创大赛][Bug] 自定义指令的参数配置和校验功能在 tuix→tui 架构迁移后丢失 #1697 [Bug][Linux/SSH][TUI] 输入框里按 ↑/↓ 不调输入历史，反而滚动上方对话（指针交回 + mouse_reported 时单发箭头被当成滚轮）"],["v5.2.4","v5.2.4 2026-10-21","Overview This release strengthens long-running tasks and recovery, lets running terminal sessions continue in the background when switching history, and loads large MCP tool schemas on demand. It adds a read-only IDE language-service bridge, phone access to the WebUI and custom provider headers, alongside improvements to terminal editing, reading, configuration synchronization and plugin permissions. Changes Long-task recovery and goal verification : improve /goal recovery and persisted paused checkpoints, retaining observed work, verification evidence and pending questions. Distinguish execution, recovery, verification and completion, with duration and token usage accumulated across turns rather than presenting verification replies as completed tasks. Switch sessions while work runs : leave a running terminal session working in the background when switching history. Keep live state and queued input consistent through switches. On-demand MCP tools : search with mcp_search to load large MCP tool schemas as needed instead of sending them all on every request. Reconnect individual servers from their detail panels, with cancellable reconnects that keep the runtime responsive; fix request correlation for MCP replies. IDE language-service bridge : add a read-only bridge to editor-provided types, definitions, references and diagnostics. Discover IDE windows and inspect bridge connection status; existing file and code search remains available without an IDE connection. Phone access to the WebUI : connect through the relay, or scan a terminal QR code for LAN access. Update remote-access guidance accordingly. More provider options : configure custom HTTP headers per account and opt into the DeepSeek Messages protocol. Saved WebUI model settings reconcile live sessions, and reasoning effort accepts levels declared by the model, including xhigh . More reliable streaming : remove the default total deadline for responses that keep making progress, avoiding the 600-second cutoff. Align first-content timeouts, improve bounded continuations and diagnostics, and retain explicit failure when recovery is exhausted. Round budgets follow configuration : honor unlimited rounds for main and delegated tasks. Explicit budgets produce a progress summary when exhausted rather than letting implicit limits stop complex tasks early. Terminal editing and reading : configure newline shortcuts, restore backslash followed by Enter, and add a menu entry for newlines. Improve Shift+Backspace, repeated keys and Emacs editing while protecting drafts from Ctrl+D. Add a terminal reader and viewport paging; manual navigation stops edge autoscroll. Clearer code and task display : wrap long code lines instead of truncating commands. Background surfaces group code blocks without copying decorative gutters, and language labels stand out. Todo plans start folded with expandable scrolling; team panels acknowledge expanded, collapsed and empty states. Restore generation-speed display and improve cache-reuse statistics. Consistent sessions and context : retain the actual session storage binding across configuration reloads, avoiding lease mismatches after directory changes. Identify history and summaries retained by compaction rather than presenting them as new requests. Unify cross-platform file and history references and add local cross-session messaging. WebUI interaction fixes : refresh skills when reopening menus, keep directory creation controls reachable alongside recent projects, and resolve shared questions on the web when answered in the terminal. Skill preauthorization and static permissions : support user and project JSON allow/deny policies and turn-scoped skill allowed-tools preauthorization. Unlisted tools still follow normal approval rules; explicit denies and sensitive-operation boundaries remain in force. Plugin and platform compatibility : validate plugin hook script entry points, bind trust to bundle content and support checked script wrappers. Improve serialized Windows clipboard access, MobaXterm rendering and unsupported pipe-input errors. Ignore stale sudo identity for non-root home resolution and resolve installer fallback versions from the release manifest. Command boundaries and startup : standardize on the current terminal UI, removing --classic and the ui.screen selector. Clarify that /worktree done returns to the main checkout without merging. Reduce repeated Git probes, prepare automatic upgrades without blocking terminal startup, and clarify repository lookup and Git credential failures. Related issues 本节收录 v5.2.4 里程碑 中已关闭或标记 fixed 的 issue； fixed 不代表已关闭或已完成发布验收。 #1264 install scripts fallback DEFAULT_VERSION still pinned to v5.0.2 (current release is v5.0.3) #1274 [security] hook/skill sh -c execution lacks source whitelist — command injection surface #1332 [permissions] 支持静态工具 allow/deny 配置（settings.local.json），让插件 hook 命令能预批准 #1333 [skill] frontmatter 支持 allowed-tools 字段，让 skill 能声明自己的工具白名单 #1365 [feature] 终端对话输入框支持 Ctrl+Z 撤销粘贴/输入（可选 Ctrl+Y 重做） #1397 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 建议增加针对单个mcp server 的重连操作 #1632 [共创大赛][Bug] atomcode 无法正常授权 #1651 ghostty 终端下回复代码或命令等片段会带竖线导致，导致复制会复制上该竖线，之前版本没有该问题 #1652 [Bug] 模型流式响应在恰好 10 分钟（600s）处被切断（dropped_before_terminal），长任务频繁\"异常中断\" #1653 【BUG】WebUI 设置页修改服务商 ID 后，聊天区模型标签仍显示旧 ID（live 会话未随配置重建） #1656 [Feature] 支持自定义 TUI 快捷键配置（换行键可重映射，如 Alt+J） #1657 复杂任务自动停止 #1659 TUI 长输出缺少翻页/滚动手段，长内容阅读困难 #1660 [Bug] WebUI 切换工作目录弹窗：最近项目区块遮挡「创建」按钮且无法滚动，需手动删除最近项目条目才能操作 #1661 [Bug] 配置重载失败 \"session lease belongs to ..., expected ...\"：runtime 重配置仅按 session ID 复用旧租约，项目 bucket 变化后必报 LeaseMismatch #1663 /worktree done 未按文档把 worktree 改动 squash 回主分支（仅切回主检出） #1664 【功能请求】MCP 工具 schema 延迟加载 / tool search，避免大型 MCP server 撑爆上下文 #1665 /team：回执、折叠、重开已修复（d925a3ea0），仅剩 status / clear 是否补待定 #1670 [BUG] Provider 配置缺少自定义 HTTP 请求头支持 #1671 [Feature] 内置 IDE 语言服务通道：悬停类型 / 转到定义 / 语义引用 / 诊断 / 代码操作（让有 IDE 的场景不再退化为 grep + 读文件） #1672 Feature request: 回合运行中支持切换会话 / 多会话并行运行 #1673 [Bug][WebUI] 技能列表缓存不刷新，思考强度 xhigh 被后端拒绝 #1674 [Feature][AtomGit] 仓库工具支持查找公开仓库，或明确提示个人仓库列表为空 #1675 [Feature][WebUI] 压缩锚点消息与压缩摘要缺来源标注，易被模型误读为新指令、被用户误认为消息乱入 #1676 【Windows】大上下文请求流式输出中途停滞（stream idle timeout），自动续接未能挽救，附 9 条客户端日志证据"],["v5.2.3","v5.2.3 2026-10-13","Overview This release improves network recovery and terminal interaction: continue replies from confirmed progress, refresh connections after silent timeouts and bound total OPEN retry waits. It also improves scrolling, copying and SSH display, adds math rendering on the web, and fixes restored-session commands and configuration handling. Changes Native Anthropic prompt caching : add up to four cache breakpoints across tools, system and conversation history while preserving thinking blocks and signatures. Update cumulative streaming input and cache usage without double counting, retaining prior values when fields are absent. Recover silent connections : when response headers time out and retries are allowed, refresh the connection pool at most once. OPEN attempts and backoff share a total budget, 180 seconds by default, with no automatic retry after exhaustion. Covers OpenAI-compatible, Responses and Anthropic requests, with local diagnostics for timeouts and recovery. Smoother terminal interaction : click or drag the conversation scrollbar to navigate; fix jumps when grabbing an endpoint thumb and unstable geometry around changing task panels. Clipboard waits run off the UI thread; fix Linux copying, stale selection highlights and context menus closing on mouse release. Math on the web : render inline and block TeX formulas while preserving code and currency text. Unrenderable formulas retain their source text, and search highlighting leaves formula structures intact. Commands in restored sessions : /goal , /loop , /queue , /policy and /worktree remain available after restoring history. New sessions, project switches and runtime rebuilds also retain the same command entry point. Worktrees use the current project : /worktree operates on the current session's Git repository, avoiding operations on the startup repository after restoring a session or using /cd . Consistent web session counts : project counts use the same visibility rules as expanded session lists, excluding unused empty sessions and counting fork lineages once. Adding a workspace reuses the session already opened by the runtime instead of creating a duplicate empty record. Read complete memories : /memory shows full global, project and local memory in a reader with wrapping, scrolling and paging. Long workflows are no longer truncated by prompt budgets; model injection keeps its existing limits. Continue interrupted replies : after a connection reset, premature close, or provider stream idle timeout, a request with saved text or a fully successful tool batch can continue once, provided the broken stream has no new tool calls or argument fragments. During recovery, completed side-effecting calls with the same tool instance, arguments and working directory reuse their confirmed results. Recovery shares the timeout budget, remains cancellable, and reports progress in the terminal and web UI. Pinned prompts in long conversations : once a user message leaves the viewport, show a one-line summary for the turn being read. Long inputs collapse whitespace and use display-width ellipsis. Visible prompts and small windows need no header; copying and exports keep the original content. Concise edit failures : an unmatched original text shows a short explanation, with full errors and current file text available on expansion. The model still receives complete recovery details; tool guidance requires fresh text and discourages repeating failed arguments. Less repetitive background waiting : merge consecutive polls with no new output for the same task into an expandable waiting record with a check count. New output, completion and failure stay separate, with guidance to avoid repeated waiting narration. Clearer request progress : distinguish streaming reasoning, retry countdowns, renewed requests and periods without output. Ctrl+O directly shows or hides received live reasoning, with an explicit hint when nothing has arrived. Expanded reasoning keeps following the bottom, and outer blank lines no longer pad assistant replies. Saved model preferences : persist thinking and reasoning effort per model across restarts, validating supported effort levels before saving. More reliable WebUI startup : skip Windows reserved ports when selecting a default port. TUI /webui --port is honored and unsupported arguments produce an explicit error. SSH and links : restore the mascot on Linux and SSH, strip terminal control sequences from notices, and fix unstable link pointers in cmux and links losing metadata during selection. Commands and skills : resolve commands and same-named skills through their own entry points while retaining built-in command priority. Plugin commands appear in the slash menu, and input history recalls slash commands. Windows Bash compatibility : prefer Git Bash POSIX tools so Windows programs with the same names do not intercept find and sort . Task failures stay failures : one-shot agents report internal errors for task panics, abnormal cancellation or missing turn terminals, retaining partial text and tool results. Terminal, headless, web and ACP mappings recognize the failure. Configuration and credential safety : report missing explicitly selected configuration files across interactive, headless and ACP entry points; redact quoted secrets as well. Source builds without official gateway signing support reject requests explicitly instead of crashing. Related issues #1448 在鸿蒙PC使用atomcode，时长提示\"API error 网络连接失败\" #1524 [BUG] 频繁出现\"响应中断\": error decoding response body: Connection reset by peer (os error 54) —— v5.0.9 仍高频复现（#1334 同类，疑未被现有重试覆盖） #1636 [Web UI] 项目侧栏会话计数包含空会话记录，与展开列表\"该目录暂无会话\"不一致 #1637 对话窗口体验问题:回滚困难、鼠标复制无高亮且卡顿、滚动滑块无法直接点击 #1639 [共创大赛][Bug] 插件 command 与 skill 同名时，command会覆盖 skill #1640 [Bug][Windows] bash 工具下 find/sort 被 System32 同名程序抢占，GNU 语义失效且报中文错误 #1641 [Bug] gnome-terminal 下 /app 配对屏二维码被静默降级为仅口令（cell_background 能力检测漏判不自报的终端） #1642 [Bug] TUI 斜杠命令 /webui 的 --port 参数不生效，仍尝试绑定默认端口 13457 #1643 [Bug] webui 绑定默认端口 13457 遇 10013（Windows 保留端口）时不触发端口顺延，直接启动失败"],["v5.2.2","v5.2.2（v5.2.0） 2026-10-10","Overview This release is about rebuilding the architecture and the terminal UI : the runtime is rewritten in layers, every front end shares one runtime, and a session is a log of events that comes back whole; the new full-screen terminal UI is the default, with settings, models, MCP, plugins and background sessions in panels. Changes A new architecture : the runtime is rebuilt in layers (agent loop / capability assembly / coding runtime) and the old engine is retired; the terminal, web UI, VS Code and ACP share one runtime and behave alike. A session is now a log of events: undo, rewind and compaction are appended rather than rewriting history, so a session comes back whole after an interruption or a crash. The new terminal UI is the default : running atomcode opens the new full-screen UI (switch back with --classic or [ui] screen); click, double-click a word, triple-click a line, right-click for a menu, drag-select across screens with auto-scroll, and click links and file paths to open them; the terminal title and tab show the session name and flag the session that is waiting for you. Settings and management in panels : /config opens a settings panel (Settings / Config / Status / Usage / Stats) with quota, daily usage and per-model usage; /provider manages accounts and models and checks connectivity once saved; /mcp turns MCP servers on and off one by one; /toolbox toggles single tools mid-session; /plugin manages plugins; /status shows the signed-in account and when the subscription ends. Background sessions and teams : /background (/bg) keeps the current session running in the background, grouped, switchable and retrievable; /review runs in the background by default; questions from background sessions come to the front to be answered in place; the team panel lists the main session, members and subagents with status, elapsed time and context use, and member sessions are saved and come back with their lead. More reliable sessions : /resume previews what a session last talked about, and Ctrl+D twice deletes one; sessions survive renaming the project folder; double Esc opens the rewind panel; in a Git repository /rewind can take the code back too, on by default (ATOMCODE_CODE_REWIND=0 turns it off). New and better commands : /changelog shows what changed in each release; /worktree creates a separate working copy and switches to it; /diff and /diff git show this session's and the workspace's changes; /loop 5m repeats on an interval; /todo add and /todo clear edit the plan; /cost itemizes tokens by model; /copy copies the last reply, /copy code the code blocks; /raw prints the whole conversation to the terminal for its own selection; !cmd runs a command locally; /cd keeps bookmarks and recent directories; the new UI also has /proxy, /schedule, /openrouter, /app, /webui and /sync, and /upgrade upgrades in place and restarts; the slash menu is ordered by how often you use each command. Rebuilt model settings on the web : grouped by provider, one card for the provider and its models, connectivity checked once saved; set the reasoning effort levels a model offers and its default. Models and reasoning effort : F2 / Shift+F2 switch models quickly, with effort chosen right after; /effort lists only the levels the model supports; GLM and Qwen reasoning is kept; when two accounts share a model name the status line says which provider; OpenRouter no longer sends you to the browser once authorized, and retired models drop off the list. Smoother interaction : paste screenshots and image paths into the composer, with long pastes folded; file writes and edits show their diff inline; Ctrl+R searches this project's input history; Ctrl+X interrupts the turn and sends queued messages at once; sudo and ssh in tools ask for the password in the composer instead of hanging. Security, stability, Windows, and fixes : reading credentials, keys or .env files asks for approval first; delegated subagents have clear limits; the repeated-call fuse is gentler and tunable with [coding] repeat_stop_rounds; images per request are capped and compressed so requests are no longer too large; legacy Windows consoles, colors, keys and box drawing work, and a console that cannot draw the new UI falls back to the classic one and says why; /upgrade on Windows no longer fails with \"access denied\" while an old version holds the slot; background processes in bash keep their output and stop reliably; switching to a strict provider no longer fails every request with 400. Related issues #1352 [共创大赛][Bug] diff预览有丢失问题 #1479 [共创大赛][Bug] Ver5.0.7在使用 /upgrade 更新到5.0.8时会出现拒绝访问 #1564 Windows Terminal 下 Ctrl+V 无法粘贴剪贴板图片（Cline CLI 同环境正常） #1565 刚上的deepseek-flash模型报错了 #1568 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 希望在添加Provider的时候根据Provider的地址拉取模型列表进行选择 #1570 bug：读取图片后，服务连接失败且当前会话中无法恢复 #1573 [共创大赛][Bug] V5.1.0更新说明中修复ESC逻辑，实测未修复，反倒更糟糕 #1574 [共创大赛][Bug] 表格渲染不完整 #1576 [共创大赛][Bug] 系统提示末尾注入 Today's date，跨零点后约 91.7% 的 prompt 前缀缓存失效 #1577 [memory] 记忆注入无预算上限,长期使用 token 成本线性上涨并稀释系统提示 #1578 [mcp] 外部输入边界存在大量 unwrap/panic,单个 MCP server 故障可致整个会话崩溃 #1579 一直提示 工具输出一直被截断 之类的，要怎么解决的？ #1581 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 提供 AtomGit 工具的运行时开关 #1583 [v5.1.0] POST /chat 不挂载 MCP 工具，GET /live 挂载：是有意取舍还是缺口？ #1585 [共创大赛][Bug] 长任务偶发\"突然结束\"，UI 却显示为成功完成 #1586 基于 daemon HTTP API 做垂直发行版的一批实测问题汇总（v5.1.0，33 条，附最小复现） #1588 [v5.1.0] 工具返回 16KB 截断阈值写死在源码里，没有配置入口（截断后模型会用记忆补数） #1589 [v5.1.0] GET /live?session_id= 被「孤儿 runtime」占住后无法恢复，只能重启 daemon #1590 [v5.1.0] switch_session 之后 MCP 工具全部消失，而 /mcp/status 仍显示 connected #1591 [v5.1.0] .hooks.json 解析失败是静默的，hooks list 仍显示文件 ✓ 存在 #1592 [v5.1.0] hook 的 command 不做环境变量展开，而 .mcp.json 会做 #1593 [v5.1.0] docs/hooks.md 与 docs/webhook-guide.md 与实现不符（13 个扩展点 / webhook 均已失效） #1594 [v5.1.0] 被 PreToolUse 拒绝的调用，PostToolUseFailure 不带 tool_name，审计里记不下是哪个工具 #1595 [v5.1.0] latest.json 在 release tag 上写的是上一版的校验值，按 tag 锁版本会拿错 sha256 #1596 [共创大赛][Bug] todowrite 单条 action:update 报成功但状态不落盘，叠加 tool-loop 守卫导致会话死锁 #1597 [共创大赛][Bug] Linux版的 AtomCode 在询问是否执行时，选择 全部允许 依然重复询问 #1598 tool-loop guard 误报频繁：todowrite 状态对账 / 长任务轮询 / 任务列表重置 三类合法重复被拦截 #1601 [bug] Ctrl+O 无法切换查看详细思考过程：仅 Streaming 阶段生效，Idle 阶段被 Buffer::apply 静默吞为 NoOp #1602 [Bug][新TUI] 输出区滚动鼠标切换的是输入框 prompt 历史——鼠标交还态下终端把滚轮转成 ↑/↓ #1603 [Bug] /resume 会话列表 Ctrl+D×2 无法删除历史会话（删除确认提示未出现） #1604 [Bug][TUI] 推荐输入（下一句猜测）无消失手势且与真输入同形——左移光标/退格后读起来像「已被确认进输入框」 #1605 [Bug] 已命名的历史会话（AI/自动命名）切换后输入框上方名字徽章不显示，与 picker 列表可见性不一致 #1606 [Bug] /mcp reload 在 Agent 回合中被当作普通消息转发给模型，模型编造\"不认词/+mcp withdraw\"假报错；reload 异步结果反馈弱 #1607 [Bug] TUI 输出区 URL 链接边界越界：吞入尾随 ) 与后续中文内容（markdown 链接未渲染且无 OSC 8 超链接） #1608 [Bug] VL 折叠行的“点击展开”提示用 muted 样式与正文同色，用户无法辨识可点击（应用 Accent 交互色） #1609 [Bug] Ctrl+R 历史搜索：打开即带入上一条 prompt（Enter×2 可误重发），且过滤只显示单条命中、计数为全历史条数而非匹配数 #1610 harness 会话日志重复追加：同一会话每条事实落盘约 6 份，顺序哨兵判据确定性失败（release/v5.2.0） #1611 [Bug] fresh 会话启动竞态：首轮事实提交先于 publish_staged_session，撞 NotFound(index) 后 session-store 判死并 cancel，日志永久丢写 #1612 [Docs][TUI] 中断并发快捷键已改绑 Ctrl+X：物料按 e1f32e135 标题引用会带上旧键名 Ctrl+B #1614 [Bug] 新 TUI：Ctrl+O 思考过程文本颜色由终端实测调色板计算而非固定灰，macOS iTerm2 下不是灰色 #1618 TUI 应能解析 CSI-u 键报（vs code 1.140.0, atomcode 5.2） #1619 5.2.x 会话存储迁移后部分旧会话从 TUI 消失（无 .index，daemon 报 Corrupt） #1620 [5.2.1] 自动升级后 5.2.0 写入的 v2 会话（.index/.events）全部从 /resume 消失；5.2.1 疑为比 5.2.0 更旧的构建（缺 review 子命令，附二进制指纹与 rollback 验证） #1621 workspace 全量测试下 session::snapshot 两条稳定失败：store 路径取自其它测试临时改写的 $ATOMCODE_HOME，随后该目录被删除 #1622 webui 在旧内核浏览器（华为浏览器 Chromium 99）中无法正常显示：前端 CSS 使用 105+/108+/111+/117+ 特性，且缺最低浏览器版本说明与无 token 引导页 #1623 webui「登录账号」在 PWA 应用窗口中静默失败：window.open 弹出的 OAuth 授权页无提示、轮询 10 分钟无反馈，需先在浏览器登录 gitcode.com 才能绕过 #1624 team 角色缺 permission 字段时每轮对话重复告警刷屏，且 agents/*.md 角色文件 frontmatter（含 permission）完全无文档、无迁移引导 #1625 webui 服务随 TUI 进程退出而静默停止，桌面客户端只提示\"服务没有启动\"且无启动引导——建议支持独立守护模式 #1626 会话 bucket 内的备份子目录（bak_*）被扫描器计入，导致同一会话 ID 重复、聊天连接报 HTTP 409 Conflict #1627 客户端关闭后重启：webui 进程反复短命退出且不绑定端口 16 分钟，登录按钮无服务可连（附完整监控+daemon 日志时间线） #1629 [共创大赛][Bug] v5.2.1 版本新TUI，windows 平台，对话过程中 control + c 复制，会导致对话终止。 #1630 [共创大赛][Bug] v5.2.1 新TUI，选择右击会出现 “copy the selection put the selected text” 一个类似的按钮提示，会遮挡你选择服务的内容。 #1632 [共创大赛][Bug] atomcode 无法正常授权 #1633 长会话多次 compact 后模型重发相同 todowrite，连续触发 tool loop detected 熔断（附日志证据与改进建议） #1634 [TUI] 执行 skill 时 SKILL.md 全文原样刷入 transcript 对话区，应折叠为摘要展示"],["v5.1.0","v5.1.0（v5.2.1） 2026-09-18","Overview This release widens what you can connect: the OpenAI Responses API and OpenRouter's free models, stronger AtomGit tools and code graph, plus opt-in code rewind and a daily work recap. Changes More providers : support for the OpenAI Responses API. AtomGit tools and code graph : atomgit_issue can update and close issues; atomgit_pr can list your own PRs (list_mine) and update a PR; the code-graph tools (list_symbols / read_symbol / trace_callers) now understand Kotlin. Sessions and memory : a new list_sessions tool lists this project's past sessions; a new machine-local memory layer (global > project > local). Code Rewind (opt-in) : set ATOMCODE_CODE_REWIND to roll back the code changes a session made. Approvals and safety : a new \"allow all Bash\" option, with the reason shown when you are asked again; press Tab in the approval panel to see the full bash command. OpenRouter in one step (free models included) : /openrouter [key] or an OAuth (PKCE) sign-in connects OpenRouter and sets up its free models automatically. /worklog daily recap : sums up the day's work across projects into a short report. Faster, smoother TUI, and fixes : the /resume list scans in parallel, about 4× faster; -c / resume only scans the current session's directory at startup. Related issues #756 [共创大赛] telemetry write_flag覆盖损坏的配置文件 #762 [共创大赛] OpenAI流式解析tool_call索引无上限导致OOM #765 [共创大赛] skill模板shell注入执行顺序导致命令注入 #1368 [bug] marketplace 同步失败警告前缀异常（⚠g/⚠d）+ 失败提示冗长刷屏 #1472 [Rust Review] workspace 代码检视：P0/P1 命中点跟踪（2026-08-20） #1500 [Bug] /mcp tools <server> 传入不存在的 server 键时提示 \"(none — server not configured)\"，误导用户以为未配置 #1504 [共创大赛][Bug]Team explorer 无法关闭 #1506 [共创大赛][Bug] 模型响应显示不完整，经常说半句就断了，再继续追问立马再回一段 #1511 [共创大赛][Bug]在鸿蒙电脑中shift+tab无法切换模式 #1513 v509接入mmm3出现3次工具调用失败, 依旧念出来系统提示词, 我觉得可能是这个模型就是这么拉胯 #1514 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 希望添加response协议 #1532 [bug] /loop 模式下 goal 为空时陷入死循环，模型重复输出模板回复 80 次 #1535 [共创大赛][Feature] 状态栏常驻显示缓存命中率（cache hit rate） #1538 codeintel 图谱工具(file_dependencies/blast_radius等)在大工作目录下挂死:CodeIndex 全量建索引无上限无超时 #1539 [共创大赛]-[Feature] openrouter #1546 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 给底部展示正在使用的模型增加渠道信息展示 #1549 [共创大赛][Bug] atomcode连接https://mcp.espressif.com/docs这个MCP时提示出错。 #1550 [共创大赛][Bug] AtomCode 代码图谱工具对 Kotlin 语言超级不友好，任务大的时候非常容易遇到折叠墙 #1551 [Bug][Windows] datalog 会话日志 O(n²) 膨胀：每轮全量快照写入 jsonl 且无轮转/保留策略，29 天写满 36GB 磁盘 #1553 [bug] 网络短暂中断直接掐断响应（os error 10054），无网络探测等待与断点续传 #1558 [共创大赛][Bug] 会话日志只记录轮级汇总，缺少每次 LLM 请求的耗时/token 明细，建议增加请求级粒度 #1561 [Bug][VSCode 扩展] 模型限流（rate_limited）时本轮直接结束 + 排队消息被清空：应保留排队并在限流恢复后自动继续 #1562 [共创大赛]-[Feature]linux/鸿蒙终端环境中，完善允许 Bash执行命令。 #1563 [共创大赛]-[Feature] TUI 审批弹窗信息不足：bash 命令被截断，无法判断执行后果 #1566 模型报错［invalid_request_error/invalid_request_error］ Invalid schema for function 'code_review': null is not of type \"array\"］ #1567 [共创大赛][Bug]建议提高这个超时时间 stream idle timeout — reconnecting (1/5)"],["v5.0.9","v5.0.9 2026-08-27","Overview This release lets AtomCode bring in more help: Codex and Claude Code as external subagents, a deep code-review mode, reasoning effort driven by configuration, and the ACP v2 protocol. Changes External subagents (Codex / Claude Code) : use Codex or Claude Code as a subagent backend. Deep code review : /review deep and verify review along several dimensions in parallel, check every finding on its own, then merge the duplicates. Reasoning effort from configuration, with a new xhigh level : effort levels come from configuration, including reasoning_effort_levels sent by the server. ACP v2 : sessions and resume, elicitation forms, MCP, and v2 HTTP MCP connections. Resume a session from the command line : -p --resume and the resume subcommand reopen a given session; its id is printed on exit. TUI and compaction : the ● dot turns green when a tool call succeeds (serial, parallel and resumed alike); even one huge turn can be compacted; compaction always keeps the latest real exchange. Fixes : sturdier provider and model management and weak-model handling, plus sign-in and security fixes. Related issues #1456 [共创大赛][Bug] Todowrite工具调用更新状态出错 #1473 5.0.8更新后TUI渲染表格好难看 #1482 [共创大赛][Bug] 使用/login登录时，若用户点击“取消”按钮，则会导致Windows控制台会卡住 #1487 动不动就截断......一点token全浪费在处理截断上了 #1488 [共创大赛][Bug] 输出折叠频繁，消耗很多无意义的 token #1490 希望添加会话恢复功能 #1492 gmi的mmm3接入atomcode跟个**一样, 但是接到cc里就开了智了 #1494 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 打开的web页面聊天框无法@模糊匹配文件名,希望增加一个 #1495 resume 指令处理超时"],["v5.0.8","v5.0.8 2026-08-20","Overview This release improves selecting and copying in the terminal, adds a Zhipu Coding Plan preset and more hook events, and cuts the round trips weak models make on large files. Changes Select and copy with the mouse : double-click a word, triple-click a line, and the selection is copied; tool blocks such as bash commands and output can be drag-selected too; mouse capture is now off by default, so the terminal's own selection works. Zhipu Coding Plan preset : add Zhipu Coding Plan straight from /provider; the protocol toggle gains Ollama, filling in the local address when left empty. New hook events : Stop, StopFailure and PostToolUseFailure let plugins see a turn end, an API error, or a failed tool call. /code-review shows progress : the current round (round X/N) and the findings so far. Fewer round trips on large files : read_file can jump to a spot from the outline and read several ranges at once. Fixes : an interactive /resume of a busy session now forks it; replies cut off by the length limit happen less often; the web UI can send messages over plain HTTP on a LAN and no longer stacks duplicate notices; an unmatched edit_file is a yellow warning, not an error. Related issues #1329 [hook] 补齐 PostToolUseFailure 事件，让插件能区分\"工具成功\"与\"工具失败\" #1468 没有ollama版？ #1470 TUI: 带圈数字序号（①②③等）与后续字符重叠/错位 #1471 [共创大赛][Bug] ghostty 新版本复制回答内容文本有问题"],["v5.0.7","v5.0.7 2026-08-19","Overview This release focuses on the web UI: manage providers and discover models there, and install it as a desktop app; reasoning effort can be set per model, and the terminal gets much better interaction. Changes Providers and model discovery in the web UI : manage providers, discover and add models, and reuse an existing account when adding a model. Install the web UI as an app, with notifications : install it as a desktop app (PWA) and get a browser notification when a task finishes; a persistent Todo panel, a reworked sidebar, adjustable font size, and per-turn stats. Reasoning effort per model : configure effort levels per model; /provider in the TUI takes several at once, the web UI offers only what the endpoint supports, and the choice stays in sync across clients. Much better TUI interaction : select conversation content by meaning, select text with the mouse in the composer and history, preview sessions in the picker, and move Up/Down by wrapped lines; repeated pastes can be expanded; long tasks wrap more reliably. Security : the credential shell guard is configurable, and approval conditions you grant are remembered. Fixes : IME input being overwritten, sidebar flicker, the waiting indicator, lost turn timestamps, the notification permission prompt, and message queueing and sync in the web UI; Orca terminal support, table rendering on Windows, and a proxy loopback leak; truncated session tab titles in VS Code and the model dropdown highlight in JetBrains; duplicate plugin scans of the home directory, per-project prompt history, and folded Team tool output. Related issues #1312 [共创大赛][Bug] vscode的扩展一旦出现会话名字过长，在窗口过小的状态下会出现不显示关闭按钮 #1348 5.0.5 历史会话webui里的时间戳 显示的时间是恢复时的时间吗, 能改成显示这条消息发送时的时间吗 #1349 [bug] 对话界面显示内部系统文本（\"我就在任务1上！继续任务2！\"、<system-reminder> 块泄漏到会话显示） #1376 [Feature] 文本输入类似编缉一样删除/修改 #1381 [共创大赛]-[Feature] /init指令需要自定义 #1390 [Enhancement] TUIX 输入历史应按工作目录/会话隔离，避免跨项目上下文污染 #1395 在回复skill提问的时候应该允许多行输入 #1396 [共创大赛][Bug] Tab键误触发切换模式 #1400 fix(plugin): 修复 home 目录下插件 scope 重复枚举（对应 PR #992） #1409 /paste在回答skill提问时无效 #1410 终端输入 atomcode 后自动填充了 OSC 转义序列残留 ］11;rgb:ffff/ffff/ffff\\ #1414 [bug] Windows 窗口缩放到 1/4 大小（Win+←+↑）后对话输入框无法输入 #1415 [bug] load session failed：.lease 文件被锁定 os error 33（Windows ERROR_LOCK_VIOLATION） #1416 [bug] /resume 恢复会话出现 \"loading session\" 卡死（加载无超时/锁死锁/无法中断） #1418 [共创大赛][Bug] 作答输入无法用左右键控制光标 #1419 [共创大赛][Bug] windows上powershell中使用时模型回答部分内容未正常显示 #1422 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 长文本ctrl + v两次，把全文贴到终端里 #1425 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 视觉化移动光标 #1426 [Bug] TUI markdown 列表编号低对比度不可见（选中才可见） #1427 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 希望webui增加任务完成时的浏览器提醒 #1429 [共创大赛][Bug] 我只开了auto，不知道什么时候改成build了？ #1432 [共创大赛]-[Feature] /provider 添加模型增加默认的思考强度字段 #1433 [bug] request_user_input 自由文本输入长内容无换行，被截断隐藏（truncate 而非 wrap） #1434 [bug] 切换窗口后输入内容不实时回显，需按删除/空格才触发显示 #1435 [共创大赛][Bug] 23%tok窗口就过早自动压缩 #1437 task 子代理(hard 档)只路由到 capable_model 模型(GL M-5.2)且易卡住 #1438 PR 说明中拦截 token/key 关键词：无文档无开关，建议改为密钥格式识别+分层策略 #1444 [共创大赛][Bug] agent 执行多任务过程中，手动取消，输入新提示词，还是会继续上一次的任务 #1447 申请给auto模式解除限制 - 安全策略已阻止工具调用：凭据不能通过通用 shell 参数、临时文件或环境变量传递 #1450 web UI 历史对话的时间显示不对,时间总是显示的当前系统时间（atomocode v5.0.6） #1454 [Bug] webui 切换模型推理强度未广播同步到 TUI #1455 [优化] 模型思考强度配置展示优化：档位符号、官方模型锁定、默认值合并 #1457 [优化] 会话历史：事件时间显示在文字前且带年月日、prompt/回答左右对齐+背景色区分"],["v5.0.6","v5.0.6 2026-08-12","Overview This release brings agents working in parallel (Agent Team) and semantic code intelligence (LSP) when you want it, more reliable recovery for long tasks, and an interactive configuration editor. Changes Agent Team : several agents work in parallel, with each member's status, task details and token use shown live. Semantic code intelligence : enable LSP when you need it for symbol reading, reference search and call-chain analysis, making large projects easier to analyze. Goal recovery for long tasks : progress and context survive a pause, compaction, a model switch or a crash, so work is neither repeated nor lost. Interactive /config editor : manage configuration inside the TUI; new Xiaomi MiMo and OpenCode Zen presets, and per-model vision settings. MCP improvements : follows the usage instructions an MCP server provides; tighter HTTP response limits, stdio timeout recovery and concurrency handling make it steadier and safer. Sessions and web UI : configurable /resume history truncation, continuing a session across workspaces, and adding messages while a task runs; TodoWrite rows name the task; better input and model switching on mobile. Images and large files : a model can declare native image support with supports_vision; read_file hints at paging so a huge file never lands in context all at once. Fixes : DeepSeek V4 tool calls, F2 skipping unavailable models, Goal/Todo panels out of sync, long-task wrapping, a lost input prefix, web UI queueing and sync, and internal reminders leaking into the session. Related issues #737 [共创大赛] bash工具dd命令绕过危险操作检测 #738 [共创大赛] bash工具无空格重定向绕过关键文件保护 #752 [共创大赛] MCP HTTP响应体无大小限制导致OOM #787 [共创大赛] MCP registry call_tool跨await持锁导致阻塞 #880 WeCom WebSocket errcode 846609: aibot websocket not subscribed - response delivery fails silently #1324 w10 v5.0.4 TUI出现标号文字重叠问题 #1335 tui v5.0.5 win10在429以后添加provider, 写完4项以后按回车没反应 #1347 [bug] 新对话自动名称变成 <system-reminder>；/webui 输入中文在终端显示乱码 #1357 [共创大赛]-[Feature] atomcode工作时，若配置的多模态模型，可以让agent自己就能看到png的图，现在多模态模型接入无法查看图片 #1358 askpass 测试使用固定临时目录，可能因目录残留而失败 #1361 [Bug/确认] MCP client 是否注入 server initialize 返回的 instructions 字段（说话纪律等行为约束未生效） #1362 [bug] /webui 每轮对话结束后终端回显乱码的 <system-reminder> 块（UTF-8 破坏 + system 消息泄漏） #1363 [Bug] atomcode多模态支持设计路线完全错误，再次催促官方合入多模态BU修复的PR #1371 任务规划不够详细 #1377 fix(capabilities): 清理 LSP 写入失败后的 pending 请求 #1384 [feature] 安全拦截触发时不应直接终止回合，应给用户提供可选择、可执行的替代方案 #1386 [共创大赛]-[Feature] #1387 [Bug] WebUI turn 进行中无法发送 prompt（输入被吞/按钮无反应） #1388 [共创大赛][Bug] 添加自定义 provider， Base URL 显示不全 #1389 [Bug] 插件 hooks 配置 {\"hooks\":{...}} 包装格式不兼容，导致 plugin trust 报 \"no hooks\" #1392 【Bug / WebUI 移动端】聊天输入框无法换行：手机软键盘回车键直接发送消息"],["v5.0.5","v5.0.5 2026-08-07","Overview This release makes a goal something you can keep pursuing, lets you steer a running task and suggests the next step when a turn ends, and edits GBK-encoded files in place. Changes Persistent goals : a goal stays after it is met or runs out of rounds, and your next message carries it on; Esc pauses it and your next submit resumes it; its status stays on screen. Steer mid-task, with next-step suggestions : add guidance while a task runs; when a turn ends you get a suggested next prompt based on its results. Edit GBK / GB18030 files in place : the edit tools keep a file's original encoding. Redesigned directory picker : /cd has a new picker; when a typed path prefix does not exist, Enter takes the highlighted match. Every server address is configurable : change any service address in configuration, for private deployments. Fixes : comments in .mcp.json, normalized MCP tool names and protocol negotiation; the first transient 429 is retried silently; a missing path suggests its nearest existing parent; credential shell commands are no longer retried in a loop; text contrast on light and dark terminals; reflow after resizing the legacy Windows console. Related issues #894 使用问题：终端交互界面缩放（窗口大小调整）因未做防抖处理的SIGWINCH信号引发类内存溢出卡死 #1252 bug: 同名 skill 不同目录时去重逻辑误删全部而非保留一个 — /skills dedup-skill 结果为空 #1287 模型提问时, 模型输出在cli里显示不全, 看起来新增的提问区域把输出遮挡了 #1290 [共创大赛][Bug] 【Bug】历史会话迁移后按\"回合\"被拆成多个独立会话，旧格式文件未清理，/login 同步后会话列表错乱 #1291 [共创大赛][Bug] TUI 窗口最大化/恢复后界面消失 #1292 todolist很难触发 #1293 [共创大赛][Bug] 首次使用/webui报错，无法正常打开web界面 #1295 5.0.4版报告 os error 5 #1296 [5.0.3][Windows] datalog 追加 .jsonl 路径在沙箱身份下报 os error 5，每轮对话弹 \"session transcript was not saved\" #1297 [Bug] request_user_input 在 TUI 端选择后，WebUI 对应弹窗未隐藏 #1298 [共创大赛][Bug] #1299 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 新增功能 #1302 5.0.4: session transcript .jsonl save fails with EACCES on Windows (os error 5) #1303 llm在尝试读取secrets时遭到cli阻止导致多次工具调用失败从而出现对话中断 #1304 [共创大赛][Bug] session transcript was not saved #1305 mcp stdio的不知道为啥用不了了 w10 v5.0.4 #1306 [共创大赛][Bug] 一直出这个警告“⚠ session transcript was not saved; check available disk space: C:\\Users\\73887\\.atomcode\\sessions\\51b941699e6d8685\\bf2f0af7-4c5d-43d4-94cf-404dc148ad8c.jsonl: 拒绝访问。 (os error 5)” #1308 [共创大赛][Bug] 在webui 中做出选择后cli 的选择框未及时同步关闭 #1313 [Bug] 使用 /webui 后直接退出，会话结束时报 \"session transcript was not saved; ... 拒绝访问 (os error 5)\"，jsonl 落盘为 0 字节 #1314 [Bug] Windows 平台会话转录文件（.jsonl）持续写入失败 — 5.0.2/5.0.4 均复现，transcript writer regression #1315 [Bug] 多开 atomcode 进程时，会话结束同样报 \"session transcript was not saved; ... 拒绝访问 (os error 5)\"，jsonl 为 0 字节 #1316 [Bug] /cd 切换工作目录时可选目录数量过少，少于 /webui 浏览器界面展示的项目分组 #1317 [Bug] Windows 5.0.4 会话结束时 transcript 保存失败: 拒绝访问 (os error 5) #1320 [Bug] Windows: 活跃会话 transcript jsonl 写入报 os error 5（拒绝访问），datalog 主记录正常 #1321 [Windows] Session transcript save fails with 拒绝访问 (os error 5) since auto-update — all session .jsonl stay 0 bytes #1323 [BUG] session transcript 拒写 os error 5: append_jsonl_line lock_exclusive 撞同session snapshot写流程排它锁规律触发"],["v5.0.4","v5.0.4 2026-08-04","Overview This release adds local scheduled tasks that run unattended through the system scheduler, along with a /rewind command and input history search. Changes Local scheduled tasks : a new atomcode schedule subcommand (add / list / remove / enable / disable) registers with the system scheduler (launchd, systemd, Windows Task Scheduler) and refuses risky commands in unattended runs; /schedule lists the tasks in the TUI. /rewind and history search : /rewind opens the checkpoint picker; Ctrl+R searches your input history. CodingPlan models sync after sign-in : signing in to CodingPlan fetches the available models. Custom project memory directory : ATOMCODE_PROJECT_MEMORY_DIR sets where project memory is kept. Fixes : output received before a dropped connection is kept, with a hint at a likely proxy cause (10054); pasting screenshots on Windows; overlapping tool blocks; unreadable grey text on dark themes; updating the bundled binary in the VS Code and JetBrains plugins; faster startup. Related issues #1255 memory 工具 project scope 存储路径硬编码 .atomcode/，建议支持宿主自定义 #1258 rewind 不能用 #1260 [共创大赛][Bug] 无法粘贴图片提示[错误：剪贴板中没有图片。] #1268 [共创大赛][Bug] AtomCode 扩展 0.1.2 后台持续写 rewind 快照（git 仓库），导致 cmd/git.exe 窗口频繁闪现、C 盘被持续占满、部分会话历史对话无法显示 #1269 [Bug] 鸿蒙 PC 上 /provider 配置界面无法使用 Ctrl+A 添加快捷键添加模型 #1271 [共创大赛][Bug] request_user_input 在多条驱动路径下被静默 Null 应答，导致前端无弹窗、模型误判\"用户取消\" #1275 [共创大赛][Bug] 删除会话失败，请查看 AtomCode 日志了解详情。 #1276 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 能否加速一下会话删除功能，当我删除大量会话的时候要等一会才能删除 #1277 [共创大赛][Bug] webui 会话列表选中后滚动位置丢失——点击深层会话后列表回滚到顶部，且从不滚动到选中项 #1279 [共创大赛][Bug] webui左侧的对话列表里面点击其他会话的时候，如果当前会话没有结束，会触发当前会话中断，并在喇叭里面听到响声。稳定复现。 #1281 [共创大赛][Bug] atomcode工具内部指令优先级超越用户指令，用户输入明确禁止编译和禁止执行脚本，但是任务完成后还是执行了脚本 #1283 TUI 流式长行重复扫描缓冲，导致渲染性能退化 #1288 [共创大赛][Bug] 双击ESC看更新日志改进了Rewind功能，但是我的5.0.3没生效"],["v5.0.3","v5.0.3 2026-07-30","Overview This release rebuilds the /provider panel and adds checkpoint-based rewind, an archive for tool output and a round-limit checkpoint, keeping long sessions under control. Changes Rebuilt /provider panel : separate Accounts and Models tabs, adding from vendor presets (TaoToken added), and editing accounts and models; /model groups models by account. Safe rewind : workspace checkpoints take the conversation and its code changes back to an earlier step together. Tool output archive : very long tool output is stored aside and read page by page with fetch_output when needed, so long sessions stay lean. Round-limit checkpoint : on reaching [coding] max_rounds you are asked whether to continue or stop, instead of being cut off. TUI : your input sits on a background block; subtask progress is pinned in the footer; shortcuts to switch models; /skills takes several skills with fuzzy filtering; shell completions. More accurate /cost : priced from models.dev and broken down by provider and model. Fixes : Windows uses the system TLS to get past fingerprint blocking; AtomGit sign-in recovers after a 401; HarmonyOS falls back to sh when bash is absent; MCP stdio servers recover after their process exits; /compact in the web UI's sync mode, uploaded images surviving a refresh, and refusing a model switch mid-turn. Related issues #1188 [Feature] App 端支持 request_user_input 工具交互（选择弹窗） #1193 [Bug] webui上传图片bug #1194 [共创大赛][Bug] 配置了provider不生效，终端还是提示让配置provider，无法正常使用 #1199 Installer may skip PATH update when an existing entry only contains the install directory as a substring #1201 [共创大赛][Bug] 版本更新后 开启多个AtomCode窗口时，webui界面切换模型问题 #1202 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 自定义指令的参数配置和校验 #1203 [Bug] atomcode.exe webui 直接启动时 MCP 工具在 Chat 中不可用 #1204 atomcode 5.0.2 的 /cost 命令无法区分单个模型各自消耗的词元 #1206 [共创大赛][Bug] VSCode 扩展聊天面板中 vscode://file/ 协议链接不可点击跳转 #1207 [共创大赛][Bug] 无法登录+设置代理失败 #1208 [共创大赛][Bug] TUI偶发出现两行或多行重复行 #1209 429等错误不应直接结束 #1210 BUG: v5.0.2 crash-orphaned .lease / .meta.lock 0-byte files block SessionManager::delete — session stuck as undeletable #1211 BUG: v5.0.2 legacy .json + native .ui.json dual-form coexistence causes session click to jump to a new session #1212 BUG: v5.0.2 fork_native_session leaves orphaned fork copies shattering one conversation into many session rows #1215 [BUG] 会话JSON末尾缺turn_count必填字段导致反序列化失败,会话点开卡死 #1217 [共创大赛][Bug] 在补充回答大模型的问题场景下，无法粘贴信息,只能键盘输入 #1222 [共创大赛][Bug] #1223 [Bug] /webui 启动后 TUI 未获得 sync 状态，webui 消息不同步到 TUI #1225 内容重复展示 #1229 [共创大赛][Bug]AtomCode多窗口时，在webui删除会话404 #1230 [共创大赛][Bug] #1231 cli使用领取的glm5.2时, 莫名其妙使用了不存在也未声明的brainstorming skill, 并且markdown表格底边显示不全, 还出现了滚动页面文字重复和内容显示不全的问题 #1234 [共创大赛][bug] GLM-5.2是支持1m的，还写200k就不对了 #1237 [共创大赛][Bug] #1238 模型回复太慢的问题请求解决 #1240 [Bug] PluginManager Marketplace 选择后按 Enter 导致 atomcode abort 退出 #1241 插件 marketplace 安装的 skill 无法被 $ 和 /skills 发现 #1242 [Bug] WebUI 刷新后图片和 error 信息不展示 #1243 [bug] vision_preprocessor_provider 未配置/配置不存在的 model 时，图片没有透传，显示 [图片识别失败] #1244 [bug] webui 贴图发送后，同步的 TUI 只显示文本不显示图片 #1245 [Bug] /skills 贪婪匹配多个 skill 名未生效 #1246 [Bug] WebUI 模型下拉框未展示 CodingPlan 等新 schema 模型 #1247 [Bug] WebUI sync 模式下 /compact 提示\"暂不支持\"，无法压缩会话 #1248 [Bug] WebUI sync 模式：模型与 TUI 不一致 + 切模型中断 TUI 任务 + \"继续\"不接中断的现场 #1251 [bug] daemon live hub 广播未按 session_id 过滤，不同会话的模型切换互串"],["v5.0.2","v5.0.2 2026-07-24","Overview A stability update: custom command arguments work, a broken configuration no longer stops startup, and network compatibility improves. Changes Custom command arguments work : the args field of a custom command now takes effect, filled into the command's text. Tolerant configuration : an invalid provider section is set aside instead of stopping startup, and writes such as /model still go through. Network compatibility : AtomGit connections retry over TLS 1.2; one broken system root certificate no longer stops all networking. Fixes : the web UI keeps the TUI in sync when switching projects and polls the model selector less; the install script matches whole PATH entries. Related issues #518 [共创大赛]-[Feature] git commit message 有时会是英文 #1015 需求：建议VSCode插件支持实时展示模型规划的任务清单 #1022 [共创大赛][Bug] idea atomcode插件还在对话中，报login failed #1175 [Bug] VSCode/JetBrains 插件运行模式与 TUI 不一致（缺 AcceptEdits，命名不统一） #1195 无有效移除项目功能，且“设为默认目录（重启后仍生效）。”并不会生效。 #1200 [Bug] WebUI 切换项目目录后未同步到其他端，sync 状态丢失"],["v5.0.1","v5.0.1 2026-07-24","Overview This release lets the model ask you questions right in the UI, tightens trust for project MCP servers and plugin hooks, and connects better on corporate networks. Changes Answer questions right in the UI : when the model needs a decision, the TUI or web UI shows a single-choice, multiple-choice or free-text question, and several questions can be answered at once; on by default. Trust for project MCP servers : servers in a project's .mcp.json connect only after /mcp trust, and /mcp untrust takes it back; .mcp.json accepts comments; plugin hooks run only once trusted, and you are asked again when a plugin changes. Corporate networks : follows the system proxy (Windows / macOS); trusts the system root certificates and SSL_CERT_FILE; sign-in connection failures come with troubleshooting hints. TUI : a live token counter while waiting, so long tasks no longer look stuck; a redesigned /resume picker that shows the delete and rename keys; /status, /diff, /rename and more run while a task is in progress; /todo add adds a task directly. Skills trigger more reliably : the skill catalog is in the system prompt and a matching skill is used first; the subagent task tool is on by default. Fixes : a bash timeout or cancel ends the whole process tree (Windows / Unix); the edit tool tolerates whitespace differences; wide tables, QR codes in Windows Terminal, and arrow keys under TERM=dumb; a third-party model's 429 is no longer reported as CodingPlan quota exhaustion; room is kept for the reply near the context limit. Related issues #514 [共创大赛][Bug] ❌ 不使用 Windows 证书库 ❌ 不读取 SSL_CERT_FILE ❌ 不信任系统 CA store ❌ OCSP/CRL 在企业代理下失败 ❌ 直接 connection failed #693 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 添加 AskUserQuestion 交互式问答工具和 TUI overlay #817 提问，调用mcp，选了总是，但还是需要反复确认 #956 [P0] provider/retry.rs std::thread::sleep 阻塞 tokio 运行时风险 #960 [P1] pre_exec 闭包缺少 async-signal-safe 约束注释 #964 [P2] 部分 ? 传播链路缺少 .context() 错误注解 #977 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 当.claude文件夹被添加到.gitignore忽略时, atomcode cli无法艾特其下的skills, 也不会自动使用其下的skills #1004 [Bug] TUI 中执行斜杠命令的输出未同步到 webui #1006 [Bug] TUI 中 /cd 切换目录和 /resume 切换会话未同步到 webui #1043 bug：任务完成后AtomCode自己给自己发了一句毫无关联的对话并自己澄清了（疑似与他人对话串一起了） #1045 [共创大赛][Bug] webui输入prompt发送之后不见了，但是同步状态下的tui会显示 #1074 FAQ文档中的几处错误：auth.json文件名与cargo install路径 #1076 bug：正常对话过程中突发的AtomCode无响应(AtomCode daemon started but not responding) #1097 bug：上下文对话的搜索关键词功能失效 #1102 Plugin loader 应兼容 Claude Code 默认目录约定（plugin.json 未显式声明时下钻扫描） #1112 [Plugin] 插件描述截断无省略提示，用户无法感知内容被截断 #1113 [Doc] bundled docs 快照（docs-zh.json）未包含 /loop 相关内容 #1114 [共创大赛][Bug] 429处理问题 #1117 新的usage没有以前cost好用 #1118 [共创大赛][Bug] #1121 增加粘贴图片alt+v快捷键 #1123 check_destructive_command 漏判单文件删除与 mv 移出目录，删除审批可被等价命令绕过 #1124 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 新增 ask 内置工具，支持 LLM 在对话中向用户发起单选/多选/文本输入 #1125 [共创大赛][Bug] 终端TUI模式下markdown表格没有渲染显示，直接显示的markdown源码，网页模式正常 #1126 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 建议安装脚本支持MSYS2 #1127 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 聊天窗口字体问题 + 文件路径截断问题 #1131 [共创大赛][Bug] TUI 模式下 use_skill 工具无法识别已安装 plugin 的 skill #1138 [共创大赛][Bug] webui 搜索功能不合理改造优化 #1141 atomcode在windows 10系统中，无法用上下箭头选择菜单项 #1145 atomcode的/cost命令在windows 10系统中后续命令失效 #1146 接入商汤的免费ds4f无法调用工具, 测试过cc没问题 #1150 TUI模式下，复制窗口文本，不能保留原有格式 #1151 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 需要支持从环境变量获取apikey #1152 /desktop 下载的 桌面端跟功能介绍不一致 #1153 relay-client: 3条daemon连接导致响应重复推送到手机端 #1154 【bug】加载会话失败：corrupt presentation anchor — legacy turn boundaries 非严格递增 #1156 [共创大赛][Bug] mac终端，首次启动 二维码有点问题，整个布局也是乱的 #1157 [共创大赛][Bug] 删除.atomcode 目录，执行cargo run 直接输出一点内容然后闪退。 #1158 [共创大赛][Bug] 在登录窗口，调整窗口大小，历史格式内容乱了，而且感觉很卡，resize的时候。 #1160 [共创大赛][Bug] idea 终端，/login 命令不弹二维码 #1161 [共创大赛][Bug] tools的调用后输出正文内容上面要一个空行，不然和tools的内容贴到一起了，没有层级。 #1167 新建会话首个 prompt 报 provider 不可用（AwaitingProvider 无自恢复机制） #1169 bug：疑似死循环了，一直在Bash同一个任务 #1170 [Bug] TUI 模式切换未同步到 webui（Plan/Build/Auto/AcceptEdits） #1171 [Bug] TUI 模式切换未同步到 App（Plan/Build/Auto/AcceptEdits） #1173 [Bug] TUI/webui/App 三端同步缺陷汇总：目录、会话、模式切换未正确同步 #1174 [Bug] webui 发送 prompt 后 TUI 未显示用户消息，只显示回答 #1176 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 会话进行中，支持部分斜杠command #1177 [共创大赛][Bug] 我不清楚为什么它写着谢谢会跟 sed 干起来 #1178 [Bug] 第三方模型欠费/超限时无错误提示，直接显示\"已中断\" #1179 [Bug] 同一目录不同终端窗口无法独立使用不同模型，一个终端切模型影响所有终端 #1181 request_user_input 工具触发率低，需增强 persona 引导文案使模型主动调用 #1182 [共创大赛][Bug] windows 首次启动，二维码无法展示 #1184 [共创大赛][Bug] 耗时任务会出现死循环耗尽系统资源atomcode进程强制终止也不会释放 #1185 [Bug] /usage 等斜杠命令的 ANSI 输出混入对话历史，不可读 #1186 [共创大赛] Bug: /cd 在同一路径下创建新会话目录分组，导致 /resume 看不到其他分组会话 #1187 [Feature] /cd 命令提示信息和site里面的文档描述要调整，目前/cd到对应目录是 切换工作目录并开启新建对话 #1189 [Perf] /cd 和 /resume 重配置慢 — MCP eager connect 导致全量重建阻塞数秒 #1190 [Bug] /resume 会话选择器中 Ctrl+D 删除无效果"],["v5.0.0","v5.0.0 2026-07-17","Overview The first AtomCode 5.0 release: four unified execution modes with approvals, read-only tools in parallel, a new /usage panel, and a better Todo panel, plugin marketplace and /init. Changes Better Todo panel : tasks update one item at a time, the in-progress item is checked every round to stop drift, and the run continues once more when items are left; /todo clear empties the list. Unified execution modes and approvals : Tab cycles four modes: plan, build, auto (no approvals) and accept edits. Read-only tools run in parallel : file reads, grep and read-only bash run concurrently, speeding up multi-tool turns. /usage panel (replaces /cost) : the current 5-hour window and CodingPlan plan, a 60-day heatmap, per-model charts and a usage table. Better /plugin page : marketplace browsing with search, install scope shown, and a two-line list. Better /init : an agent analyzes the repository and writes AGENTS.md; skills in ~/.agents/skills and .agents/skills are found and shared across agents. Context, stability and terminals : tighter tool-output limits keep long sessions lean; the web UI reconnects on its own and saves incrementally on a crash. Fixes : the context window now reloads after a model switch, /clear really starts a new session, and approvals and turns display better. Related issues #628 memory使用问题 #755 [共创大赛][Bug] cd 切换了路径，问他所在路径还是没有变化 #794 [共创大赛] 对话压缩摘要prompt注入防护不足 #944 [共创大赛][Bug] 在浏览器中点了 “本会话总是允许”后，还是会第二次出来要确认 （Deepseek模型） #955 [P0] MCP 注册表 std::sync::RwLock::write().unwrap() 锁中毒风险 #1018 bug：任务的执行耗时显示错误，显示0.0s，并且持续卡住（Read_file、Bash等） #1036 [Enhancement] VS Code 插件会话列表未按工作目录区分展示 #1037 [TUI][Bug] /model 切换模型输入关键字过滤时，输入内容未在输入框显示 #1040 [Enhancement] loop 功能未在功能文档中增加相关说明 #1041 [Enhancement] /todo 功能未在功能文档中增加相关说明 #1042 [共创大赛][Bug] 执行到一半webui刷新内容全丢失 #1047 [Bug] App 中出现重复消息显示，过一会儿又恢复正常 #1053 [Bug] Windows 下刚打开时插件更新信息逃逸到了输入框 #1055 [Bug] Windows 和鸿蒙下 /app 指令生成二维码失败（relay-client 未找到） #1059 [Bug] iOS GitCode App 扫码未连接上 atomcode 时黑屏 #1085 [Bug] App 中连续输入 2 个 prompt，排队中的 prompt 被中断不执行 #1094 SseDecoder:finish_reason 为 stop 等终止原因时不终止,退化的流式响应导致解码循环不结束 #1095 [共创大赛][Bug] 怎么禁止atomcode 执行git命令 #1096 [共创大赛]-添加Skills支持 #1098 /app 使用报错 #1099 [共创大赛][Bug] /cd 回车无法再输入路径，导致用户只能选择 #1100 [共创大赛][Bug] Ctrl+o 输出的详细内容 和 思考内容，没有根据窗口大小来适配 #1101 [共创大赛][Bug] 不能自动触发skill了 #1104 [Bug][Win] TUI 输入框光标无法定位到行尾最后一个字符后面 #1105 [Bug] 取消回合后输入新 prompt，旧任务列表仍然在底部展示 #1106 [Bug] Plan mode 下 MCP 查询工具仍弹审批，未细化到工具粒度 #1107 ［Bug］ /usage 页面在 Mac 下文字不可见（\\x1b［90m 配色导致） #1108 [Bug] 插件市场界面 3 个问题：未选中 tab 文字不可见、缺搜索框、描述截断无省略提示 #1109 [Bug] 删除插件市场时需手工先卸载插件，应自动卸载并弹确认框 #1110 插件市场顶部 tab \"Browse Marketplaces\" 展示的是 plugin 而非 marketplace，建议调整名称 #1111 [Bug] 插件详情页未展示 Marketplace 和 Version 字段"],["v4.26.0","v4.26.0 2026-07-09","Overview This release brings subagent delegation across strong and fast models, /loop, and Todo tasks, a much stronger web UI, and smarter context compaction. Changes Subagents across strong and fast models : the main model orchestrates and routes by provider capability (a strong model plans, a fast one executes), with subtasks in parallel; off by default, turn it on with ATOMCODE_SUBAGENT=1. /loop : repeat a task on a self-paced rhythm or a fixed interval, with stopping, a round limit and cancellation all handled. /app for the GitCode app : pair the GitCode app with AtomCode to use AtomCode from GitCode. Todo tasks : the todowrite tool manages a task list, the current list is given to the model each round, the footer shows the current task and progress (N/M), and /todo shows the list. A much stronger web UI : slash commands throughout (/undo, /compact, /context, /status, /config, /diff, /cost, /memory, /skills and more); three approval modes (Build / Plan / Bypass); a cross-project session sidebar; searching and jumping within a session; message timestamps; output follows only when you are at the bottom, with a back-to-bottom button. Context and compaction : multi-level compaction on overflow (mechanical plus an LLM summary) that keeps recent working context and bounds the summary's input, cache-friendly history compaction, and compaction pressure recomputed for the new model's window after a switch. Export and copy : /save exports the conversation as Markdown and /copy msg copies a whole reply; /provider can set context_window and suggests 128k / 256k / 512k / 1m. Fixes : grep no longer reads a whole large file into memory and freezes low-end machines, plus other fixes. Related issues #844 [共创大赛][Bug] atomcode经常出现堆栈缓冲区溢出的问题 #917 bug：VSCode插件中，一旦输出\"示例（Pandoc）\"，输出结果就会断层，无后续内容返回 #936 bug： 报错Failed to buffer the request body: length limit exceeded #950 [共创大赛][Bug] vscode 终端运行atomcode，调整终端大小时atomcode界面会异常 #970 [共创大赛][Bug] harmonyos ctrl+v无法粘贴图片 #978 [Bug] 终端 UI：任务执行完成后转圈动画未清除 #979 【功能请求】新增内置 Todo List 待办清单功能 #980 [TUI][Bug] 从历史记录翻页回访 prompt 时 $ 前缀丢失，skill 无法调用 #983 [共创大赛][Bug] 当前会话的Token上下文剩余量无法正常查看 #985 鸿蒙pc无法黏贴图片 #987 [共创大赛]webui界面，模型输出时自动滚动增加开关，允许用户自由浏览历史记录 #993 [Bug] Windows 路径大小写漂移导致重启后历史对话列表为空（写入归一化但过滤未归一化） #997 [Bug] 在历史对话中续聊必报 HTTP 400 \"glm-5.2 is not a multimodal model\"，新对话正常 #998 bug：输入的提示词和输出的结果被截断 （</script>截断） #1001 [共创大赛][Bug] JetBrains插件输入报错400 #1002 bug：VSCode插件中，排队中的提示词一直没被触发(整个对话结束了都没触发) #1003 [Bug] /app 扫码连接文案错误：\"AtomCode App\" 应为 \"GitCode App\" #1005 [Bug] 手机 App 缺少 \"Always Allow\" 审批选项，且审批决策后卡片状态未同步 #1010 [共创大赛]-[Feature] tui输入框在触发 bash 模式后，给用户交互提示 #1012 bug：从「deepseek-v4-flash」模型切换到「GLM-5.2」模型后报错 #1013 自动升级最新版本后不能使用了，网络有代理？ #1016 [Bug] Android App 上弹了两个相同的审批卡片 #1017 优化：AtomGit Bash的OUT的结果无法输出中文路径，显示问号 #1019 [Bug] GitCode App 扫码连接后会话名称未展示 #1020 [共创大赛][Bug] SKILL脚本调用失效 #1034 [Bug] TUI/WebUI 中发送 prompt，App 显示 2 条相同消息，执行完后变为 1 条"],["v4.25.9","v4.25.9 2026-07-04","Overview Sessions now name themselves, and the terminal tab shows the session name and its status, so several windows are easy to tell apart. Changes Automatic session names : after the first turn the AI names the session, never overriding a name you set with /rename, and the web UI shows it too; turn it off with [ui] ai_session_naming. Tab status light : the terminal tab title shows the session name with 🟢 idle, 🟡 working or 🔴 waiting for approval; turn it off with [ui] terminal_status_glyph. /compact no longer hangs : generating the summary is capped at 120 seconds. Fixes : /cd paths on Windows no longer carry the \\\\?\\ prefix, and the /cd picker lists each directory once; > nul is rewritten to /dev/null under Git Bash; the web UI opens the browser correctly on Windows; web UI output no longer corrupts the TUI screen; the Ctrl+O expand hint appears as soon as a tool starts. Related issues #945 [共创大赛][Bug] 版本显示不统一，如图 #966 [共创大赛]-[Feature] cli程序在标题栏添加一个工作状态标记 #967 [共创大赛][Bug] win下概率生成nul这个异常文件 #969 [共创大赛][Bug] #975 [共创大赛][Bug] 疑似 ACP 协议不兼容 #976 Windows下WebUI处理prompt时TUI切换目录触发同步快照回放及daemon日志泄漏"],["v4.25.8","v4.25.8 2026-07-03","Overview This release rounds out copying and exporting in the web UI, makes login state clear in /status, lets @ mentions step into directories, and improves bash detection on Windows. Changes Web UI copy and export : a copy button on messages copies the whole turn, tool calls included; sessions export to a Markdown file; image history displays properly, and a hard stop mid-turn no longer loses the whole turn. Login state in /status : the first line shows whether you are signed in and as whom (nickname and username), and an expired login clearly says to run /login; the Token line is gone. @ mentions into directories : @ completion steps into subdirectories and keeps the selected item in view; the / and @ menus share one highlight color. Windows bash detection : Git Bash is found on drives other than C:, WSL's app aliases are no longer mistaken for bash, and the model is told truthfully whether it is using Git Bash or cmd.exe. VS Code extension : @ file references, input history with the arrow keys, and an interface in Chinese and English. Fixes : auto-copy of code blocks is off by default and, when on, copies only when a reply has exactly one block; web_fetch decodes pages by their charset, so Chinese pages no longer garble and non-ASCII pages no longer crash it; paths from the model accept ~; MCP tool arguments show up to 450 characters; adding a plugin marketplace lists its plugins and the install command; tool names display correctly in resumed sessions; the input cursor shows while a reply streams; the web UI opens the browser reliably on Windows. Related issues #63 [Feature] 支持acp #447 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 支持acp和a2a以及 尝试支持claude code 的plugins市场 #811 [共创大赛][feat] 修改TUI 根据系统来制定不同的渲染方案，并设计降级策略，确保在不同的终端更好的交互。 #858 【Bug】VSCode 插件未处理 artifact 事件，可能导致代码块内容不展示 #868 [共创大赛]-[Feature] ACP 支持 #889 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 希望能够增加ACP支持 #893 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 优化微信插件消息 #902 [共创大赛][Bug] #903 [共创大赛][Bug] BYPASS模式，使用 /skill 调用技能，还是会出现审批 #905 [共创大赛][Bug] Windows版本，如果用户没有启动浏览器，输入/webui命令，不会自动打开默认浏览器 #907 4.25.7 版本无法执行命令，windows环境 #908 [共创大赛][Bug] Windows版：会话中断重启后记录丢失（应有2条仅剩1条） #909 [共创大赛]-[Feature] AtomCode for VS Code 增加 “输入历史记录导航（方向键 ↑/↓）” 功能 #910 [Bug] /resume 恢复会话后工具名称显示为原始 snake_case 而非 PascalCase #912 长代码块内容被截断/横向滚动失效 #915 [共创大赛][Bug] #916 在上一个问题回复过程中，输入框中光标不显示 #920 [共创大赛][Bug] ATOMCODE_PLAIN=1 模式下 OSC 11 终端探测响应泄漏为 ANSI 乱码 #921 [共创大赛][Bug] ATOMCODE_PLAIN=1 模式下自更新 eprintln 抢占启动输出 #928 [共创大赛]-[Feature] vscode插件通过@可引用文件夹/文件 #931 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 导出atomcode对话为markdown文件 #932 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 不要自动复制代码到剪切板 #933 bug：服务商返回空响应Provider returned an empty response #934 bug：阅读文件时报错中断任务(no reasoning detected) #935 [共创大赛][feat] webui 对话标题点击可以下来，修改对话标题，导出、删除功能 #937 [共创大赛][feat] webui用户发送的消息下面增加复制功能，还有大模型返回内容下面增加复制功能。 #940 [Feature] TUI 的 CodeReview 调用时未显示参数信息 #946 fix(acp): 内核死亡时 cmd_tx.send 错误被 .ok() 吞掉，客户端收到假 EndTurn #947 refactor: 两个 crate 重复定义 strip_reasoning_filler 函数，应共享实现 #948 执行命令为啥一定要强制通过wsl？ #949 VS Code插件/命令列表无法滚动查看且高亮状态残留 #952 [BadCase] ReadFile 对 ~ 开头路径未展开家目录，被当作相对路径处理 #965 /app 命令的说明缺少中文 i18n 翻译"],["v4.25.7","v4.25.7 2026-06-30","Overview This release focuses on rate limits and long tasks: a 429 now waits or pauses based on your plan's window, sudo passwords can be entered in the interface, /goal is steadier, and compaction notices are unified. Changes Waiting out rate limits : on a 429, AtomCode uses the real reset time to decide whether to wait and resume automatically or pause with a countdown; the TUI and web UI show the reset time instead of an error. sudo password prompt : when a command needs a sudo or ssh password, the TUI shows a hidden input box; Ctrl+C cancels it and it closes when the turn ends. Steadier /goal : it keeps going after recoverable interruptions, gains round and duration limits, stops after repeated rounds without progress, and no longer comes back after the goal has ended. Unified compaction notices : automatic and manual compaction share one progress indicator and divider; the footer always shows how much context is used. Double Esc to undo : with an empty input box, press Esc twice to undo the last turn; the first press tells you to press again. Vision models see images : with a vision model, images read by read_file are passed to the model. Long output no longer cut off : when a reply hits the output limit it continues automatically, and large files are written in parts. Fixes : answers a model puts in its reasoning are shown instead of a blank turn; Windows bash detection, quoting and Chinese Python output are fixed; pasted text expands correctly in history recall and after sending; the terminal is restored after the process is killed by a signal; todo updates show the task title; web_search shows source domains; tildes are no longer read as strikethrough; /login shows your real plan name. Related issues #540 [共创大赛][Bug] 拖拽程序窗口大小，会导致程序闪退 #736 [共创大赛][Bug] windows 上面 cmd和powershell 在对话中，用户不能线上滚动，一滚动又被强制回到了底部 #819 JetBrains插件需要增加插件主页，方便用户了解使用，支持中英文 #825 [WebUI][Bug] 同步模式下路径前的 ~ 指示符丢失 #827 [WebUI][Bug] sync 同步异常时 TUI prompt 未同步到 WebUI，且无法终止 #843 [共创大赛][Bug] 历史对话复制的内容无法使用 #845 [共创大赛][Bug] webui开启同步，切换session对话，TUI应该也要同步切换对话 #847 【Bug】JetBrains 插件 代码块（code block）无法正常显示 #848 JetBrains插件市场安装AtomCode下载失败且概览未加载 #850 [共创大赛][Bug] webui未开启同步的情况，新建对话TUI也会新建，应该不需要 #851 [共创大赛][feat] webui字体优化 #857 上下文使用进度条 / Context Usage Progress Bar #861 能不能把那个gitbash集成到atomcode里, 现在这种终端兼容性太差了, 空格都识别不了, 而且经常出现cmd/pwsh/PowerShell混用的问题 #872 [共创大赛] 上下文超200K后系统失效：5层防御缺口导致不可恢复 #884 [共创大赛]-[Feature] Ctrl+C 中断对话后保留已生成的上下文记忆 #885 [共创大赛][Bug] Codingplan Pro 中的 Qwen/Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct 无法正常使用 #891 TUI中/skills技能执行内容未在WebUI同步展示 #892 [共创大赛][Bug] todo工具并行调用，未展示任务名称"],["v4.25.6","v4.25.6 2026-06-25","Overview This release fixes a long list of Windows problems, improves automatic compaction and /cd, and adds a single network proxy setting; the web UI and JetBrains plugin also get many improvements. Changes Unified proxy setting : a new [network.proxy] section lets you follow the system proxy, pin a proxy, or use none, for every outbound connection; switch with /proxy in the TUI and check it with /status. Windows experience : the bash tool no longer flashes a console window each time; command output is decoded with the console's code page; CRLF line endings and GBK-encoded files no longer break reading and editing; /quit no longer hangs. More reliable auto-compaction : near the context limit it summarizes like /compact instead of only folding tool results; a very long paste no longer triggers empty summaries over and over; progress is shown while compacting. Better /cd : typing in the picker filters recent directories, and you can type a path directly; after changing directory, /resume lists that project's sessions. Forgiving edits : edits still match when tabs and spaces differ, so the model is no longer pushed into rewriting files with scripts. Web UI : a new welcome page, Skills and MCP menus, session search and date grouping; new sessions appear in the sidebar right away; the sync toggle survives a refresh; several instances no longer sign each other out. JetBrains plugin : a welcome page and onboarding, pasting or dragging in files, pasting images as attachments, and colors that follow the IDE theme. Fixes : MCP trust/autoApprove settings take effect and \"Always\" sticks for MCP tools; /setup writes MCP servers to the .mcp.json that is actually read; a connection reset mid-stream reconnects with a readable message; no more \"authentication expired\" after /login; resizing no longer duplicates output; a renamed session keeps its name; parallel_edit shows per-file progress. Related issues #173 [共创大赛][Bug] permission channel 关闭时静默返回 Deny，导致工具被误拒绝且缺少可观测性 #175 [共创大赛][Bug] OpenAI 流式 tool call： ToolCallStart 事件可能发送空 name，UI 显示空白工具名 #177 [共创大赛][Bug] 文件编辑跟踪依赖工具输出文本格式（“Edited …”），输出措辞变化/本地化会导致跟踪失效 #703 Windows下窗口全屏/缩放后会话历史重复，内容错乱表格未对齐 #709 [共创大赛][Bug] windows 11、10 PowerShell 放大缩小后，历史记录会多出2条 #713 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 非 JSON SSE 数据不应该显示空响应，应区分有数据但非法 和 没数据 #714 [共创大赛][Bug] 使用 atomcode -y 偶尔还是需要执行确认 #715 JetBrains插件输入栏按钮布局与快捷键说明UI优化建议 #716 JetBrains插件背景色需随编辑器主题联动，增加与编辑器的分隔线 #718 JetBrains插件未展示会话列表，不支持新建会话 #719 JetBrains插件没有打开的会话时设置按钮点击无效 #724 JetBrains插件建议支持文件拖拽、@选择文件和/命令 #725 [共创大赛][Bug] [错误：stream read error: error decoding response body: error reading a body from connection: unexpected EOF during chunk size line] #727 [共创大赛][Bug] mcp服务权限问题 #735 额度耗尽错误被误判为可重试:识别英文/结构化 quota 文案,避免 ~45s 无谓重试 #759 JetBrains插件建议支持粘贴截图 #760 JetBrains插件快捷键文本提示建议用placeholder展示在输入框内 #799 [共创大赛][feat] webui 改造 #813 [共创大赛][Bug] 频繁的读不到内容 #816 [共创大赛][Bug] webui 同步按钮开启和取消浏览器的sync参数要跟着变化，不然用户刷新一下又开启了 #818 # Bug: 多项目目录下先后执行 /webui ，前一个 Web UI 页面 token 失效 #820 [共创大赛][Bug] webui 发送对话，左侧sessions列表不刷新、或者标题不止那是问题 #824 [WebUI][Bug] 重命名会话后发送消息，会话名称被重置为默认名称 #826 [Bug] TUI 中切换目录未同步到 WebUI（/sync 会话） #828 [共创大赛][Bug] 微信clawbot 调用OpenClaw 调用 atomcode去干活，cmd窗口一直在闪 #829 [Bug] /setup 安装 MCP 到 .atomcode/mcp.json 但加载器不识别该路径 #859 Windows下TUI执行任务时无法向上翻页查看历史消息，固定在底部且翻动闪烁"],["v4.25.5","v4.25.5 2026-06-23","Overview A stability fix: a broken plugin hook no longer blocks every prompt, and empty model replies are retried automatically. Changes Broken hooks no longer block : a plugin hook that fails to launch or exits without giving a reason is no longer treated as a block, so prompts and tool calls go through. Empty replies retried : when the service occasionally returns a completely empty reply, AtomCode retries a few times with a notice instead of silently ending the turn. Fixes : the warning shown when running with administrator rights now advises running without elevation. Related issues #635 [共创大赛][Bug] Provider returned an empty response (no text, no tool calls). no reason 无回应"],["v4.25.4","v4.25.4 2026-06-23","Overview This release adds in-session code review with /review and persistent goals with /goal, ships a JetBrains IDE plugin, and improves context compaction. Changes /review code review : review your changes inside the session, with built-in rules per language, diff line numbers, and coverage driven by the changed files. /goal persistent goals : set a goal and the agent keeps working toward it across turns, checking progress each round. JetBrains IDE plugin : multi-tab chat, session state and a diff viewer, integrated with the IDE. Context and compaction : multi-level compaction on overflow (mechanical plus an LLM summary) and cache-friendly history compaction. Fixes : the context window now reloads after a model switch, /clear really starts a new session, and approvals and turns display better. Related issues #619 [共创大赛][Bug] ParallelEditFiles时仅能看到第一个文件名称 #633 [Bug] 插件市场 Skill 详情移动端页面留白太多，需优化 #686 /skills skill name 过滤应使用子串匹配而非前缀匹配 #694 [共创大赛][Bug] 使用GLM-5.2模型时，他无法使用复制的到CLI中的内容。 #697 [共创大赛]-[Feature] todo工具优化 [#698 [共创大赛][Bug] 最近一直Web UI一直提示[错误: [warning] conversation compacted]文字变成红色，但任务继续进行。](https://atomgit.com/atomgit_atomcode/atomcode/issues/698) #699 [共创大赛][Bug] #700 长文本粘贴被截断成多段，显示异常 #701 bash命令执行后转义序列未过滤，输入框出现乱码panic #702 [共创大赛][Bug] skill hub 安装命令直接运行会报错 #704 邀请页登录授权后重新进入需再次登录，登录态未持久化 #705 收款信息手机号输入未做校验，允许输入无效非数字字符 #706 强制杀进程后终端残留ANSI乱码 #707 WebUI停止按钮无法终止运行中的任务 #708 Markdown表格渲染时CJK字符导致表格边框|未对齐"],["v4.25.3","v4.25.3 2026-06-20","Overview A small update: write approvals are scoped by path again, and mouse handling in Windows terminals works normally. Changes Path-aware write approval : ordinary edits inside the workspace are approved automatically; \"Always\" is remembered per path for files outside it; sensitive files such as .env or SSH keys are asked about every time. Native mouse on Windows : AtomCode no longer changes the console mode, so wheel scrolling, drag-select, copy and right-click paste all work on conhost and Windows Terminal. Fixes : no more garbled input from mouse movement in the JetBrains terminal. Related issues #687 README 缺失 /wechat、/review、/goal 等斜杠命令的文档说明 #688 [共创大赛][Bug] 《总是》授权无法正确使用，目前《总是》授权后，还需要多次授权 #689 # AtomCode 聊天窗口鼠标失灵 Bug 报告 #690 鼠标移动后出现乱码 #691 [共创大赛][Bug] 更新后power shell 窗口不能上下滚动"],["v4.25.2","v4.25.2 2026-06-19","Overview This release moves to a new agent engine, makes cancelling, approvals and usage display more reliable, and fixes many web UI sync problems. Changes Cancel means undo : a turn cancelled with Esc no longer stays in the context, so the model won't bring it up later; a turn stuck while connecting can be cancelled at once. A focus for /compact : add a focus after /compact and the summary is written around it. Truer usage in the footer : each turn shows the tokens actually billed and the cache-hit share, instead of counting the re-sent context every round; token counts use K/M. Sensitive reads need approval : reading SSH keys, .env files, cloud credentials and similar files asks for approval first. Fixes : interactive approvals wait for your answer instead of timing out into a denial; new /exit; a \"slow response\" hint when the model is slow; private plugin marketplaces use your login and git no longer freezes the UI; stale connections recover on their own; the stream timeout rises to 300 seconds; web_fetch can return Markdown; skills in nested folders are found; table borders show on dark themes; the input box tops out at 6 rows; cancelled approvals no longer reappear after a /model switch; the web UI sidebar refreshes after starting a new chat. Related issues #213 [共创大赛][Bug] 读文件经常出BLOCKED，这究竟是什么意思？ #220 [共创大赛][Bug] 总是试图在未授权路径查询代码 #495 [共创大赛][Bug] websearch功能不能使用 #605 no reasoning removed) #606 bug：长文本复制粘贴不全 #610 [共创大赛][Bug] skills只能识别到相对于skills/目录下一级目录下的SKILL.md, 无法识别二级目录下的SKILL.md #614 [共创大赛][Bug] atomcode --help i18n 问题 #615 [共创大赛][Bug] cancel之后会覆盖输入框中已有内容 #629 [Bug] Skill 翻译描述只支持中文，翻译 README 抛 504 Gateway Time-out #637 [共创大赛][feat] skills hub 发布skill 需要支持 atomgit.com #640 [共创大赛][feat] skill hub 默认排序调整，根据star #641 TUI resume切换会话时界面闪动 #642 turn运行中时ESC和Ctrl+C无法取消或终止运行 #643 [共创大赛][Bug] WriteFile工具显示异常 #644 [共创大赛][Bug] v2引擎缺少工具并行调用时的显示 #645 [共创大赛][Bug] v2引擎不支持OpenFile工具 #646 [共创大赛][Bug] BYPASS模式下，WriteFile依旧弹出了审批 #647 [共创大赛][Bug] 审批确认信息中，SearchReplace工具和mcp调用工具的参数显示错误 #648 [共创大赛][Bug] OpenFile工具显示异常 #650 [共创大赛][feat] skill_hub 发布支持 test.gitcode.net #651 [共创大赛][Bug] skill hub 定时更新，仓库的 star、download数据 #652 [共创大赛][feat] skill hub 控制台skill管理，翻译频率限制，避免用户一直点翻译 #653 [共创大赛][Bug] skill hub发布skill没有 home page 数据 #654 [共创大赛][Bug] 每次对话结束后下方的token显示异常 #655 [共创大赛][Bug] v2引擎无法识别图片，缺少VL预处理 #656 [共创大赛][Bug] 使用/model切换模型后，不应该出现黄色warning信息 #657 [共创大赛][Bug] /compact功能不可用 #658 [共创大赛][Bug] v2 下重试机制/UI 渲染变了 #659 [共创大赛][Bug] 切换模型后，询问agent当前模型，回答的仍是上一个的模型 #660 WebUI打开后TUI执行过程未同步展示，仅展示结果 #661 插件市场简介和README翻译后，英文语言下仍展示中文内容 #663 [共创大赛][Bug] EditFile工具参数显示异常，而且diff也不显示了 #664 engine v2 provider提示在每次turn完成后重复显示，应仅在provider实际变化时打印 #665 bug: /setup 后 bridge respawn 失败导致 atomcode 直接退出 #666 [共创大赛][Bug] 终端添加市场源，填写git配置失败，导致终端卡死 #667 [v2 engine] 缺少 VL 图片预处理逻辑，图片被直接发送给纯文本模型导致 400 错误 #668 Skill Hub 同一仓库地址可创建多个重复 Skill，应做后台限制 #670 [共创大赛][feat] skill hub 新增运维工具，支持手动同步，skill的 star和download数 #671 [共创大赛][feat] skillhub homepage 数据替换脚本 #672 [共创大赛][feat] skill hub 控制台菜单切换支持刷新恢复 #673 [共创大赛][Bug] TraceChain工具缺少了参数的显示 #674 Token数量展示不友好，大数值建议以K/M单位显示 #675 [共创大赛][Bug] v2引擎会导致开源构建直接崩溃，TUI启动后几秒自动退出 #677 [共创大赛][Bug] webui 开始使用一个无法使用的模型对话，然后再切换到一个可以用的模型对话，结果无法切换还是使用的上一个模型始终报错 #679 /goal help 命令的 Notes 以及 help 文案需要中文 i18n 支持 #680 图文一起发送后，文本未立即显示，跑完后才出现 #681 [共创大赛][Bug] webui 输出内容回答中，点击新建对话，此时TUI中内容还在输出上一个对话的内容。 #682 goal执行过程中Esc/Ctrl+C/goal clear均无法中断 #683 取消prompt A后切换模型，旧的pending工具调用重新触发执行 #684 [共创大赛][Bug] webui 首次对话完成后，第二次对话，TUI就没有任何输出 #685 goal执行时在状态栏常驻显示goal状态，/goal status信息被刷走看不到"],["v4.25.1","v4.25.1 2026-06-12","Overview This release adds /view for files and a WeChat channel, switches web search to Exa by default, and improves performance and rendering in large directories. Changes /view files : /view <path> shows a code file right in the terminal UI. WeChat channel : talk to AtomCode through a personal WeChat ClawBot; see the AtomCode-Channel repository for the plugin. Exa web search by default : WebSearch uses Exa by default, with the web_access skill as a fallback. Performance and rendering : faster @ file indexing in very large directories, whole-line CJK rendering fixed in the DevEco terminal, and stronger SSRF protection in WebFetch. Fixes : and other fixes. Related issues #243 [共创大赛][Bug] 经常读写某个文件报告没有权限，但是又用BASH命令读到了 #542 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 请求给win11增加任务完成后的系统通知 #570 [共创大赛][Bug] 为什么在VS Code里一直压缩上下文？在终端里没发现这种情况 #571 [共创大赛][Bug] webui tools的调用没有根据宽度来展示，后面会有很大一个空白 #595 @符号 新创建的文件@不出来 #598 [共创大赛] web_fetch SSRF防护存在TOCTOU竞态窗口和IPv4映射绕过 #604 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 弹出来的让人工选择项A,Y,N 能否给个默认值？然后让按Enter可以继续 #608 deepseek-v4-flash 模型频繁出现 (no reasoning recorded) 占位符，导致对话卡顿/中断 #609 [共创大赛][Bug] 经常提示(no reasoning detected)后中断执行 #611 [Bug] 用户昵称展示长度未限制，登录与修改资料后展示不一致 #616 [共创大赛][Bug] PLAN模型，直接去写代码了 #617 [共创大赛][Bug] 使用 MCP cpu占用率100%，任务完成后也持续占用 #618 [共创大赛][Bug] Always提权无效 #621 [Bug] 发布 skill 到 marketplace 时 source.path 指向了 SKILL.md 文件而非目录 #622 [Windows] webui切换工作目录带 \\\\?\\ 前缀导致会话分组 hash 不同步，WebUI 与 TUI 之间无法同步会话记录 #624 [Bug] 安装 wechat channel 插件后 slash 命令 /wechat 未加载 #625 [共创大赛][Bug] 大小窗口问题，小窗口渲染丢失了内容，大窗口展示的内容完整 #626 [Bug] WebUI 提交 prompt 后无任何返回，但 TUI 有正常返回 #627 [Feature] [共创大赛] TUI样式优化 #630 [Bug] /api/admin/skills 查询过滤结果不准确，包含不相关条目 #631 [Optimization] 用户昵称展示长度过长，UI 显示不协调"],["v4.25.0","v4.25.0 2026-06-06","Overview This release adds ! to run commands directly and reasoning effort for DeepSeek V4, simplifies approvals, and improves WebFetch and the web UI. Changes Run commands with ! : type ! and a command, such as !git status, to run it directly; its output goes into the model's context. DeepSeek V4 reasoning effort : pick high or max with /effort. Simpler approvals : approval rules are simpler; see the approvals page in the docs. Faster WebFetch : no more max_chars limit, and fetched HTML is converted to Markdown. Web UI : switching the working directory, model and effort in the browser works better. Fixes : and other fixes. Related issues #152 [共创大赛][Bug] 以Administrator运行缺少安全提示 #222 [共创大赛][Bug] 往符号连接写好像有问题 #325 [共创大赛][Bug] window11下 powershell 终端中打开 atomcode 输入中文有乱码 #364 [共创大赛][Bug] AtomCode在WSL2 Ubuntu环境下不可用 #489 【Feature】MCP 工具调用审批弹窗需展示完整入参信息 #530 [共创大赛][Bug] 在执行bash等命令时，下面的输入框在不停地闪烁 #561 [Bug] Sync 模式下 TUI 和 WebUI 不在同一会话，三端历史互相独立、刷新后丢失 sync 对话 #572 [共创大赛][Bug] webui 信息流顺序和 TUI 不一致，不正确。 #573 [共创大赛][Bug] webui 模型选择下拉框，会溢出屏幕 #574 [共创大赛][Bug] 卸载插件后，终端会卡死无法输入 #575 [共创大赛][Bug] upgrade命令异常 #576 [共创大赛][Bug] /skills命令显示后，删掉下面会有文字残留 #581 [Feature] MCP 工具调用展示样式优化 + 审批提示样式优化 #583 [Bug] /webui --host 后终端输出的\"访问地址\"缺少 sync=1，且浏览器打开的 URL 丢失 token #585 [Enhancement] WebUI 工具调用展示格式对齐 TUI：点号分隔 + key:value 参数 #588 atomecode打开窗口在会话中不能调整大小，只要改变大小，界面布局就会乱"],["v4.24.2","v4.24.2 2026-06-03","Overview This release adds /undo to roll back the conversation, ties the web UI and TUI more closely together, and fixes several causes of periodic drops in the cache hit rate. Changes /undo the conversation : roll the conversation's memory back to an earlier prompt, so what came after leaves the context. Web UI and TUI in sync : model switches carry over both ways in real time; /webui opens the TUI's current session; approvals from the TUI work in sync mode, and a second tool in the same turn is no longer denied instantly. Fuller session restore : resuming a conversation brings back the dividers between turns along with each turn's token and tool counts. Steadier caching : the session's system prompt stays fixed, Plan mode notes and compaction summaries move out of it, and earlier file reads stay unchanged, so the prefix cache no longer collapses periodically. Image paths recognised : a local image path typed in, or pasted on Windows, is sent as an image attachment. Fixes : rate-limit retries wait for the cooldown the gateway suggests; web UI live output no longer leaks into other sessions, finished turns no longer leave approval cards behind, and the default port moves to 13457 to avoid clashing with VSCode; Windows system folders get sensitive-path protection, and Windows paths and multi-line content are no longer mis-escaped; files are found when you point at .atomcode, .claude and similar folders explicitly; CodingPlan no longer falsely reports model-list drift. Related issues #534 安装 skill/plugin 时未提示安装到用户全局位置还是项目目录位置 #563 [共创大赛][Bug] 恢复对话之后，模型最终输出和用户输入之间没有间隔，token统计和tool调用统计间隔丢失 #564 关于/undo的使用问题 #565 修复 referral install_completed 客户端上报可靠性问题 #568 [Bug] WebUI 请求 TUI 审批时，第二次审批自动 deny（response_rx 未按 call_id 区分）"],["v4.24.1","v4.24.1 2026-06-03","Overview This release introduces a new local web UI that shares the same live session with the terminal, adds the $ skills menu, and simplifies adding a provider. Changes A new local web UI : /webui starts a web server in-process and opens the browser, with streaming chat, tool runs, approvals, a session sidebar and directory switching; the terminal and the browser share one live session, and remote access is supported. $ skills menu : type $ at the start of a line to list and filter skills, Tab to complete, and $name with arguments to run one. Simpler /provider add : pasted curl, JSON or TOML is recognized, the Base URL comes first and the type is filled in. Bash : long tasks can run in the background (run_in_background), and destructive commands are flagged before they run. Fixes : and other fixes. Related issues #513 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 建议curl命令下载时不体现版本号 #523 【Feature】webui页面支持 #541 [共创大赛][Bug] 现在atomcode如何 设置不审批？回复没有 atomcode --dangerously-skip-permissions 或者 atomcode -y #544 [共创大赛][Bug] skills hub 缺少 atomcode provider #547 [共创大赛][Bug] [错误：auto-update: auto-update of marketplace atomcode-plugins-official failed: spawn git pull] #548 [共创大赛][Bug] 鸿蒙系统启动报错 错误: auto-install: auto-install of marketplace https://atomgit.com/atomgit_atomcode/atomcode-plugins-official.git failed: clone https://atomgit.com/atomgit_atomcode/atomcode-plugin #549 [Bug] webui 执行过程中输入框被禁用，用户无法键入 #551 [Enhancement] 编辑模型对话框增加 context_window 上下文大小配置 #552 [Bug] 编辑模型时，模型名称字段无法修改 #553 [Bug] 新建模型时名称重复直接覆盖原有配置，无提示 #555 [Bug] 移动端页面设置菜单部分被遮挡 #557 [Doc] 文档和 Ask 中增加虚拟组网（手机端访问 WebUI）相关指引 #558 [Bug] WebUI 上传文件只能选择当前目录层级下的文件 #559 [Bug] 虚拟组网后手机端 WebUI 会话消息需手动刷新才能同步（无实时推送） #562 [共创大赛][Bug] bash调用playwright会阻塞主会话，直到用户主动按ESC取消"],["v4.24.0","v4.24.0 2026-06-01","Overview This release centers on plugins, with an interactive /plugin manager and an official marketplace, and adds a -y flag to skip permission prompts and a much higher prompt cache hit rate. Changes Interactive plugin manager : type /plugin on its own to browse marketplaces and install or uninstall plugins in one step, with no name@marketplace to remember; plugins can also be installed and removed by name alone. Official marketplace : the official marketplace is now the default, marketplaces sync at startup and newly added plugins install automatically; plugins can come from a git subdirectory. Skip permission prompts : new --dangerously-skip-permissions (short form -y), shown as a red BYPASS badge in the footer. Higher cache hit rate : the system prompt stays identical across launches and compaction no longer fires needlessly, lifting the cache hit rate from about 79% to about 96%. AGENTS.md support : a project's AGENTS.md is read as project instructions; new /guide to ask how to use AtomCode; configurable hooks, including webhooks. Fixes : a failed turn shows \"interrupted\" instead of the success banner; the input box no longer flickers while streaming; pasting tab-indented text no longer misplaces the cursor; shell prompt characters are stripped from pastes; Windows no longer steers the model toward bash syntax; HarmonyOS self-update picks the right package; CodingPlan reports an exhausted monthly quota correctly; a failing UserPromptSubmit hook no longer blocks the conversation. Related issues #26 [Feature] 面向编程小白的入门引导建议 #109 [Feature] 希望支持hook机制 #208 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 支持 AGENTS.md 标准 #286 插件包安装的skill在建议 superpower:brainstrorming 冒号前后都支持自动筛选并tab补全，方便快速定位到对应的skill #326 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 从 Claude Code 已安装的插件中加载 skills/commands，避免重复安装 #440 [共创大赛][Bug] 已经取消的prompt，再下个prompt对话时仍然执行并返回了结果 #456 [共创大赛][Bug] 工具调用详细描述和resume提示线颜色与正文一样产生视觉混淆 #467 [共创大赛][Bug] skills name包含大写字母时抛错误提示 #468 [共创大赛][Bug] 已经安装的 plugin 提示存在问题，应该告诉用户已经安装了，如果需要重新安装使用什么命令先卸载，在重新执行什么命令安装 #471 [共创大赛][Bug] ParallelEditFiles 审批的时候，没有展示细节，不知道 ParallelEditFiles 需要干啥 #472 [共创大赛][Bug] ParallelEditFiles 是 AutoApprove，而 edit_file 是 RequireApprovalAlways #478 [共创大赛]-[Feature] vscode插件能否增加选中文字添加到对话中这个功能点？ #501 [共创大赛][Bug] 鸿蒙版本每次自动升级后，都无法运行 #504 [共创大赛][Bug] 在windows上模型生成多行命令的情况都会调用失败，经历几次尝试最终都会变成使用临时文件传递参数或调用命令 #507 [共创大赛][Bug] 当◐ Running Grep… · 320.4s 时 esc 无法取消 #509 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 请求添加类似cc的--dangerously-skip-permissions, gemini cli的 --yolo 启动参数来让cli全自动默认允许通过审批任何权限相关工具/命令 #520 怎么总是会操作一些不属于当前项目，也不属于他自己的目录？ #521 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 增加atomcode官方插件市场和优化plugin命令 #522 [共创大赛][bug] marketplace 始终没有更新，启动时自动 git pull 同步 marketplace #524 [共创大赛][Bug] /plugin 在 marketplace 安装成功，实际/skills 中没有 #525 [共创大赛][Bug] /plugin 已安装里面 -> 卸载插件 提示卸载成功了，但是 /skills 里面还能看到 #527 [共创大赛][Bug] /plugin 在 “浏览并安装” 里面选择插件回车安装，会卡住，此时没有任何交互，卡了很久安装成功了才有提示，优化一下交互，中间可能会去clone 仓库下来，会比较慢 #528 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 优化粘贴代码后光标的位置 #532 [共创大赛][Bug] 优化一个 /plugin install 安装问题， 目前按照 /plugin install control-ui-e2e@atomcode，后面还需要@对应 marketplace 这样很不方便，直接根据名字去安装即可。 #533 [共创大赛][Bug] /plugin uninstall control-ui-e2e 卸载一个不存在的 plugin 时，提示不够友好。 #535 [Enhancement] --dangerously-skip-permissions 提示文案优化：badge 红色+BYpass、banner 参考 CC 详细警告 #536 [共创大赛][feat] atomcode 官网新增 插件菜单和链接 #537 [共创大赛][feat] 文档更新 --dangerously-skip-permissions 和 -y 说明 #538 [Bug] atomcode 启动没有触发更新市场和插件"],["v4.23.3","v4.23.3 2026-05-28","Overview A fix update focused on display and Chinese output in Windows terminals, and on how much context thinking models use in long turns. Changes Windows terminal improvements : fixes duplicated Chinese characters and a flickering input box in PowerShell 7 and similar setups; Chinese text in bash output is no longer garbled. Long turns stay within context : compaction keeps recent content by token count, so models with heavy thinking output no longer overflow the context window. CodingPlan usage notice : when the monthly quota is used up, a single line says how many days to wait, and /status shows durations the same way as /login. Fixes : slash commands go into input history and come back with Up; web searches stop immediately on Ctrl+C; a stray {} at the end of a path is removed automatically; a 1M context window shows as 1m; Markdown table borders and widths are measured correctly; uninstall no longer triggers an automatic update first. Related issues #476 [共创大赛][Bug] autocode 使用微信扫描登录后运行/codingplan 失败 #493 atomcode uninstall卸载触发更新 #500 【Feature】支持npm和brew安装"],["v4.23.2","v4.23.2 2026-05-28","Overview This release mostly improves the terminal interface: history flows into the terminal's native scrollback and the mouse wheel, selection and copy go back to the terminal. It also fixes many Windows display problems, and destructive commands always need approval. Changes Native scrolling and copy : AtomCode no longer captures the mouse, so the wheel scrolls through history and selection and copy work the terminal's own way. Windows display fixes : duplicated or shifted characters in Chinese locales and laggy menu navigation are fixed, and wide characters and emoji are measured more accurately. Destructive actions always ask : dangerous commands such as rm -rf or a force push, and edits to sensitive files such as .env or keys, are never skipped because of a session-wide grant. Install with npm : AtomCode can now be installed through npm, including on HarmonyOS. Faster startup : plugin and skills marketplace setup runs in the background, so the input box is ready sooner and new skills appear without a restart. More models supported : tool calls that Qwen3 and similar models write as text are recognised instead of shown as plain text. Clearer CodingPlan usage : /codingplan status shows usage per time window and says plainly when the monthly quota is used up. Fixes : sessions resumed after compression still begin with the original request; reading large files uses less memory; cancelling or timing out ends bash's child processes too; \\t and similar sequences in Windows paths are no longer read as escapes; skills refresh after /setup, and /plugin gains reload; table rows with code or \\| split correctly; startup no longer crashes when both tokens have expired. Related issues #424 为什么不能上划,进行到哪一步,就只能看当前这一屏幕的内容,上面的就看不到了 #451 [共创大赛][Bug] 使用setup生成的skill，无法正常修改 #460 会话历史只能查看到终端高度的内容，无法滚动查看到之前的内容 #461 工具执行结果中 └ 树形连接符出现在折行文本行首，导致渲染异常 #462 [共创大赛][Bug] 使用 /setup 安装的skills，没有重新加载skills，导致安装的skills无法使用，也没有提示 #464 [共创大赛][Bug] /plugin 命令后面没有 reload 提示，和i18n处理 #466 [共创大赛][Bug] windows下 Waiting for approval 展示不正常，输入Y后上一个的 Waiting for approval 还存在 #474 【Feature】TUI改版 #480 【冒烟测试】Step 7 search_replace 步骤标题重复显示，审批后变为一个 #481 【冒烟测试】小窗口下 WriteFile 文字显示错位断裂 #485 【Bug】小窗口下执行 /help 指令，文案重叠 #486 Ctrl+O 详细模式展示存在重复行及 ANSI 序列泄漏问题 #488 【Bug】并行 bash 调用计数与显示数量不一致：「Running N calls in parallel」N 值与实际列出的调用数不匹配"],["v4.23.1","v4.23.1 2026-05-24","Overview A fix update: approval prompts are clearer and more reliable, reading outside the workspace needs confirmation, and an occasional long bash hang is fixed. Changes Better approval prompts : prompts show the replacement details and wrap in narrow windows so Y/A/N stay visible; the input box no longer disappears after you answer; while waiting the spinner says it is waiting for approval instead of counting up. Stricter permissions : actions that always need approval can no longer be passed by a session-wide grant; searching, diagnostics and symbol listing outside the workspace also ask first. Bash hang fixed : the workspace snapshot taken around each command now times out instead of holding a command up for minutes. Consistent ATOMCODE_HOME : when set, ATOMCODE_HOME is used as the config directory itself, without an extra .atomcode level. Fixes : Tab switches modes even with text in the input box; an expired token is refreshed and retried once, and silent refreshes no longer type into the input box; Enter on the QR step opens the link in a browser; headless mode no longer breaks thinking output onto a line per token; paths starting with ~ resolve correctly; automatic upgrades for Linux ARM64. Related issues #351 [共创大赛][Bug] 从Jebtbrain IDEA中进入以后 随机乱码 #400 [共创大赛][Bug]atomcode的会话内容和iterm中git log日志内容混在一起 #446 [共创大赛][Bug] 等待审核 命令超长没有换行，导致审核指令看不到了 #448 【Bug】查询终端背景色超时污染了输入缓冲区 #450 [共创大赛][Bug] 工具调用的权限决定阶段出现语义丢失问题，RequireApproval覆盖了RequireApprovalAlways #453 [共创大赛][Bug] 审批后输入框消失，resize 后恢复 #454 [共创大赛][Bug] 待审批一行就够，换行了 #455 [共创大赛][Bug] 待审批输入 Y 后，输入框没了 #457 【Bug】审批过后，之前等待审批的行占位还在 #458 【Bug】SearchReplace等待审批时，无法知道替换内容，审批过后才知道"],["v4.23.0","v4.23.0 2026-05-21","Overview This release rebuilds first launch around a WeChat QR sign-in that also claims CodingPlan on one page, and adds /setup project recommendations, light and dark themes, and syntax highlighting in code blocks. Changes QR quick start : first launch shows a QR code; scan it with WeChat and AtomCode detects completion, saves the sign-in, claims CodingPlan and opens the interface. /setup recommendations : analyses the current project and recommends skills, MCP servers, hooks and more, installed in one step; also available as atomcode setup on the command line. Light and dark themes : colours follow the terminal's background automatically, with higher contrast on light backgrounds; code blocks are syntax-highlighted by language. Default skills marketplace : the official skills marketplace is installed on first launch, and installed marketplaces update after an upgrade. Open files for preview : a new open_file tool opens generated pages, PDFs and images in the system's default app, and says so plainly over SSH or without a display. /keys shortcut reference : lists every keyboard shortcut and notes which newline combinations your terminal may not pass through; in multi-line input Up and Down move between lines before browsing history. Safer git commands : force pushes, history rewrites, interactive rebases, forced checkouts or branch deletions, and skipping hooks now need approval. Fixes : approval prompts tell apart parallel calls on files with the same name; tools already allowed for the session no longer prompt again; upstream errors read more clearly (429 shortened to one line); the total request timeout rises to 30 minutes; finish notifications in Ghostty; the VS Code extension gains sessions in multiple tabs, bulk session deletion and a workspace file picker. Related issues #405 [共创大赛]-[Feature] 是否可以添加色彩支持，提升视觉交互体验 #423 【Feature】错误上报细分 #425 [共创大赛][Bug] 快速安装中的命令未按平台分别提供复制命令按钮 #426 [共创大赛]-[Feature] vs code插件中的会话列表，建议支持多选删除 #429 [共创大赛][Bug] ATOMCODE_HOME 设置后 Skills 运行异常 现象 #432 [共创大赛][Bug] API error (429 Too Many Requests) #437 [共创大赛][Bug] 优化Tools并行调用展示问题 #439 [共创大赛][Bug] tools并行调用，用户审批不知道是审批哪一项 #441 [共创大赛][Bug] 修复 /setup 安装后，没有刷新 skills #443 [共创大赛][Bug] /setup 支持国际化i18n #444 [共创大赛][feat] /setup 交互优化不再需要 /recommend 来触发 #445 [共创大赛][bug] 修复/setup 设置 ATOMCODE_HOME 无法运行问题"],["v4.22.3","v4.22.3 2026-05-18","Overview This release adds background session commands, launches the redesigned website, and fixes a few problems that got in the way. Changes Background sessions : the new /bg commands run a session in the background, list background sessions, and bring one back. Redesigned website : atomcode.atomgit.com has a new look. Fixes : the /codingplan 401 error; Ctrl+C failing to copy a selection on Windows; WebFetch parsing errors; cd switching directories by itself. Related issues #267 用户能成功要求atomcode删除系统skill目录下的文件，没做权限控制？ #376 [共创大赛][Bug] Linux下登录链接 #394 [共创大赛][Bug] 在全局路径:~/.atomcode/skills/下的SKILL在TUI下无法发现 #396 [共创大赛][Bug] 通过/plugin安装karpathy-skills无法使用 #403 [共创大赛][feat] 优化 /login 二维码太大，连接太长问题 #414 [共创大赛][Bug] /bg 命令，中途需要确认的会话，切后台后，重新恢复，没展示之前的prompt和输出内容 #415 [共创大赛][Bug] /bg bash命令申请情况，/bg 回来，内容为空 #417 [共创大赛]-[Feature] bg命令的说明内容需要支持中文语言下的中文内容 #421 【Feature】site站点风格和样式更新"]],"x":"Changelog Browse AtomCode features, fixes and related issues by release. View releases and downloads ↗ Browse by version v5.2.9 v5.2.8 v5.2.7 v5.2.6 v5.2.5 v5.2.4 v5.2.3 v5.2.2 v5.1.0 v5.0.9 v5.0.8 v5.0.7 v5.0.6 v5.0.5 v5.0.4 v5.0.3 v5.0.2 v5.0.1 v5.0.0 v4.26.0 v4.25.9 v4.25.8 v4.25.7 v4.25.6 v4.25.5 v4.25.4 v4.25.3 v4.25.2 v4.25.1 v4.25.0 v4.24.2 v4.24.1 v4.24.0 v4.23.3 v4.23.2 v4.23.1 v4.23.0 v4.22.3"},{"s":"headless-daemon","t":"Headless & Daemon","y":"Hd","h":[],"x":"Headless & Daemon In addition to the interactive TUI, AtomCode offers two non-interactive modes: -p headless on the CLI for scripts and CI, and atomcode-daemon — an HTTP + SSE API service that any client can drive. Headless CLI mode Add -p / --prompt to atomcode to execute a single task and write the reply straight to stdout (like Claude Code's -p mode): atomcode -p \"give me a brief overview of this repo\" By default only the AI's final reply text goes to stdout — handy for piping. Tool calls and token usage are kept out of stdout. Common headless flags Flag Description -p, --prompt TEXT Task description to run --prompt-file PATH Read the prompt from a file (good for long input; mutually exclusive with -p ) -v, --verbose Send tool-call logs, token usage, and turn summaries to stderr ; stdout is untouched --no-tools Headless only. Exposes no built-in, MCP, skill, or child-agent tools to the model. --ephemeral Run without creating, resuming, or writing a persistent session. --output-format text|jsonl Write assistant text by default, or versioned JSON Lines events with jsonl . --require-approval-hook Require an enabled, catch-all required approval hook for tools. -C, --dir PATH Working directory; defaults to the current directory --provider / --model Temporarily override provider or model --no-telemetry Disable telemetry for this invocation Examples # Generate a project summary and write it to a README draft atomcode -p \"summarise the project structure and produce a README draft\" > README.draft.md # Explain existing lint output in CI without exposing tools atomcode --prompt-file lint-report.txt --no-tools --ephemeral # Read the prompt from a file atomcode --prompt-file task.md -v 2> run.log # Local Ollama, completely offline atomcode -p \"explain this code\" --provider local --model qwen2.5:14b Exit codes 0 — normal completion Non-zero — an error occurred. The error message goes to stderr; details are in the -v log Note: permission model A normal -p run has no interactive prompts. Approval requests for bash and bash_start are approved automatically, with the tool name written to stderr: [headless] auto-approved bash Other requests that reach interactive approval are denied by default, for example: [denied] edit_file requires interactive approval An approval denial causes a nonzero exit. Use --no-tools to remove the entire model tool catalog in CI. Unattended scheduled runs deny every tool call that reaches interactive approval. atomcode-daemon atomcode-daemon is a standalone transport adapter over CodingRuntime . It exposes an HTTP + Server-Sent Events API for web frontends, IDE plugins, and editor extensions. The official AtomCode VS Code extension and the AtomCode Air desktop app both connect through it. Launching # Launch the daemon in the CLI process, bound to 127.0.0.1 atomcode daemon # Pick a port and client identity (drives telemetry segmentation) atomcode daemon --port 13456 --client vscode # You can also invoke the daemon binary directly (more options) atomcode-daemon --host 127.0.0.1 --port 13456 \\ --client atomcode-air --idle-timeout 1800 The daemon reads the same ~/.atomcode/config.toml as the CLI — login state, provider config, and session history are all shared. Launch flags Flag Description --host HOST Standalone atomcode-daemon only. Sets the listen address and defaults to 127.0.0.1 . --port PORT Listen port; default 13456 --client NAME Tags client telemetry. Both entrypoints recognise vscode , jetbrains , and atomcode-air . --idle-timeout SECS Idle timeout. Defaults to 1800 seconds, and 0 disables it. Also configurable via ATOMCODE_DAEMON_IDLE_TIMEOUT . The standalone binary clamps nonzero values to at least 60 seconds. --no-auth Disable API token authentication for isolated local development. --no-telemetry Disable telemetry for this process Security Both daemon entrypoints require API token authentication by default. GET /health is available without a token. For protected endpoints, read the token from $ATOMCODE_HOME/daemon-<port>.json (under ~/.atomcode/ by default) and send Authorization: Bearer <token> . The standalone binary refuses non-loopback binds with authentication disabled by default. Keep authentication enabled and use TLS for remote access. Endpoint overview Common endpoints are listed below. Routes are registered or merged in crates/atomcode-daemon/src/lib.rs . Health & lifecycle Method + Path Description GET /health Health check POST /shutdown Shut the daemon down gracefully (used when the client exits) Sessions / projects Method + Path Description GET /sessions List all sessions POST /sessions Create a new session GET /sessions/search Search history by keyword GET /project Project state for the current working directory POST /cd Switch working directory GET /projects List every project that has had sessions GET /projects/:hash/sessions Sessions under a specific project GET /projects/:hash/sessions/:id Session details DELETE /projects/:hash/sessions/:id Delete a session PATCH /projects/:hash/sessions/:id/rename Rename a session Chat & models Method + Path Description GET /models List available providers / models POST /chat Send a prompt; returns an SSE stream POST /chat/stop Stop an in-progress /chat Config / providers Method + Path Description GET /config Read the current config.toml POST /config/reload Reload config.toml GET /providers List all providers POST /providers Add a provider PATCH /providers/:name Update a provider DELETE /providers/:name Delete a provider POST /providers/:name/default Set this provider as the default PATCH /providers/:name/thinking Toggle / adjust the provider's thinking mode MCP Method + Path Description GET /mcp/status MCP server connection status POST /mcp/reload Reload .mcp.json Auth / CodingPlan Method + Path Description GET /auth/status Current login status POST /auth/login/start Kick off AtomGit OAuth login POST /auth/login/:login_id/poll Poll for the login result DELETE /auth/login/:login_id Cancel an in-flight login POST /auth/logout Log out POST /codingplan/setup Claim CodingPlan and write the provider config (equivalent to the CLI atomcode login ; atomcode codingplan is kept as a hidden alias) SSE streaming chat The SSE stream returned by POST /chat includes events for AI text deltas, reasoning deltas, tool-call batches (start / end), token stats, errors, and more. The daemon wire schema is defined by LiveWireEvent in crates/atomcode-daemon/src/live_api.rs . Frontends can consume the stream with the native EventSource or any SSE client library. CORS The daemon configures CORS to allow only loopback origins : the host must be localhost , 127.0.0.1 , or ::1 (any port, any protocol). Other origins are rejected. This is defence in depth alongside the default --host 127.0.0.1 bind — even if someone tries DNS rebinding to forge a request, the CORS layer still blocks it. Typical uses Editor plugins / IDE extensions (VS Code, JetBrains) Desktop GUIs (e.g. the official AtomCode Air) Self-hosted local web UIs (move the terminal agent into the browser) Local script orchestration: dispatch multiple tasks over HTTP, share session history Next steps Skills — codify workflows into commands; particularly useful with headless FAQ — common headless / daemon pitfalls"}];
